{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation","id":152033,"title":"The Spirit Nation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-28T20:10:08-07:00","id":152033,"title":"The Spirit Nation","content":"Seeing the comments that a pure Native American pantheon would be good to represent America, I thought that it would be also a good idea. And then I remember the huge list of mythical creatures that start with A on that one website. After groaning, I thought about the stories that are based on Native American mythology. What I did remember was that the ones I recognized were about the Animal spirits. So I decided that having the stereotypical Great Spirit accompanied by the animal spirits of common lore. The reason I decided on calling the pantheon &quot;The Spirit Nation&quot; was that, given what I knew, the spirits of the country would aid and guide the tribes of America (or as they called it: Turtle Island). If there's something more accurate, please tell me, because I'm going off with what I know.<br /> <br /> The Gods: As I said before, I was thinking of the so-called Great Spirit being the all-father of this pantheon, with the animal spirits commonly told about in the lore as the other gods of the pantheon. As a picture, I could see them as basic Native American people with a part of their dress bearing a symbol of the animal spirit that they are representing<br /> <br /> Besides the Great Spirit, the Animal spirits that I know of commonly are thus:<br /> <br /> Coyote: This is a no-brainer because the deity was not only part of some trickster stories, but was also written up in the Scion:God fiction where he stole the Sacred Necklace from Yukiko during her search for the knob of Sun Wukong's staff. He was considered an alternative identity of Brer Rabbit, but I think in this case that Coyote being his own character would be good for this pantheon. Also of note, read Coyote Blues by Christopher Moore. In it, he places some tales of Coyote and emphasizes his nasty gambling habit, not to mention that the main story would be a good example of a Scion of Coyote. Also, if it's feasible, we can also have Rabbit in there as well, since he's mentioned in one of Coyote's stories (Apparently the animal spirits can change gender by removing the penis).<br /> <br /> Eagle and Raven: I heard about this story and it fits well into the global pantheon story of a solar blackout due to the sun missing. In this case, it was said that Eagle coveted the sun so he took it to his place and the world was cast into darkness. Raven, hearing about this, thought of stealing the sun for himself. Raven succeeded, but not without alerting Eagle into chase. During the chase, Raven dropped the Sun back into the sky and Day was restored. Something to think of.<br /> <br /> Other animals of note are Bear (thanks to the Brother Bear movies) and Wolf because he seems common enough.<br /> <br /> That brings to a total of seven gods total. Are there some Animal spirits that should be included to maximize the pantheon? Should the alligator be included to represent the swamp tribes like the Seminole and Okeechobee tribes?<br /> <br /> History: Since that it's fact now that Native Americans dealt with the Vikings beforehand and kicked them out. I was thinking that in the early days, after their Titan was sealed, the Spirit Nation had to deal with invasions from the Aesir in the East, The Chinese Bureaucracy in the West (I'm saying this because of the somehow dubious map that predated Columbus), and their bloodthirsty brothers, the Aztantl to the South, They were doing well until the titanspawn unleashed a plague that weakened the tribes, and the pantheon in kind. Because of this, they couldn't handle the resurgence of the Aesir and Aztlantl and the arrival of other pantheons as well, which ended in tenuous relations with the pantheons. When the Titans escaped, they teamed up to handle the return of their own Titan who renewed efforts to oppress their people.<br /> <br /> Relations with other Pantheons: Given the Native American relations with the Norse, I would think that the Spirit Nation would hate the pantheon for past transgressions. With the other pantheons, there would be an air of caution about them as akin to invading armies. The two pantheons that the Spirit Nation would deal with on a daily basis would be the Loa (some in the Nation would think that it was an attempt by the Orisha of Africa to claim a piece of their land as their own) and the Polynesian Pantheon (the pantheon which contains the Hawaiian Islands and the Phillipean Islands) since part of their area of influence (Hawaii) became part of their land.<br /> <br /> Pantheon Purview - I actually don't have an idea of how to make this. I don't know much about Native American terminology to get a name, much less to form the purview. Any help will be nice.<br /> <br /> Titan: Even though, the monsters in the Native American lexicon would make good antagonists or titanspawn, I don't know what to name the Titan and I'm confused as to what he/she is a Titan of. Again, any help would be nice.<br /> <br /> So this is the bare bones that I came up with about The Spirit Nation. Any help to flesh it out further and to clarify things would be great. If anything, I'm hoping that the suggestions will help Onyx Path to create this as a replacement to the Yankee Pantheon for 2E.<br /> <br /> So thanks for the help. Any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:35:48-07:00","id":152055,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Wolf</b></u> taught cooperative hunting. (Ancient people were able to observe how they hunted in packs).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bison</b></u> was held in awe as the Great Sprit's gift of life to the Plains Peoples. (When a bison is killed, almost every part of it is found a use)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 05-28-2014, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:45:12-07:00","id":152064,"title":"","content":"Trying to create a &quot;Native American&quot; Pantheon is about as feasible as trying to create an &quot;African Pantheon&quot; or a &quot;European Pantheon&quot;. It completely ignores that 'native American' is a blanket term that covers an area <i>much larger</i> than all of Europe, yet no one floats the possibility of combining the Celtic, Germanic, Greco-Roman, Baltic and Slavic cultures together into a single generic Pantheon with figures like &quot;Sky King&quot;, &quot;Thunder&quot;, &quot;Love Woman&quot; and &quot;Sea Lord&quot;. I mean, Perun and Thor, they're the same. Manannan mac Lir, Njord and Neptune are practically identical!<br /> <br /> It's much more practical, and logical, to use a single native American culture like the Cherokee, Iroquois, Lakota, Inuit or Navajo. You know, how every other Pantheon in Scion works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:42:37-07:00","id":152099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation#post152033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing the comments that a pure Native American pantheon would be good to represent America, I thought that it would be also a good idea. And then I remember the huge list of mythical creatures that start with A on that one website. After groaning, I thought about the stories that are based on Native American mythology. What I did remember was that the ones I recognized were about the Animal spirits. So I decided that having the stereotypical Great Spirit accompanied by the animal spirits of common lore. The reason I decided on calling the pantheon &quot;The Spirit Nation&quot; was that, given what I knew, the spirits of the country would aid and guide the tribes of America (or as they called it: Turtle Island). If there's something more accurate, please tell me, because I'm going off with what I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your idea is one rooted in nothing but good intentions, I am sure, to address a large problem in Scion, it carries with it some rather large issues. Ranging from small, to incredibly offensive, though I do not believe you have any intent to do anything but try to solve this problem of representation<br /> <br /> The primary issue here is that you are attempting to combine an entire continents worth of peoples, with their own unique histories, mythologies, and ways of life, into a single group. That is incredibly offensive to these groups. This idea forces connections that do not exist, implies that all of the Natives of North America are effectively the same culturally, or if not that, religiously, and that is just not true in any way, shape, or form.<br /> <br /> To try to put it in a way you may better understand, this would be the same as saying the Tuatha de Dannan, and the Anunna of Mesopotamia are the same. Something which we know is entirely not true.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you are playing into stereotypes of Native religion. Some, yes, are Animist, but some were not. Some had animal worship, but some too had Hero worship, or had entire Pantheons of very human figures. The entire root of this idea is one based on the Native American tribes being all the same, but that is a falsehood so colossal and great, I can't even begin to touch on how horribly wrong it is.<br /> <br /> You have Hunter Gather societies, Agrarian societies, Herders, Raiders, Urban, Nomadic, all of them different and unique from one and other. They may have once, in some long ancient past all come from an original root society that we have failed thus far to identify in any way shape or form, but even if they did and this progect attempted to play off this idea of the collective past of all of these hundreds, and hundreds of cultures, I would have to tell you that by the same logic, the Deva, the Yazata, the Tuatha, the Aesir, the Theoi, the Elohim, the Nemetondevos, and more are, by that logic, the same Pantheon for they descended from the same root culture.<br /> <br /> While, Jackalope, I believe that you had no intentions of this being anything but productive in attempting to solve this issue of a lack of representation, you have fallen into the same trap that the game's French developers, and many other members of the community have fallen into. This is the easy solution, but one that is fundamentally a bad one. It is an idea that has good merits for the desire to represent an entire continent of unrepresented peoples, but carries with it horrible implications of uniformity across numerous unique and wonderfully different cultures.<br /> <br /> If you wish to represent one of the Native American tribes through Scion, that would be wonderful. Maybe the Cree, Navajo, Iroquois, or any one of the other cultures. But, pushing an entire continents worth of peoples, making grand sweeping statements about their cultures, destroying any individuality, or uniqueness, that is not a good way to go about this.<br /> <br /> Now, of course, I can't magically stop you, or any others from working on this project, but, this is just my advice. If you would like to work on one of the individual Pantheons of one of these individual cultures, I am sure there would be many, many people on the forums who would be happy to brainstorm with you, and help you. But, this is one of those roads to hell, paved with good intentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 05-29-2014, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T09:45:08-07:00","id":152608,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me that the reason this type of project keeps cropping up might be because of how the Celestial Bureaucracy consumed each and every indigenous god from that region into one whole. No one even tries to separate them into their original parts either. Hell, there's probably no documentation on it by this point, just like the mostly oral tradition Native (NORTH)American tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T10:02:47-07:00","id":152618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=152608#post152608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that the reason this type of project keeps cropping up might be because of how the Celestial Bureaucracy consumed each and every indigenous god from that region into one whole. No one even tries to separate them into their original parts either. Hell, there's probably no documentation on it by this point, just like the mostly oral tradition Native (NORTH)American tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, that may be it. People seeing precedent in the Shen. I don't particularly like the way the Shen were handled, but it is incredibly difficult to get access to the research one would need due to the Chinese Government not releasing it. But, thankfully, that is not the issue with Native North American groups for two reasons.<br /> <br /> First, there has already been a nice amount of research done, meaning that the myths have been recorded and examined academically to a degree that is, for example, far greater than the records we have of the Nemetondevos. And second, there are actually people still alive who have grown up with these myths and legends, they are not lost to us.<br /> <br /> It is a really common idea that the Native North American tribes have little documentation, not really sure why, but we have way more than we have for the Gauls, and we can legitimately look people up and send them an email asking about the myths and legends. They are by far not dead yet. Though, unfortunately we are getting close to the death of that knowledge, which would very obviously be a bad thing.<br /> <br /> So, it may take more effort than, say, writing a Welsh Pantheon, but it is still very possible. I do think you are right, Darksol, that the Shen may be planting this idea in people's heads. That would explain why it comes up so often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T10:03:05-07:00","id":152619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=152608#post152608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that the reason this type of project keeps cropping up might be because of how the Celestial Bureaucracy consumed each and every indigenous god from that region into one whole. No one even tries to separate them into their original parts either. Hell, there's probably no documentation on it by this point, just like the mostly oral tradition Native (NORTH)American tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a slight difference between the two though...that being that the Chinese Gods are mythologically part of the same Pantheon. For eg, Guan Yin is, in all probability, an import of the Hindu Avalokiteshwara mixed in with the Tibeto-Indian Tara. But she's worshipped by the Chinese people as a Chinese God, and has myths where she interacts with chinese figures like Sun Wukong, the Dragon Kings and the Jade Emperor.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, no Haida ever went to the Eskimo and said 'Hey, Sedna's really cool, I'll borrow her for my religion', and no Hopi ever went, 'Hey guys, White Buffalo Woman is totally something we're worshipping now.' The peoples of Native America are unique cultures and their Gods have unique mythologies that simply do not interact the way Chinese mythology does, and they should be treated as such.<br /> <br /> And before somebody asks, no Coyote is not a thing...there are a dozen different Coyote Gods across the continent each his own unique deity, as much as Zeus and Indra are unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T10:24:23-07:00","id":152665,"title":"","content":"Some things survived to grow beyond Native consciousness.<br /> Or so it seems to me:<br /> <br /> Kokopelli (fertility, luck); Coyote (great trickster); Thunderbird (eagles, sky/storm spirit); Wakanda (Supreme spirit, Sun father); Wolf Moon (female, huntress, Moon, Night); White Buffalo (medicine/healing magic); Brother Bear (Forest Guardian, Warrior/Strength (<i>&quot;Only you can prevent forest f...OW! ok! ok..</i>); Raven; (Creation, Trickster) Mountain Lion (grace, power, Death); The Three Sisters (Corn, beans and squash which could lead to other planted foodstuff, Health); Grandmother Spider (chthonic deity, Deep earth, Darkness, Creator, Fate); etc...I'm kinda making this stuff up as I go along, but I'm connecting the dots as I see it today.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T10:56:33-07:00","id":152691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=152665#post152665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things survived to grow beyond Native consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what this means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T11:33:33-07:00","id":152731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=152665#post152665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things survived to grow beyond Native consciousness.<br /> Or so it seems to me:<br /> <br /> Kokopelli (fertility, luck); Coyote (great trickster); Thunderbird (eagles, sky/storm spirit); Wakanda (Supreme spirit, Sun father); Wolf Moon (female, huntress, Moon, Night); White Buffalo (medicine/healing magic); Brother Bear (Forest Guardian, Warrior/Strength (<i>&quot;Only you can prevent forest f...OW! ok! ok..</i>); Raven; (Creation, Trickster) Mountain Lion (grace, power, Death); The Three Sisters (Corn, beans and squash which could lead to other planted foodstuff, Health); Grandmother Spider (chthonic deity, Deep earth, Darkness, Creator, Fate); etc...I'm kinda making this stuff up as I go along, but I'm connecting the dots as I see it today.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean that those are common themes Shadowflame? Because, this runs into the issue that if you group all of them together for possibly having a root in this 'Native conscioness', why not group all of the Indo-European Pantheons together and make them one single mass? Break Zeus, Ba'al, and Indra down into the same figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:42:30-07:00","id":152809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=152608#post152608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that the reason this type of project keeps cropping up might be because of how the Celestial Bureaucracy consumed each and every indigenous god from that region into one whole. No one even tries to separate them into their original parts either. Hell, there's probably no documentation on it by this point, just like the mostly oral tradition Native (NORTH)American tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, Chinese minorities still have their own religions, though there is some degree of syncretization in most of them. For example, the Qiang still practice Ruism, which has important figures with no clear counterpart in Shenism.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about separating the pantheons of the people who became the Han, then I'm not sure where you could even start. Separating Shangdi and Tian is about as simple as separating Zeus and Jupiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","user":"Creticus","date":". 05-29-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T16:57:26-07:00","id":153245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean that those are common themes Shadowflame? Because, this runs into the issue that if you group all of them together for possibly having a root in this 'Native conscioness', why not group all of the Indo-European Pantheons together and make them one single mass? Break Zeus, Ba'al, and Indra down into the same figure?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm saying that certain spirits have entered a somewhat more mainstream consciousness. &quot;Coyote&quot; is almost ubiquitous in current day North America. Red man, White man, Black man, we all know of this trickster figure. However, refer to him as &quot;Sk'elep&quot; (Secwepemc) and no one will know who that is and thus becomes a minor figure compared to &quot;Coyote.&quot; We know of Thunderbird, but we don't recognize the Ojibwa &quot;animikii.&quot; I think that for the purpose of the thread, we can take what became &quot;mainstream&quot; and fill things out a bit. (I do believe that spirits are more tied to geographically cultural areas, but see little harm for a thread)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:00:23-07:00","id":153247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=153245#post153245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm saying that certain spirits have entered a somewhat more mainstream consciousness. &quot;Coyote&quot; is almost ubiquitous in current day North America. Red man, White man, Black man, we all know of this trickster figure. However, refer to him as &quot;Sk'elep&quot; (Secwepemc) and no one will know who that is and thus becomes a minor figure compared to &quot;Coyote.&quot; We know of Thunderbird, but we don't recognize the Ojibwa &quot;animikii.&quot; I think that for the purpose of the thread, we can take what became &quot;mainstream&quot; and fill things out a bit. (I do believe that spirits are more tied to geographically cultural areas, but see little harm for a thread)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is entirely possible to do this, and if yourself and others wish to do so, then more power to you. But, I think the best way to handle the Pantheons of North America is to not make large generalizations of them and to properly show them as they were pre-contact, just as we show the Tuatha de Danann before Christianity, and treat other Pantheons in the same way. <br /> <br /> But, once again, if you wish to do this, no one can stop you. Have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:02:14-07:00","id":153332,"title":"","content":"I don't understand how pop-culture ignorance is a reason to consolidate an entire continent together into a single culture. How much pop-culture presence do Indra and Perun have? Not a lot. Is that a good reason to merge them together with Thor into a single &quot;Thunder God&quot; character for an Indo-European Pantheon? Scion is full of figures that don't have much pop-culture traction.<br /> <br /> Also the idea that all the North American native cultures had a single overriding idea suitable to a PSP is just as hilarious as the idea that all of Asia has a single communal idea that could work for an &quot;Asian&quot; Pantheon. Continents aren't cultures. Australia possibly being an exception, though I don't know very much at all about Australian aboriginal cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T23:18:17-07:00","id":153569,"title":"","content":"I understand how the generalization can make some people feel left out. I thought of the pantheon being that way because, just like other posters said, some legends got absorbed into pop culture. I chose the story of Eagle and Raven because it fits with the global mythologies where the sun apparently went out (Amaterasu hiding in the cave for the Amatsukami and Apollo taking a nap in the Dodekathon). Coyote is such a key player that he's mentioned in the first edition of Scion, both as fiction and in the write-up for Brer Rabbit.<br /> <br /> Personally, if we need to focus the pantheon on a single tribe (redundant given the multiple names that the gods of the pantheons have), I would go with the Navajo, given that their language is still being used and it would give us a basis for the Pantheon purview and other relics.<br /> <br /> Still, thanks for the help and I hope that Onyx Path will notice this thread for a possible pantheon in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T23:23:26-07:00","id":153571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=153245#post153245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm saying that certain spirits have entered a somewhat more mainstream consciousness. &quot;Coyote&quot; is almost ubiquitous in current day North America. Red man, White man, Black man, we all know of this trickster figure. However, refer to him as &quot;Sk'elep&quot; (Secwepemc) and no one will know who that is and thus becomes a minor figure compared to &quot;Coyote.&quot; We know of Thunderbird, but we don't recognize the Ojibwa &quot;animikii.&quot; I think that for the purpose of the thread, we can take what became &quot;mainstream&quot; and fill things out a bit. (I do believe that spirits are more tied to geographically cultural areas, but see little harm for a thread)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is much more accurate to say the opposite. Mainstream consciousness has conflated multiple native spirits who used to have greater individuality into a messy amalgam that does not properly represent any of the individual native spirits in question. Of course, we can certainly take the mainstream consciousness and make a fictional pantheon out of them as an exercise in fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T06:26:22-07:00","id":153780,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=153332#post153332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand how pop-culture ignorance is a reason to consolidate an entire continent together into a single culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that's what's being presented here.<br /> It's more or less taking what's more commonly known and presenting it for fun. No culture created here that I can see.<br /> But if you do however see that, then perhaps my definition of &quot;culture&quot; is different from yours.<br /> <br /> I recall Palladium books doing something similar. And it was a fun time reading it. But I never once thought it was a different culture, or an attempt at such a thing.<br /> <br /> I do see this as similar to what White Wolf did with Werewolf the Apocalypse, and the totem system (and related hierarchies) created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:06:08-07:00","id":153913,"title":"","content":"It's very, very common to lump all native North American cultures together and say they're the same thing. That the Cherokee are just a tribe of &quot;Native Americans&quot;, along with the Lakota and the Navajo and the Zuni. Sure, they're from hundreds or thousands of miles away from each other, living in entirely different ecologies and societies, but they're all basically the same! They all have Ravens and Coyotes and Thunderbirds! That attitude purvades modern pop-culture and, unfortunately, a lot of scholarly research on North American cultures as well. It's a remnant of colonialism when lumping &quot;primitive cultures&quot; together into archetypes was super popular because actually trying to understand them was <i>hard work, you guys.</i><br /> <br /> Just to repeat: the idea of a single &quot;Coyote&quot; figure existing across multiple cultures that had little or no contact with each other in pre-modern times is <b>exactly as weird and crazy</b> as saying that every European Thunder God is the same figure and that their name is Thunder. <br /> <br /> The only reason to consolidate every single North American culture together into one big Pantheon of Archetypes is because it'd take a lot of research to actually create a Pantheon for any specific culture. It's so much easier just to consolidate all the Coyote figures into one archetypical &quot;Coyote&quot; even though that ignores the dramatically different perspectives each culture has on that archetype. <br /> <br /> <br /> You can certainly <i>make</i> a Pantheon out of archetypical beings, but it wouldn't be a Pantheon that anyone ever worshipped at any point in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T10:30:29-07:00","id":153968,"title":"","content":"I don't believe Natives practiced &quot;worship&quot; so much that it was more &quot;reverence and respect.&quot; (unless one is a &quot;shaman&quot; to use the term)<br /> I don't believe this thread is for anyone to take personally. But then the game Scion&quot; isn't something to take personally either.<br /> <br /> It's a make-fun list. I like Grandmother Spider, Thunderbird, Bear, White Buffalo Woman, Hare (which we see in Brer Rabbit), Raven, Manitou (in all its meanings), and so much others that have become a part of US culture.<br /> As I already posted, my preference for something serious would be based more along lines of geographical cultural areas. But this isn't serious. So, no need to take it so...My scion, a son of Owl Woman will find out how strong his &quot;Manitou&quot; is (specific purview) through his own adventures, even as he learns from the Wankan Tanka (organization of spirits that leads to the Great Mystery.)<br /> <br /> ...just making this up as I go along...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:10:49-07:00","id":157096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=153968#post153968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Natives practiced &quot;worship&quot; so much that it was more &quot;reverence and respect.&quot; (unless one is a &quot;shaman&quot; to use the term)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is unbelievably offensive. You cannot take an entire continents-worth of cultures and make such a huge generalization about their religious practices. You're also feeding into the harmful stereotype that Native Americans were &quot;tied to the land&quot; and had some super special mystical connection to the Earth that the evil White Man fucked up by introducing Christianity. Some tribes were animists who believed in the spirits of the land, some had gods that they worshipped, some had other systems that I personally know nothing about. Why is that so hard for you to accept? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2425-trueprep1818","name":"TruePrep1818","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T18:53:22-07:00","id":157236,"title":"","content":"I think you should cease the attempt at reading more than what's presented for a game. Or do you find a game that plays with Hindu beliefs (among others) offensive as well? If so, I have to wonder at your reason for being here to begin with, or even posting in this thread. Because this is a <b>game</b> that does exactly that. So feel free to be offended. It's a free country or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:03:46-07:00","id":157254,"title":"","content":"Just because something is a game does not mean that you shouldn't strive to present cultures in a fair, unbiased way. I know a number of Storytellers who descend into mountains of research, read religious texts, all in order to present the Pantheons of the game in the most accurate, and least offensive manor to those who worship the Gods who we depict. <br /> <br /> It is entirely possible to depict the ancient cultures of the Native North Americans in such a way. It just requires some research. Now, of course you are entirely free to depict any Pantheon in any way in which you see fit Shadowflame, but it isn't particularly fair of you to lash out against someone for pointing out that smashing hundreds of cultures down into a stereotypical view of them is not a particularly good thing.<br /> <br /> Now, TruePrep can't make you stop presenting them in whatever way you want, but, the excuse that something is 'just a game', or 'just a joke' is something that can get iffy sometimes. We have to remember that we are dealing with people's religions here, and we therefore, should be respectful of that. We are choosing to represent things that are near, and dear to many people's hearts, and it really does not require much effort from ourselves to present them in a respectful, nicely researched way.<br /> <br /> You are welcome to present the many thousands of Gods and many hundreds of cultures as one homogeneous group Shadowflame, but just as you are allowed to do that, you shouldn't be mad when people complain about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:07:14-07:00","id":157258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157236#post157236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should cease the attempt at reading more than what's presented for a game. Or do you find a game that plays with Hindu beliefs (among others) offensive as well? If so, I have to wonder at your reason for being here to begin with, or even posting in this thread. Because this is a <b>game</b> that does exactly that. So feel free to be offended. It's a free country or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am understanding your position correctly, you would prefer there to be no Hindu beliefs at all. Just an Indo-European pantheon with popular archetypes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:19:09-07:00","id":157289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157236#post157236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should cease the attempt at reading more than what's presented for a game. Or do you find a game that plays with Hindu beliefs (among others) offensive as well? If so, I have to wonder at your reason for being here to begin with, or even posting in this thread. Because this is a <b>game</b> that does exactly that. So feel free to be offended. It's a free country or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't playing with beliefs, this is literally erasing Native Cultures because you don't feel like putting in the time or effort to present them in a fair or balanced way. Also, saying that Native Tribes never worshipped is a baseless claim made due to a racist stereotype of Native Americans as peaceful, animist nature worshippers rather than a huge group of people who all had different beliefs and religious practices. Scion is a game that, by it's very premise, forces storytellers and players to tread some touchy subjects that are incredibly sensitive to people of various cultures; something being a game is no excuse to allow people to be blatantly racist or culturally insensitive. Or were things like blackface okay because they were just PLAYS guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2425-trueprep1818","name":"TruePrep1818","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:21:10-07:00","id":157293,"title":"","content":"How often has it been posted that this is a thread that's for play? How often has Scion been complained about? Because no matter how much you or anyone else refrain about all how respectful you are, you are still playing games with others' beliefs. Now, it doesn't bother me much. And I find it difficult to believe in some anonymous face posting a complaint. After all we are all here to buy into it and perpetuate the game. Anyone who claims otherwise, probably has no business being here. Unless he or she is just trolling...? If he or she really wants to actually do <i>something</i> to help his/her cause celebre, then they can donate some time to help out at Pine Ridge reservation. (or any other res. An acquaintance was at Pine Ridge for a month but they can all use some help.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:23:10-07:00","id":157296,"title":"","content":"Stop putting words in my posts. That's a troll response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:32:35-07:00","id":157305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157296#post157296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stop putting words in my posts. That's a troll response.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's normal for people to be upset when someone is accidentally being racist. It's also normal for others to point out that person is being racist. It's unfortunate that sometimes things get heated. It's not like people are supposed to quietly accept what they consider to be social injustices, even in a game, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:35:16-07:00","id":157306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157293#post157293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often has it been posted that this is a thread that's for play? How often has Scion been complained about? Because no matter how much you or anyone else refrain about all how respectful you are, you are still playing games with others' beliefs. Now, it doesn't bother me much. And I find it difficult to believe in some anonymous face posting a complaint. After all we are all here to buy into it and perpetuate the game. Anyone who claims otherwise, probably has no business being here. Unless he or she is just trolling...? If he or she really wants to actually do <i>something</i> to help his/her cause celebre, then they can donate some time to help out at Pine Ridge reservation. (or any other res. An acquaintance was at Pine Ridge for a month but they can all use some help.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly understand what you mean Shadowflame, so, please correct me if I am wrong.<br /> <br /> But, I think you are saying that we shouldn't be offended because we all play a game that includes ancient cultures, and therefore we are being offensive to them just for the fact that we are playing a game where their Gods, and ancient cultures play large parts.<br /> <br /> Seriously, please let me know if that's wrong. I just had a really hard time reading your post for some reason.<br /> <br /> If that is what you did mean though, I don't think you are right at all. But, even if you are correct, something which I very fundamentally do not believe (that we are being offensive to these cultures and religions just for playing this game, no matter the extent we go to in order to present everything fairly and properly), I still don't believe you are correct in smashing together all of these cultures, religions, and societies into a single mass.<br /> <br /> Even if I am being offensive when I spend hours of research to help Storytellers present ancient cultures in the most accurate way possible (which, again, I don't believe.), I am in no way being equally as offensive as I was if I was refusing to do that research and just basing everything off stereotypical views of those cultures.<br /> <br /> I don't think that TruePep, Twich, or anyone in this thread has been trolling. I believe you very strongly believe that your idea is right, and I believe everyone else here very strongly believes that things could be better handled another way.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I don't understand your reference to the Pine Ridge reservation. I believe you are attempting to make the people who are disagreeing with you guilty, since I can see no other point in including it when you are talking to an international audience.<br /> <br /> I don't believe there is any reason to create a fictional Native American Pantheon, when someone could do their best to present an accurate Pantheon for a single culture, without using stereotypes for the backbone of their concept. If it is just a game, why not play an accurate game? It really is not difficult to do this research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:37:39-07:00","id":157307,"title":"","content":"You mean when someone imagines there's racism. Troll responses typically use false equivalence for their supposed crusades. A little bit of critical thinking should be applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:41:58-07:00","id":157312,"title":"","content":"Once again, Shadowflame tells us that one cannot show a culture any respect within a game. And that a game is so frivolous a notion that the idea that one might actually try and research for it and present it with something close to respectful is a wasteful gesture. And we are presented the false dichotomy that one may only show a culture respect by excluding it from a game about gods of different cultures.<br /> <br /> And, continuing down this path, if someone wants to point out that they feel they can present the Hindu religion faithfully and respectfully in a game, it does not mean that we feel the 1st edition Companion Deva supplement did so. It did not. It was not the best work White Wolf did, to put it diplomatically. (I'm reminded of an oWoD splat that discussed gypsies in a horrendously stereotypical way that they disavowed and had a self-deprecating aside to it in nWoD.) Not to mention that no one has ever proposed doing to the Hindu deities what people FREQUENTLY propose for the various Native American tribes.<br /> <br /> We went through this same song and dance before with Shadowflame on the old forums (this isn't putting words in your posts, so much as using examples you'd previously posted on this exact same topic. Link here: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default73b8.html?g=posts&amp;t=79135\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/d...=posts&amp;t=79135</a>. Shadowflame is midnightsfire there). <br /> <br /> And stereotypes are really the problem here. See, the lumping together of many disparate Native cultures into a single homogenized mess is something that has been done both unintentionally and very, very deliberately to Native Americans for hundreds of years, with the goal of dehumanizing and delegitimizing them. This continues to this day, and causes a ton of problems for Native Americans in financial, political, and social arenas. It's a line of thinking that American culture has only recently tried to correct, and rightly so in the cases where they do. It's a poisonous way of thinking that doesn't do anyone justice. Thought influences actions, and trying to change it is better than doing absolutely nothing. Keeping that attitude of &quot;they're all the same&quot; is a harmful thing in and of itself, and should be corrected where possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:43:49-07:00","id":157315,"title":"","content":"I think Shadowflame can't see my posts or something of the sort.<br /> <br /> I have to say that I think it may be best to just drop this discussion. Neither side is going to be able to convince the other that they are right, and I would really rather not see things getting out of hand and people getting swatted by the Mods after they get caught up in the moment.<br /> <br /> I do hope that we see some more Pantheons produced by the fans for the different tribes of Native North Americans, but I don't think this thread is able to do any good anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:44:46-07:00","id":157318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157307#post157307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Troll responses typically use false equivalence for their supposed crusades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you make an excellent point. The amount of false equivalence you have presented in your posts is beginning to make it clear just who I am dealing with. For what it is worth, I genuinely think you have good intentions. But this is one of those 'road to hell' situations that is probably not going to be popular with very many people. Especially in real life.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157315#post157315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say that I think it may be best to just drop this discussion. Neither side is going to be able to convince the other that they are right, and I would really rather not see things getting out of hand and people getting swatted by the Mods after they get caught up in the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly think you are right. We have all tried our best. Some far more eloquently than others (excellent posts from you and griffinguy). I would hate to see some of us get caught up in the heat of the moment and say something we might regret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 06-02-2014, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T20:00:18-07:00","id":157349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157306#post157306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, I think you are saying that we shouldn't be offended because we all play a game that includes ancient cultures, and therefore we are being offensive to them just for the fact that we are playing a game where their Gods, and ancient cultures play large parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop that. A game with real world beliefs. Sure. But there's nothing that need to be taken offensive here. Too many bring their own hatred in and want to see offense when it doesn't exist no matter what. The focus was on this thread, why? Not how the Devas were handled, (which I know for certain from the Hindus I work with that they would be very offended), not how the Chinese were handled (which we all know is all over China but...). No. Nothing else but this thread which was intended as a game in itself. SERIOUSLY?<br /> I'll never understand this desire to create conflict. to make out of thin air &quot;Us vs Them.&quot; This thread could have done a fade as threads tend to do, but for this.. (I'm reminded of a pic of Muhammad in a newspaper)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157306#post157306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, I don't understand your reference to the Pine Ridge reservation. I believe you are attempting to make the people who are disagreeing with you guilty, since I can see no other point in including it when you are talking to an international audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this &quot;crusader&quot; is desirous of true accomplishment then he should let his actions do more talking and give help to the one demographic that sorely needs it more than any other. Certainly would do more than some anonymous post.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157306#post157306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is just a game, why not play an accurate game? It really is not difficult to do this research.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should &quot;convert or die&quot; be part of that accuracy? I hope not. I'm thinking that might take the fun out of the game, but I suppose it would be how a ST would present it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T20:43:10-07:00","id":157389,"title":"","content":"That's so very true. When I started this thread, I never expected a flame war. I wrote this mainly using the pantheon creation guide used in Scion: Companion. Sure, there was bound to be many worthy gods that would be cut. Hell, with the Pesdajet, I wondered why Maat, being the Egyptian Goddess of Order, and not to mention the spiritual guideline for the culture of Ancient Egypt not included. Yet, the reason why the limit was set to twelve was, to my thoughts, to keep the pantheon itself from being to convoluted. Fortuanately, this new edition is said to be open-ended, unlike the previous one. If Onyx Path is willing, they could create a Pantheon Book dedicated to the dozens of Native American pantheons that existed as a legitimate PC option. I'm just hoping that Onyx Path considers this for a future book because I consider the culture to be rich and full of opportunities for Scions that hail from that area of the world.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Watcher? I doubt that the Yazata and the Tuatha are actually the same. First of all, that connection was just a sidebar option from the Yazata book. Plus, for them to be in Ireland, they would have to be one of the previous inhabitants that got kicked out of Ireland by the Formorians before the arrival of the Tuatha. And second, their incentives are different. For the Yazata, from what I read, their incentives is based on Duty to the Virtues of the Yazata. Those who don't follow them well gain the ire of their divine parent, a possible repo of a Birthright, and their time in the Persian Underworld would be more difficult. The Tuatha, however, derive their incentives based on Enech (Irish Honor) and Geas, which, if they fail to accomplish that, means a reduction of Enech (similiar to losing face for the Japanese) and they can't use their Boons until the slight has been rectified. Completely different from the Yazata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T20:56:50-07:00","id":157395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157389#post157389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Watcher? I doubt that the Yazata and the Tuatha are actually the same. First of all, that connection was just a sidebar option from the Yazata book. Plus, for them to be in Ireland, they would have to be one of the previous inhabitants that got kicked out of Ireland by the Formorians before the arrival of the Tuatha. And second, their incentives are different. For the Yazata, from what I read, their incentives is based on Duty to the Virtues of the Yazata. Those who don't follow them well gain the ire of their divine parent, a possible repo of a Birthright, and their time in the Persian Underworld would be more difficult. The Tuatha, however, derive their incentives based on Enech (Irish Honor) and Geas, which, if they fail to accomplish that, means a reduction of Enech (similiar to losing face for the Japanese) and they can't use their Boons until the slight has been rectified. Completely different from the Yazata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm terribly sorry that I wasn't clear Jackalope, I believe you are talking about when I said:<br /> <br /> &quot;You have Hunter Gather societies, Agrarian societies, Herders, Raiders, Urban, Nomadic, all of them different and unique from one and other. They may have once, in some long ancient past all come from an original root society that we have failed thus far to identify in any way shape or form, but even if they did and this progect attempted to play off this idea of the collective past of all of these hundreds, and hundreds of cultures, I would have to tell you that by the same logic, the Deva, the Yazata, the Tuatha, the Aesir, the Theoi, the Elohim, the Nemetondevos, and more are, by that logic, the same Pantheon for they descended from the same root culture.&quot;<br /> <br /> Correct?<br /> <br /> \u200bI am very sorry if I was not clear enough with that explenation, I never intended to say that they are the same, in fact, I was attempting to show how silly it would be to combine the Native Americans into one solid culture because they 'may' have at some far distant point in the past have shared a common root culture, just as the Deva, Yazata, Tuatha, Aesir, Elohim, Nemetondevos, and Theoi do. (The Indo-European people are the source of all of those cultures. It really is fascinating.)<br /> <br /> The Yazata and the Tuatha are entirely different. I actually was one of the two main sources for information, and designed a lot of the Enech Purview which you are talking about. Or, at least I am assuming so, since RAW Enech has no ability to lose the ability to use the PsP as you reference. I was actually the source for the idea of losing the ability to use Enech if you lose too many Face Points.<br /> <br /> I am very sorry I was not clear enough.<br /> <br /> But, if I am explaining the wrong bit, please let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-03-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T20:59:23-07:00","id":157397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157389#post157389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Watcher? I doubt that the Yazata and the Tuatha are actually the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry if I missed something, but I do not think anybody suggested that the Yazata were actually the Tuatha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:03:07-07:00","id":157402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157389#post157389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, and Watcher? I doubt that the Yazata and the Tuatha are actually the same. First of all, that connection was just a sidebar option from the Yazata book. Plus, for them to be in Ireland, they would have to be one of the previous inhabitants that got kicked out of Ireland by the Formorians before the arrival of the Tuatha. And second, their incentives are different. For the Yazata, from what I read, their incentives is based on Duty to the Virtues of the Yazata. Those who don't follow them well gain the ire of their divine parent, a possible repo of a Birthright, and their time in the Persian Underworld would be more difficult. The Tuatha, however, derive their incentives based on Enech (Irish Honor) and Geas, which, if they fail to accomplish that, means a reduction of Enech (similiar to losing face for the Japanese) and they can't use their Boons until the slight has been rectified. Completely different from the Yazata.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Watcher was the guy who helped Iry and myself with designing Enech, and is probably my go-to guy for anything Irish, I really, really find that idea of educating him on the purview and pantheon that he co-wrote with me makes me chuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T21:03:55-07:00","id":157405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157389#post157389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and Watcher? I doubt that the Yazata and the Tuatha are actually the same. First of all, that connection was just a sidebar option from the Yazata book. Plus, for them to be in Ireland, they would have to be one of the previous inhabitants that got kicked out of Ireland by the Formorians before the arrival of the Tuatha. And second, their incentives are different. For the Yazata, from what I read, their incentives is based on Duty to the Virtues of the Yazata. Those who don't follow them well gain the ire of their divine parent, a possible repo of a Birthright, and their time in the Persian Underworld would be more difficult. The Tuatha, however, derive their incentives based on Enech (Irish Honor) and Geas, which, if they fail to accomplish that, means a reduction of Enech (similiar to losing face for the Japanese) and they can't use their Boons until the slight has been rectified. Completely different from the Yazata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think he said what you think he said! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 06-03-2014, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:35:48-07:00","id":158026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=157395#post157395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm terribly sorry that I wasn't clear Jackalope, I believe you are talking about when I said:<br /> <br /> &quot;You have Hunter Gather societies, Agrarian societies, Herders, Raiders, Urban, Nomadic, all of them different and unique from one and other. They may have once, in some long ancient past all come from an original root society that we have failed thus far to identify in any way shape or form, but even if they did and this progect attempted to play off this idea of the collective past of all of these hundreds, and hundreds of cultures, I would have to tell you that by the same logic, the Deva, the Yazata, the Tuatha, the Aesir, the Theoi, the Elohim, the Nemetondevos, and more are, by that logic, the same Pantheon for they descended from the same root culture.&quot;<br /> <br /> Correct?<br /> <br /> \u200bI am very sorry if I was not clear enough with that explenation, I never intended to say that they are the same, in fact, I was attempting to show how silly it would be to combine the Native Americans into one solid culture because they 'may' have at some far distant point in the past have shared a common root culture, just as the Deva, Yazata, Tuatha, Aesir, Elohim, Nemetondevos, and Theoi do. (The Indo-European people are the source of all of those cultures. It really is fascinating.)<br /> <br /> The Yazata and the Tuatha are entirely different. I actually was one of the two main sources for information, and designed a lot of the Enech Purview which you are talking about. Or, at least I am assuming so, since RAW Enech has no ability to lose the ability to use the PsP as you reference. I was actually the source for the idea of losing the ability to use Enech if you lose too many Face Points.<br /> <br /> I am very sorry I was not clear enough.<br /> <br /> But, if I am explaining the wrong bit, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Elohim are Semitic in origin. There are some false cognates and syncretism and cross-pollination (both back and forth), but the core of the pantheon is pretty dead center Semitic. So their closest relative pantheon would be..... I dunno, John and Anne's Arabian pantheon? (A much better conjuring of a pantheon out of almost thin air than the Nemetondevos.) There is some heavy Semitic influence on the Annunaki as well, though the core is Sumerian. Enlil, Inanna, Ereskigal - Sumerian, Marduk - Akkadian/Semetic. Aside: The Annunaki seem like a pantheon that is location-based as opposed to population-based. You come into their territory, you end up worshiping them. At least for a couple of thousand years. Egyptian are largely the same - the Nubian pantheon started looking a whole lot more like the Egyptian (and integrating into it) after they took over the land. Same thing to a degree with the Graeco-Roman. Just ask Marc Anthony about that. It's a big reason he lost Roman support. Worshiping foreign beast-faced gods.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Deva, Yazata, whatever you want to call the Slavic gods, Baltic gods,Theoi/Graeco-Roman gods, Aesir, Tuatha De, whatever you want to call the Welsh gods (I used Dai Twyleth), Nemetondevos (whatever those are, since we have next to nothing about them to build a pantheon on), Tocharian gods (not sure if we have enough, most of the work would be in Chinese and largely suppressed by the government) and Siwanna (Hittite gods) all have the same origin. That's why we can play the Indra is Perun is Zeus is Thor is Taranis (maybe) is Tarhunt games. (Since we can also replace Thor with Tyr... or maybe not... or both...). That's comparative mythology not game mechanics, trying to match up Virtues and Underworlds and the like. That's why it's germane to the discussion. Conflating all the Native American pantheons could playing this game and creating an ur-pantheon that never existed but might approximate one that might have. Sorta like using linguistic regression to take French, Spanish, Italian, Romansch, Romanian and create Proto-Romance. Which looks like Latin, which did exist, but isn't the same. It's at best an educated stab in the dark. And that gets dicier an dicier the further back you try to push it. <br /> <br /> However, that doesn't appear to be what is being attempted here at all. Which is taking various popular culture constructions and conflations and the more well known mythical figures from 2/3 of a continent (I presume we are keeping Mesoamerica out of this, even though, technically, it IS a part of North America) and building a pantheon (and a PSP) from those.<br /> <br /> Which renders the last issue a little tangential... There are three major not-related cutlural groupings in North America. This is backed by linguistic and genetic evidence as well as culture and archaeology (this is getting way more complicated currently, but the core ideas still pertain): the Inuit tribes of the far north, the Dine peoples (including the Navajo and a lot of other groups) and everyone else. It seems like this represents three different Siberian to North American migrations. So, if you are looking to recreate proto-pantheons, you should have three separate ones at least, with some very weird distribution on the last two. And that doesn't even work all that well mythologically speaking as there are some really profound and weird parallels between significant aspects of Aztec and Hopi/Zuni/Pueblo myths and who knows how THAT happened.... (There are some myths you can interpret, bend and twist to do so [FUN!] but there is no way to do it by culture/language... unless there is.... through the Anasazi, maybe....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:41:58-07:00","id":158034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=158026#post158026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Elohim are Semitic in origin. There are some false cognates and syncretism and cross-pollination (both back and forth), but the core of the pantheon is pretty dead center Semitic. So their closest relative pantheon would be..... I dunno, John and Anne's Arabian pantheon? (A much better conjuring of a pantheon out of almost thin air than the Nemetondevos.) There is some heavy Semitic influence on the Annunaki as well, though the core is Sumerian. Enlil, Inanna, Ereskigal - Sumerian, Marduk - Akkadian/Semetic. Aside: The Annunaki seem like a pantheon that is location-based as opposed to population-based. You come into their territory, you end up worshiping them. At least for a couple of thousand years. Egyptian are largely the same - the Nubian pantheon started looking a whole lot more like the Egyptian (and integrating into it) after they took over the land. Same thing to a degree with the Graeco-Roman. Just ask Marc Anthony about that. It's a big reason he lost Roman support. Worshiping foreign beast-faced gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, my mistake. It makes more sense as a cross pollination, I was just thinking of the Three Kings, but that makes sense as a cultural exchange between themselves and some of the other cultures in the areas where they traded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=158026#post158026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, that doesn't appear to be what is being attempted here at all. Which is taking various popular culture constructions and conflations and the more well known mythical figures from 2/3 of a continent (I presume we are keeping Mesoamerica out of this, even though, technically, it IS a part of North America) and building a pantheon (and a PSP) from those.<br /> <br /> Which renders the last issue a little tangential... There are three major not-related cutlural groupings in North America. This is backed by linguistic and genetic evidence as well as culture and archaeology (this is getting way more complicated currently, but the core ideas still pertain): the Inuit tribes of the far north, the Dine peoples (including the Navajo and a lot of other groups) and everyone else. It seems like this represents three different Siberian to North American migrations. So, if you are looking to recreate proto-pantheons, you should have three separate ones at least, with some very weird distribution on the last two. And that doesn't even work all that well mythologically speaking as there are some really profound and weird parallels between significant aspects of Aztec and Hopi/Zuni/Pueblo myths and who knows how THAT happened.... (There are some myths you can interpret, bend and twist to do so [FUN!] but there is no way to do it by culture/language... unless there is.... through the Anasazi, maybe....)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I didn't know that we actually had any solid research done on the truly ancient people in the areas. I knew there were some theories about the arrival of peoples in South America by sea, which would be incredibly impressive if true.<br /> <br /> But, my point was to show how ridiculous it would be to make a Pantheon based on a common ancestor culture. You lose so much, all of these fantastic people to interact with by boiling them down to their core concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:38:13-07:00","id":158299,"title":"","content":"I concur that it's not a good idea on several levels. It's actually a WORSE idea in some ways. than just shellacing together a bunch of things and making them fit into something resembling a coherent whole. <br /> <br /> There is a lot of material on the peopling of the Americas. Including the South American stuff. Looks like the southern route is still looking like a bust. The DNA indicates they probably came down the western seaboard, which was further out as the water level was lower. <br /> <br /> Three Kings? As in Melchior, Balthazar and Caspar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:56:21-07:00","id":158318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=158299#post158299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three Kings? As in Melchior, Balthazar and Caspar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, sorry. I mean the three kings of the Elohim. Ba'al, Mot, and Yam. Not the Three Kings from the bible. Ba'al, Mot, and Yam are similar to the other Sky, Earth, and Sea King trinities you get with the Greeks, and I think the Hittites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T16:29:45-07:00","id":158388,"title":"","content":"Mot and Yamm really come across more as Titans. (Though I have seen a votive statuette of Yamm, I have never heard of a temple to him or Mot. Unless Mot is actually Moloch, which he could be...) People didn't really so much worship them as mention them as having gotten gacked by Ba'al. Who may not have been El's son. Maybe grandson. Maybe Dagon was his father. That would explain why El was so peeved that he wanted a palace. (Not sure why El is handing out palaces or the rights to build them, since Kothar does all the building. El lives in a tent. Why doesn't he award himself a palace?) It really wasn't his place. But then again maybe not. The myths are contrary and equivocal. It's also hard to separate Asherah, Asterat and Anat. The last is more distinctive, but the other two intergrade into each other. If Asherah and Asterat are separate, that argues for the Ba'al getting kicked down a generation. Ba'al is the son of Asterat and Dagon and Mot and Yamm are his uncles? I dunno, you can play with it a lot and get enough backing to do it whichever way you want. I usually like to go for maximum distinct number of gods. More fodder for parenthood.<br /> <br /> We may be imposing our standard Sky/Sea/Earth trio on this pantheon and it just happens to fit. Or there is some influence from nearby cultures. Or the trio doesn't have a sky god and is more Upper World/Sea/Underworld (Dagon/Yamm/Mot) and El is keeping the sky to himself. Though Dagon gets some fishy-ness... Or maybe he's both fields and waves? When Yamm dies there's definitely a spot open for someone to expand his influence...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:11:58-07:00","id":159061,"title":"","content":"What's the point of my previous post(s) relevant to this thread? <br /> <br /> A lot. Look at how complex the relationships are between the Old World pantheons we &quot;know&quot;. Going back to a time 'when they were all one&quot; doesn't work as a good explanation for glomming different pantheons together. Not only is it tricky, it results in hypothetical pantheons of possible deities without any myths that aren't equally bland constructs for the purposes of the game. Plus, things that seem like they fit together, don't. They weren't the same and trying to make them the same oversimplifies the distinctiveness that makes each pantheon unique, interesting and worth playing.<br /> <br /> So making up pantheons from multiple cultures becomes and exercise of painting over distinctiveness with a VERY heavy brush and cherry-picking a few favorites. Which is, I guess, fine, if that works for you. For a lot of people who play Scion and post on here, that's not what they are looking for. At all. In depth research and persnickity detail is more the order of the day. We have people who are hell-bent on figuring out a way to separate out the Roman/Latin pantheon from the Greek! (Not me, to be clear. I can't distinguish enough cool stories between the two to make it worth my time. I prefer to think that Ares just grew up a little and we get Mars - unless it's Fateful Aura time and he's standing on the mound of Hisarlik, the site of the city of Troy. Then he'd probably be forced to act all juvenile and spiteful again. Ditto for Aphrodite to Venus. The rest of the strictly &quot;Roman&quot; gods are pretty much Etruscan. Which is another whole issue. We have few to no stories about them except in a Roman context. What does that mean? Did the Etruscan gods just move from their Godhome to Olympus? If so, why?) <br /> <br /> That means this idea is going against the grain. Anothers fine thing. I do it myself all the time. (For example, I'll NEVER talk about the &quot;Abrahamic Pantheon&quot;. Abraham doesn't matter a fig to me when I talk about Near Eastern mythology. I'm not interested in looking at those myths through that lens and I don't want to tackle the whole &quot;People of the Book&quot; issue in that way at all. See? That's my thing. I'm standing firm. Let's discuss...)<br /> <br /> The issue a lot of people are having with this isn't &quot;lumping vs. splitting&quot; . It seems to be lumping together things in a way that is similar (if not congruent) to the way in which the people who followed the deities in question have been subjected to as a part of what happened during imperialism. As a culture, we're sensitive to oppression and more interested in restitution than the people who did the original lumping that simplified the 1000 cultures of North America into&quot; Indians&quot;. Whatever the motivation, when someone does something that does the same thing, people are going to equate the two and react to the new idea just like they'd react to the old one. <br /> <br /> Which they are and they are pretty justified in doing so. This is dangerous ground. Perhaps even more dangerous than handling monotheism vs polytheism and how to deal with the interface in a game explicitly about one that goes out of its way to barely deal with the other. <br /> <br /> I guess my solution would be to pare the whole thing down and go for trying to work up the Lakota. Most of the deities you were looking to put in your uber-pantheon are represented. You can also learn a lot about something you didn't know. Which I know I love. I pick pantheons to play often based on the fact I don't know much about the myths of that culture. <br /> <br /> But, Golden Rule, you can do what you want to and this is a perfectly fine forum to get some assistance doing it. Just expect that people who fundamentally disagree with you will be chiming in as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:03:41-07:00","id":159115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159061#post159061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An amazing post goes here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to take a moment to express that this is an excellently written post that wonderfully captures the spirit of the situation, as well as my own feelings on the matter. Or in more modern parlance, <b>Truth</b>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T09:46:54-07:00","id":159151,"title":"","content":"And something similar to this was what I was looking towards:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20090103211716/rifts/images/thumb/1/1d/827.jpg/200px-827.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> A book that sold well, and was a fun read too.<br /> <br /> If I want archaeology and anthropology, well, I have those books too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T14:32:24-07:00","id":159357,"title":"","content":"And yet, that exact story can be told without disrespecting the culture of the guy on the hoverbike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T14:49:25-07:00","id":159370,"title":"","content":"Lol, You're going to say that if I reprinted some of the info in that book...(and just how generic that totem system is) there won't be the same hate-parade posts? Really? Because that's near exactly what I was posting to begin with! I just altered it to fit Scion. (The &quot;Mystic Warrior,&quot; The &quot;Totem Warrior...&quot; o yeah...) And that's the thing, it was fun. We could have all those same type of warriors in any tribal region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:00:19-07:00","id":159385,"title":"","content":"My grandma read me Little Black Sambo when I was young. I loved it, because I was young and I had no idea what it was about. It was this strange story of a little boy who gets chased by tigers and then tricks the tigers into melting themselves into butter. Why wouldn't a small child enjoy that story? That doesn't make Little Black Sambo any less racist or insensitive. I'm currently reading an anthology of HP Lovecraft. He is <i>deeply</i> racist, classist and sexist. I've read Conan, too, and Howard has the same problems (not as bad as Lovecraft, though). I'm reading them because they're hugely important to American literary history and because they inform so much of modern culture. They're still <i>super racist</i>. <br /> <br /> Just because something is fun doesn't mean it isn't racist. You can have fun without being racist, though. If no one says &quot;hey, now, that's pretty racist, maybe we should fix it so it isn't?&quot; then nothing ever changes. You can tell a story every bit as fun <i>without</i> disregarding the cultural diversity and importance of an entire half of the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:27:21-07:00","id":159393,"title":"","content":"Crying racism when posting about animal spirits is not only ridiculous, but damn selective. Or are you saying that it's racist (an intriguing use of the term) when writing about such as Hindu beliefs? Why stop at what is generously described as something with Native American flavor when we can lament over a game involving the third largest religion in the world? You only level such a charge when something speaks of totem animals. How screwed up is that priority? Maybe if we run a game based on Islam no one will complain over that. Or is the 2nd largest religion finally crossing the line? Now, I'm off to buy the pdf of Spirit West, because it was fun to read, and my book is looking a bit beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:59:33-07:00","id":159424,"title":"","content":"Shadowflame if you seriously don't understand why shrugging your shoulders and saying &quot;eh, all Native Americans worshipped the same animal spirits&quot; is disrespectful and racist, then you don't understand the history of colonialism, imperialism or modern racism.<br /> <br /> As for people <i>only</i> complaining about racism against Native Americans, that's crap. I'm also taking issue with similar treatment being aimed at the Australian Aboriginal cultures in Jackalope's other thread. People <i>in this thread</i> have agreed that the portrayal of Hinduism in Scion is poorly done. The portrayal of Aztecs is poorly done. Scion has a <i>lot</i> of problems with shoddy research that just can't be excused because <i>holy shit the Internet is a thing!</i> It takes an hour to learn more about these cultures and read primary sources on their mythology. That's an hour more research than seems to have been done in many cases for Scion. <br /> <br /> People <i>do</i> make games, movies, songs and other popular culture artifacts based on Christianity, Islam and other major world religions. They do it <i>all the time</i>. Some of them are respectful and awesome, some of them are shitty and narrow minded. Back in college, I watched anime where I'm pretty sure what happened was that someone just flipped through the Book of Revelations and pulled out pages at random. That's still pretty crappy, but it doesn't compare to the <i>systematic</i> and <i>intensive</i> denigration, disrespect and dismissal of New World native cultures and religions that has gone on for hundreds of years. So, yeah, people nowadays are a bit more sensitive to that kind of thing than the offhandedly horrible mash of Christian word-salad that occasionally pops up in video games, or CS Lewis's portrayal of Totally-Not-Islam in the Narnia series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T16:33:47-07:00","id":159440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowflame if you seriously don't understand why shrugging your shoulders and saying &quot;eh, all Native Americans worshipped the same animal spirits&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> And where did I say that? (Is there some sort of system that gives you points for putting words in my posts? Because I'm pretty sure at the &quot;worst&quot; I did post:<br /> <i>It's more or less taking what's more commonly known and presenting it for fun. No culture created here that I can see. I recall Palladium books doing something similar. And it was a fun time reading it. But I never once thought it was a different culture, or an attempt at such a thing. I do see this as similar to what White Wolf did with Werewolf the Apocalypse, and the totem system (and related hierarchies) created....It's a make-fun list. I like Grandmother Spider, Thunderbird, Bear, White Buffalo Woman, Hare (which we see in Brer Rabbit), Raven, Manitou (in all its meanings), and so much others that have become a part of US culture. As I already posted, my preference for something serious would be based more along lines of geographical cultural areas. But this isn't serious. So, no need to take it so...</i><br /> <br /> These are my words. Not the ones you made up. Racism? Seems to me that you're making up stuff as you go along now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 06-04-2014, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:10:55-07:00","id":159455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159440#post159440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are my words. Not the ones you made up. Racism? Seems to me that you're making up stuff as you go along now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a question for you. Why do you think so many different people are saying the same thing to you? Do you think so many of us are thin skinned? Or so many of us take things too seriously? Or so many of us are misunderstanding your words? I honestly want to know what you think is happening here, from your perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:18:13-07:00","id":159477,"title":"","content":"What's &quot;commonly known&quot; is wrong. What's &quot;commonly known&quot; is a bunch of racist bullcrap. You seem to be saying &quot;that's fine! It's just a game! Games don't need to be realistic or respectful! They're just <i>games!</i>&quot; No. Even fun things need to be respectful. That's why we don't use racial slurs in eeny-meeny-miny-moe anymore. That's why the Washington Redskins continue to be campaigned against for their racial slur of a mascot and team name. <br /> <br /> If that isn't what you're saying, then please do explain what you <i>are</i> saying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T17:57:56-07:00","id":159548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159440#post159440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do see this as similar to what White Wolf did with Werewolf the Apocalypse, and the totem system (and related hierarchies) created....It's a make-fun list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves aren't real. American Indians are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:19:00-07:00","id":159620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's &quot;commonly known&quot; is wrong. What's &quot;commonly known&quot; is a bunch of racist bullcrap.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's your belief talking. What's commonly known in the US today is that most of us know of &quot;Coyote.&quot; And a finer example of a trickster figure in the continental US can't be made. And if you can't make your argument without given me loaded crap terms like &quot;racism&quot; then your belief (versus the truth) isn't going to go very far. (And I assure you I am very familiar with what truly constitutes as racism. Your ill-use of it is rather astonishing to me) Quite frankly I see your argument as immaterial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spirit West</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Coyote</u></b> Traits: The spirit god Coyote has the most expansive reputation in Native American legends. He is the ultimate trickster and con man, but he is also often a hero and earns a unique place as a respected leader and trickster. The antics of Coyote are tolerated because it is believed that he understands much about the universe, and by questioning the ways of man, even sacred ways, he is helping them to learn. The Coyote Totem represents both the negative and positive (not necessarily good and evil) and is ideal for characters of unprincipled alignment (anarchist and aberrant to a lesser degree). Coyote is both smart and silly/buffoonish; crude and kind; generous and greedy; friendly and treacherous; forthright and tricky; at times he is honest, knowledgeable and helpful, yet other times he is deceitful, secretive and tricky. Coyote is curious and likes to know about everything and everybody, although he is not likely to share all his secrets or treasures. Bold, confident and charismatic (but rarely reckless or foolish), Coyote prefers to work behind the scenes, making a surprise appearance (with impeccable timing) to reap the reward and accolades of others for his handiwork. He can be manipulative but has a high regard for life and never sacrifices a pawn out of cruelty or revenge. In fact, Coyote can exhibit surprising loyalty to those he likes, respects or finds challenging. Despite his antics, Coyote tends to do what's right/moral and cares about people, especially Native Americans. He enjoys all aspects of life and drinks deeply in life's experience \u2014 the more challenging and risky, the better.<br /> Skills: Disguise (+10%), imitate voices (+5%), ventriloquism (+5%), and Cardsharp (+10%; loves to gamble).<br /> Bonuses: +1 to I.Q., +1 to M.A., +1 on initiative, and +2 to dodge. Powers: +3 to M.A., +1 to P.P., +4 to speed; claws add 1D4 M.D. to supernatural P.S. damage, bite does 2D6 M.D., heightened smell enables the coyote to track by smell: 50% +5% per level, and recognize specific scents: 40% +5% per level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what you're calling racism...I should hope that you realize by now just how silly that sounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren't real. American Indians are.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hindus are also real. Oh but look at what was done with Hinduism, among others (Your point was rather pointless.)<br /> <br /> *sigh* This is pointless. People believe what they want to believe..see what they want to see.<br /> <br /> I used to own this book:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pictures.abebooks.com/WWABE/9720677906.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But I guess that was &quot;racist&quot; too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 06-04-2014, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:19:32-07:00","id":159621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159440#post159440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These are my words. Not the ones you made up. Racism? Seems to me that you're making up stuff as you go along now.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the second page....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=153968#post153968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Natives practiced &quot;worship&quot; so much that it was more &quot;reverence and respect.&quot; (unless one is a &quot;shaman&quot; to use the term).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a direct quote, from you. And the statement here essentially translates to &quot;The Native Americans did/do not have a real religion&quot;. That is a racist sentiment. That kind of language is the kind I've read among those that felt that the Native way of life was frivolous and backwards and that if they therefore had to fully assimilate into America and abandon their culture entirely. Your previous endorsement of whitewashing Native mythic figures alludes to that, but the statement I quoted blurts it outright.<br /> <br /> Now, I freely admit, I'm a person who, more often than I would like, says things in the wrong way. I have said many things that are insensitive and stupid, but that I never intended when I said them. However, it didn't matter that I didn't MEAN to be insensitive and stupid, the thing I SAID was insensitive and stupid, and that is what you have done here. <br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to SAY racist things without BEING racist. Problem is (again, the disconnect between what is said and how it's taken), when we say an action is racist, it often comes as a value judgment. Pointing out that you said something racist comes with the invisible parenthetical statement of &quot;and you're a bad person for saying so.&quot; So, I will say this: the fact that you said something that comes across as racist doesn't mean we think you're a bad person. <br /> <br /> The fact that you keep doubling down on your statements and calling us overly sensitive about it, however... well, that tends to imply that you don't CARE if your statements sound racist or not. And... that doesn't look good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T19:38:13-07:00","id":159656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159621#post159621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis is a direct quote, from you. And the statement here essentially translates to &quot;The Native Americans did/do not have a real religion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you want to read what someone believes to be...fine. But don't add to it. Because then all you're doing is making stuff up that was never posted. You don't re-interpret the English language to make a point that doesn't exist. If you know better than what was posted then say so. Show me what you know. I enjoy learning. But no. You nor others did that. Instead all you wanted to do was castigate, belittle, and bitch and moan...<br /> <br /> And stop with the racist charge. None of you seem to know what that means. Let me help <a href=\"http://www.yourdictionary.com/racism\" target=\"_blank\">Racism</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:04:31-07:00","id":159667,"title":"","content":"Here's the first definition from that site (bold emphasis mine)... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Racism is a belief that one race is superior to the other <b>or the practice of treating a person or group of people differently on the basis of their race.</b></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You are treating a group of people (Native Americans) differently on the basis of their race. Specifically, that they get a watered down, mishmash of a pantheon whereas other groups of people (you specifically mention Hindus and Chinese) should be treated more &quot;respectfully&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:06:29-07:00","id":159670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159656#post159656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And stop with the racist charge. None of you seem to know what that means. Let me help <a href=\"http://www.yourdictionary.com/racism\" target=\"_blank\">Racism</a></div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\">Racism is a belief that one race is superior to the other or the practice of treating a person or group of people differently on the basis of their race.</span></span></span></li> <li>any program or practice of racial discrimination, segregation, etc., specif., such a program or practice that upholds the political or economic domination of one race over another or others</li> </ul>Accidentally suggesting something offensive happens to everyone, but standing your ground and insisting that your offensive behavior is not offensive is missing the point. Offensive behavior is not something that you can rationalize or tell other people they should not be feeling. It is something you have made other people feel. I would like to ask you one final time. No, I am literally <i>begging</i> you to please take the feelings of others into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:13:38-07:00","id":159676,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should have read the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:37:57-07:00","id":159694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159676#post159676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you should have read the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I am very sorry, but I feel like we have done the best we can. Many of us have tried to explain the problem as clearly as we could, and I personally begged you to put aside explanations and respect the feelings of others. But there is only so much anyone can do, even when this many people are trying to help you. I wish you good luck in your future adventures.<br /> <br /> For those who are unfamiliar with the Onyx Path Forums, I can offer steps to setting your ignore features (for those who want to use them). Left click your user name in the upper right hand corner of the screen. Left click 'User Settings'. Left click 'Account'. Scroll down and enter the name of the person you want to ignore in the 'Ignore List'. Left click 'Save Changes'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:44:07-07:00","id":159769,"title":"","content":"Yes, the modern American conception of Coyote is racist. It doesn't pay any attention to the fact that &quot;Coyote&quot; never existed. Ever. <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/12/cunning-canine-corporation.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a list</a> of a <i>few</i> of the figures that were tossed together to create the modern idea of &quot;Coyote&quot;. <br /> <br /> The approach that lead to &quot;Coyote&quot; is <i>exactly the same</i> as if someone was to propose a European Pantheon that combined Zeus, Thor and Perun into &quot;Thunder&quot;, with Manannan Mac Lir, Neptune and Njord mixed together into &quot;Sea Lord&quot;. Except while no one seriously does that to European cultures, <i>exactly</i> that was done for <i>hundreds of years</i> to New World cultures. Because who cares if some brown people get offended? They're savages anyway and their cultures aren't really anything but some savage tribes. Their religions weren't real, just some silly superstitions to be stomped out so they can find <i>real</i> religion. <br /> <br /> No one is suggesting that the original intent of this thread was malicious, but it upholds a common Western convention that <i>is</i> malicious. Not intentionally, but because of ignorance and lack of awareness. No one is <i>attacking</i> anyone, except to say that just accepting the current (raaaaacist) convention is bad and instead some research should be done so that fiction and games, which are vehicles of pop culture perpetuation, can be a little bit more enlightened.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and yeah, the old D&amp;D books about Barbarians and Shamans? Yeah, they've got some racist baggage alright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T09:36:55-07:00","id":160031,"title":"","content":"You, know, those people up North with hair like straw or an old man's, who can't even talk properly. Instead of speaking the REAL language (meaning Greek), they just make noises that sound like &quot;Bar, bar, bar&quot;. <br /> <br /> Even the word barbarian is originally a very very ethnocentric one. (Since what &quot;race&quot; means is so mutable over time, I'll go with that one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T14:01:28-07:00","id":160231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159769#post159769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the modern American conception of Coyote is racist. It doesn't pay any attention to the fact that &quot;Coyote&quot; never existed. Ever. <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/12/cunning-canine-corporation.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a list</a> of a <i>few</i> of the figures that were tossed together to create the modern idea of &quot;Coyote&quot;.<br /> <br /> The approach that lead to &quot;Coyote&quot; is <i>exactly the same</i> as if someone was to propose a European Pantheon that combined Zeus, Thor and Perun into &quot;Thunder&quot;, with Manannan Mac Lir, Neptune and Njord mixed together into &quot;Sea Lord&quot;. Except while no one seriously does that to European cultures, <i>exactly</i> that was done for <i>hundreds of years</i> to New World cultures. Because who cares if some brown people get offended? They're savages anyway and their cultures aren't really anything but some savage tribes. Their religions weren't real, just some silly superstitions to be stomped out so they can find <i>real</i> religion.<br /> <br /> No one is suggesting that the original intent of this thread was malicious, but it upholds a common Western convention that <i>is</i> malicious. Not intentionally, but because of ignorance and lack of awareness. No one is <i>attacking</i> anyone, except to say that just accepting the current (raaaaacist) convention is bad and instead some research should be done so that fiction and games, which are vehicles of pop culture perpetuation, can be a little bit more enlightened.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and yeah, the old D&amp;D books about Barbarians and Shamans? Yeah, they've got some racist baggage alright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to burst your bubble, Telgar, but from what it seems to indicate on that page that you linked to, is that the purpose of Coyote varies, depending on where it comes from. The Western tribes are more sympathetic to Coyote then the Eastern tribes, and the fact that Coyote might have originated in the Aztec line makes me think that he was kicked out of that pantheon and that he headed North to the tribes of America (Turtle Island). As for the different names, they are Coyote's ALIASES much like the other gods in Scion (if you didn't pay attention to the AKA attachment to the names before.)<br /> <br /> So your statement that Coyote never existed because of his different roles in different tribal mythologies is like saying that Christianity isn't a true religion because it borrows heavily into Judiasm (and lightly into Islam. (Seriously, the Nativity scene is mentioned in the Quran.))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T14:22:41-07:00","id":160273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=160231#post160231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the different names, they are Coyote's ALIASES much like the other gods in Scion (if you didn't pay attention to the AKA attachment to the names before.)</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They are figures from cultures so different that many of them <i>never even contacted each other</i> before colonization. They are figures from places as far apart as Britain and Russia. Saying that an East Coast Coyote-God and a West Coast Coyote-God are just &quot;aliases&quot; of the same figure <i><b><u>is exactly like saying that Indra, Zeus, Thor and Perun are the same</u></b></i>. That's racist and that's disrespectful. That's the <i>entire problem</i> that people on this thread have been discussing.<br /> <br /> The AKA section is <i>exactly as offensive</i> in many cases. Sometimes, like with some of the Egyptians, its just their name translated in other languages. Sometimes, though, it's saying that Mayan and Aztec religions were the same <i>and that is objectively wrong</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=160231#post160231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your statement that Coyote never existed because of his different roles in different tribal mythologies is like saying that Christianity isn't a true religion because it borrows heavily into Judiasm (and lightly into Islam. (Seriously, the Nativity scene is mentioned in the Quran.))</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. At all. Saying &quot;Coyote&quot; is a real figure is like saying Judaism, Islam and Christianity are the <i>same</i> religion because they share certain aspects. Coyote never existed. A few dozen different coyote-figures existed, each with their own personality, their own stories and their own unique cultural significance. Reducing them to just &quot;aspects&quot; of one big archetype is bad scholarship and bad practice because <i>that's never done to European figures</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T13:44:32-07:00","id":161049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=160273#post160273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They are figures from cultures so different that many of them <i>never even contacted each other</i> before colonization. They are figures from places as far apart as Britain and Russia. Saying that an East Coast Coyote-God and a West Coast Coyote-God are just &quot;aliases&quot; of the same figure <i><b><u>is exactly like saying that Indra, Zeus, Thor and Perun are the same</u></b></i>. That's racist and that's disrespectful. That's the <i>entire problem</i> that people on this thread have been discussing.<br /> <br /> No. In terms of the game Scion, they ARE the same person. I'm just applying the game mechanics to different personas within the same AREA. There's nothing racist about this. As for your other claim. You are saying that in the game world of Scion, Zeus, Odin/Thor, and this Perun guy are the same god. To clarify, you claim that a Mediterranean god, a Scandanavian god, and a Middle-Eastern god, three deities from three different CONTINENTAL areas are actually the same god, even though the game clearly states that they are their own being. What I'm stating, in game terms, is that let's say that the one where Coyote is known by one NAME, then he migrates to the US to the Midwestern tribes, where he's identified under another NAME, then he goes to the West where he's identified under another NAME. Same guy, three different NAMES. The Zeus, Thor and Perun gods are separate because their Pantheons are well known and set in stone.<br /> <br /> The AKA section is <i>exactly as offensive</i> in many cases. Sometimes, like with some of the Egyptians, its just their name translated in other languages. Sometimes, though, it's saying that Mayan and Aztec religions were the same <i>and that is objectively wrong</i>.<br /> <br /> Are you implying that White Wolf and Onyx Path are staffed by racists? Dude, that statement itself is offensive to the people who basically made a game based on dozens of meetings and edits. Give them a break!<br /> <br /> No, it isn't. At all. Saying &quot;Coyote&quot; is a real figure is like saying Judaism, Islam and Christianity are the <i>same</i> religion because they share certain aspects. Coyote never existed. A few dozen different coyote-figures existed, each with their own personality, their own stories and their own unique cultural significance. Reducing them to just &quot;aspects&quot; of one big archetype is bad scholarship and bad practice because <i>that's never done to European figures</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, you haven't read any Discworld. Io does this shit all the freaking time. And thinking in the game terms of Scion, so did Coyote. What you said is like three people claiming that they met a different person all because one person wore three separate hats when encountering him.<br /> <br /> But I'll be the better man and do the agnostic thing here. I can neither confirm or deny whether Coyote was a god with multiple hats nor a conglomeration of different gods, because the evidence supports both theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T14:08:20-07:00","id":161084,"title":"","content":"What? Seriously, I don't understand your response. Terry Pratchett, who writes comedic, satirical fiction that comments on everything and the kitchen sink, he's awesome. But his view on deities and religions isn't a guide for how to do a respectful treatment of historical religions in a fictional context. If anything, he's the opposite of that because nothing in his books is respectful, it's hilariously and purposefully <i>dis</i>respectful because it's satire. Are you saying that his Klatchians should be taken as a guide how to respectfully treat people from the Middle East? I'm fairly sure Mr. Pratchett would disagree. <br /> <br /> I'm not talking about some theoretical in-game Scion figure named Coyote appearing all over North America and using different aliases. I'm saying that in <i>the real, actual, historical world</i>, there was never a single Coyote figure that appeared in dozens of different North American cultures. Each culture with a coyote figure had their <i>own</i> coyote figures, just as each Indo-European culture had their <i>own</i> thunder-god figure. <br /> <br /> Scion needs to be respectful and <i>not</i> fall into the trap of treating marginalized people with the dismissiveness and disrespect that has characterized their treatment for hundreds of years. If it takes on North American, African, South American, Central American, Australian, Polynesian or Asian mythologies, it needs to do so respectfully and with as much attention and detail as is given to the Europeans. Why is that so much to ask? Why is that bad? Why is that hard, or un-fun or boring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T14:35:24-07:00","id":161133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=161049#post161049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because the evidence supports both theories.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://blogs.loc.gov/digitalpreservation/files/2011/09/citation_needed.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T16:40:59-07:00","id":161251,"title":"","content":"Thinking back, I remember a new game mechanic that they're introducing into Scion that makes both my and Telgar's arguments invalid. That new mechanic is Interprio. With this, both Coyote and the coyote-based gods of Native American lore can co-exist because of interpretation. In this case, the coyote-based gods can exist and we can have God X, God Y, and the Aztec name for Coyote in there. And because of mass interpretation by the rest of the World, Coyote himself can exist, whether or not it's racist.<br /> <br /> So Telgar, because of Interprio, we are both right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:20:25-07:00","id":161303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=161251#post161251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking back, I remember a new game mechanic that they're introducing into Scion that makes both my and Telgar's arguments invalid. That new mechanic is Interprio. With this, both Coyote and the coyote-based gods of Native American lore can co-exist because of interpretation. In this case, the coyote-based gods can exist and we can have God X, God Y, and the Aztec name for Coyote in there. And because of mass interpretation by the rest of the World, Coyote himself can exist, whether or not it's racist.<br /> <br /> So Telgar, because of Interprio, we are both right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Citation or this is as silly as you trying to use a manga as an actual source in a research debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:37:05-07:00","id":161319,"title":"","content":"From <a href=\"http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <i><br /> Interpretatio is going to be a thing in 2e. It's something all of the writers are keenly aware of, so we're taking that into account while designing the cosmology. As for PSPs, well. Those have changed a lot already. It's not fair or accurate to describe pantheon membership as a social club with fringe metaphysical benefits...but I wouldn't say it's fair to describe them as permanent mystical bloodlines anymore, either. <b>(Neall)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46292-what-about-gods-who-are-worshipped-in-more-than-one-pantheon?p=48082#post48082\">[12]</a> <br /> <br /> Seriously, you guys. It feels like every thread on Scion <b>ever</b> ends up talking about the damned WWII and Atlantean pantheons. If I were to go through this thread - which was NOT talking about those topics - and excised those posts, I'd shrink it down to at least 50% of its current size.<br /> <br /> I will say this - Scion has a focus, and that's my primary goal. But I'm sorry, I don't understand the gamer mentality that says a line ought never publish options that they themselves will never use. So no, I'm not making any promises not to revisit some of those concepts in the future. Grouse all you like about &quot;wasted word count&quot; or whatever you like, the fact is I intend to make of this system a broad, useful system for the telling of some great stories about heroes whose power derives from ancient legend, using that power to forge their own myths for the next age.<br /> <br /> I guarantee you that I'll put something in these books you hate. I guarantee that because we're going to put a LOT of stuff in them, over the lifespan of this line, because its potential is broad as well as deep. <b>(Joe Carriker)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/14870-scion-2-a-developer-s-note?p=49149#post49149\">[13]</a><br /> <br /> There is a plan for the new edition to more on religion as well as myth. I mean, people believed - and continue to believe! - this stuff. Blood was shed for it. The least we can do is acknowledge the difference between Jupiter Optimus Maximus and the King of Olympus (even if they both wield the three thunderbolts of Tinia, because they're the same dude). When I mentioned interpretatio, I meant it in the more general sense: how other cultures (and pantheons!) look at and interpret gods has an impact, if you consider that the mythology is partially driven by the acts of Gods and Fate. We're also talking about immortal, divine beings who exist over a continuum of thousands of years. People wear a lot of hats in their mayfly lives; how many more so do the gods wear, then? <b>(Neall)</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/55675-separate-roman-pantheon?p=56694#post56694\">[15]</a></i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T18:41:07-07:00","id":161322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=161319#post161319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>snip</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. *goes to investigate*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:47:52-07:00","id":161357,"title":"","content":"There are less general articles in Wikipedia; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interpretatio_graeca\" target=\"_blank\">Interpretatio graeca</a> <i>in which ancient Greek religious concepts and practices, deities, and myths are used to interpret or attempt to understand the mythology and religion of other cultures. It is thus a comparative methodology that looks for equivalencies and shared characteristics. </i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T20:08:51-07:00","id":161369,"title":"","content":"<i><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackalopevegas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. In terms of the game Scion, they ARE the same person. I'm just applying the game mechanics to different personas within the same AREA. There's nothing racist about this. As for your other claim. You are saying that in the game world of Scion, Zeus, Odin/Thor, and this Perun guy are the same god. To clarify, you claim that a Mediterranean god, a Scandanavian god, and a Middle-Eastern god, three deities from three different CONTINENTAL areas are actually the same god, even though the game clearly states that they are their own being. What I'm stating, in game terms, is that let's say that the one where Coyote is known by one NAME, then he migrates to the US to the Midwestern tribes, where he's identified under another NAME, then he goes to the West where he's identified under another NAME. Same guy, three different NAMES. The Zeus, Thor and Perun gods are separate because their Pantheons are well known and set in stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distance between Athens and Oslo is 3374 km. The distance between San Francisco and New York is 4680 km. Zeus and Thor are <b>closer</b> to each other than the Coyote God of the West Coast and the East Coast. Are you honestly trying to say that it's totally okay to treat the latter two as the same person moving around an entire continent, but the first two are totally different people? And what makes you think that the Native American Pantheons are NOT set in stone? And did you just seriously say that Zeus, Thor and Perun should be different because their Pantheons are well-known (which honestly isn't even the case for the last one) and it's totally okay to smash a half-dozen totally different Coyote Gods together because they aren't well known?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T21:44:51-07:00","id":161406,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that Interpretatio isn't going to mean that Zeus, Odin, Indra and Perun are the same person. And if it doesn't mean that, then it won't mean that Sinkalip and Manikaksis are the person. Unless, you know, they decide to be blatantly racist by saying that the cultural divisions across <i>an area greater than continental Europe</i> don't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:04:31-07:00","id":161680,"title":"","content":"Well, as already put;<br /> <i>I guarantee you that I'll put something in these books you hate. I guarantee that because we're going to put a LOT of stuff in them, over the lifespan of this line, because its potential is broad as well as deep. (Joe Carriker) [13]</i><br /> <br /> All things considered I suspect if they tried to make everyone happy there'd never be a game.<br /> <br /> And if the link above (about Greek interpretation) is indeed the route they'll go; <i>It is thus a comparative methodology that looks for equivalencies and shared characteristics.</i> I think it'll be a fun time reading and I'll likely buy every book and pdf.<br /> <br /> <i>Follow your bliss<br /> --Joseph Campbell</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:29:13-07:00","id":161797,"title":"","content":"Whatever Interpretatio is going to mean, I sure hope it doesn't mean something along the lines of all different Coyotes = 1 Coyotes across the length and breadth of a vast continent nor that it means cramming all the Indo-European Thunder Gods into &quot;Spoiled Git of Thunder&quot; . If so, unfortunately Scion:Origins will most likely be doing a faster backpedal than Changeling the Dreaming had to do about autism being the most Banal thing out there and autistic children being the ultimate monsters of the Dreaming or than Shadowrun had to do about HIV being the cause of vampirism and similar conditions amongst the various races after the big change back to magic.<br /> <br /> Those points of view were pretty odious and disrespectful to people who are suffering from pretty serious issues. To people who don't know of them, they are literal jaw-dropping conversation stoppers.<br /> <br /> If it's a replacement for &quot;Fateful Aura&quot; and Interpretatio means that Zeus acts different when he's busy being Jupiter Maximus because he's in the Roman Forum than when he's at in an Etruscan tomb standing under a fresco of Tinia than how he's going to appear atop the ruins of Phideas' lost temple at Olympia, cool. But that is NOT what we're talking about doing here with &quot;Coyote&quot; (who is always the amalgamated whipping boy in these discussions) or with &quot;Raven&quot; or with &quot;Thunderbird&quot; or whatever glommed-over-not-myths are out there.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm feeling backed into a corner here. A corner where I don't want to be. If I wanted a &quot;Coyote&quot; from one pantheon to be the same exact guy as &quot;Coyote&quot; from a different pantheon (essentially &quot;wearing different hats&quot;) for the reason of a good story AND I could find some interesting way in the myths to substantiate that these two guys are similar AND there was some connection historically and/or prehistorically between the two peoples involved, I MIGHT do so, carefully and with due diligence. MIGHT. Only MIGHT. I probably wouldn't have a problem with a Scion being a child of some dad who showed up and said he was &quot;Coyote&quot; and then having the character not be sure which exact &quot;Coyote&quot; he was a Scion of. Some of the different gods that people mash into &quot;Coyote&quot; would have no problem using people's ignorance against them or just to fuck with them for fun.<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't go so far as to say there is only and ever one Coyote because it's more convenient that way. As I started doing the research, even at the Wikipeida level I would realize there was just no way to make that idea work and remain remotely faithful to the underlying mythology. I definitely wouldn't create an overall North American Native American pantheon just to cover a blank area when there are a vast network of dedicated researchers available on this board. Why not access that incredible resource and set up a project where various interested parties start tackling different pantheons and create a more respectful and realistic representation of the wonderful and amazing tapestry of myths and legends that span a continent?<br /> <br /> Personally, I HAVE tried to integrate such mythology into my games when and where I can. I work guided by the ethic, &quot;only as much work as needed and no more&quot; just for time management purposes. But I have created a chunk of a Hopi/Zuni/Pueblo pantheon (as have others before me), I have used a specific Coyote-figure god (Navajo), I have used a specific Raven-figure god (Miwok) a brief brush with Lakota myth. If a player came to me wanting to play a Scion of a Native American pantheon, I would heave a big sigh, buckle down and create the basics. (List of 12 or so gods, the Virtues and the PSP 1-3) and I would like to think I would expect the player to contribute heavily, but I tend to pamper my players.<br /> <br /> I have used the absence of North American pantheons as a plot-element.<br /> <br /> I have also used the concept of &quot;ancient lost pantheons&quot; PRECISELY based on the idea of proto-Pantheons and the players flounder about trying to figure out what happened to them and how they related to the pantheons they know.<br /> <br /> It CAN be interesting stuff to deal with. CAN BE. But carefully and respectfully. Oh so carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-07-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T17:06:25-07:00","id":162041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=161369#post161369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><br /> <br /> The distance between Athens and Oslo is 3374 km. The distance between San Francisco and New York is 4680 km. Zeus and Thor are <b>closer</b> to each other than the Coyote God of the West Coast and the East Coast. Are you honestly trying to say that it's totally okay to treat the latter two as the same person moving around an entire continent, but the first two are totally different people? And what makes you think that the Native American Pantheons are NOT set in stone? And did you just seriously say that Zeus, Thor and Perun should be different because their Pantheons are well-known (which honestly isn't even the case for the last one) and it's totally okay to smash a half-dozen totally different Coyote Gods together because they aren't well known?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So does that mean that gods like Zeus and Thor are going to learn the name of every god who has the coyote as their divine animal, when they visit the US, or are they going to be lazy about it like the majority of humanity when it comes to specific info? Even though the minority, the native tribes, differentiate there coyote gods nicely, it doesn't mean that the rest of the world will do the same. Now if the Native Americans were given the respect the deserve and the mythology was more grounded, then we may have a different story. It's like how theologists and Aesir buffs will recognize the red-headed Thor as he is, and the normal person will recognize Thor as the interpretation from Marvel Comics. That's where Interpretio comes in, and that why we recognize Coyote as Coyote, because Coyote is like Marvel's Thor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T18:36:48-07:00","id":162062,"title":"","content":"Yes. It means EXACTLY that. Because a number, if not most of those gods associated with Coyotes are Legend 12 gods. JUST as powerful and important as Zeus and Thor. And when they are in the US, Zeus and Thor are on THEIR home ground. Where the streams are full of their stream spirits and monsters, the landscape is full of their spirits and monsters, the wind is full of their spirits and monsters, their Terrae Incognitae are all around, the entrances to their Underworlds are nearby, their Axis Mundi are nearby. Which means all their divine allies are closer to hand. So Zeus and Thor can be ignorant assholes and strut all over the place flailing around their big dicks, but they will have their asses handed to them in short order. As they would do if the Native American gods were such complete asshats if they came to visit Europe. Your postulating a level of self-involvement in the pantheons that doesn't even make sense in the context of most of Scion. It definitely makes it less interesting It's like having Zeus be unable to tell Freya and Bast apart because their both just different ways of looking at &quot;Cat Lady&quot;.<br /> <br /> Who cares what the rest of the world does? These different gods are members of different pantheons. As different as the Greek and Norse. Actually potentially as different as the Egyptian and Irish. We have LESS information about the Aztec and Mayan pantheons than we do about MANY of these pantheons. Those pantheons are LESS &quot;grounded&quot;. So, why bother splitting them out? I mean we can syncretize a lot of Mayan gods with Hopi gods. There are Aztec gods who look like Navajo gods. Why not just have Snake Guy, Jaguar, Skull Head and Sun King? Seriously? <br /> <br /> We don't recognize this. You do. And apparently one other person. You are pretty much blatantly saying that it's okay to mistreat the beliefs of &quot;minorities&quot;. In fact, the &quot;pretty much&quot; in that is being generous. You need to cogitate on that. That is the thing that is upsetting people. You've been saying both implicitly and explicitly again and again and each time people are attempting to address what you've said. None of your arguments seem to be convincing to the balance of the people posting here. It's okay for you to do what you want. Really. It is. But when so many people are upset, it's time to take a hard look and figure out why.<br /> <br /> &quot;When all others around you are wrong. Right yourself.&quot; If, Kipling (who is definitely an odd fish to be citing here, but whatever...)<br /> <br /> I know it won't make a difference having said that. It certainly hasn't to date. It just means you'll go find tools to dig even deeper excavations. <br /> <br /> If you are saying you want to do &quot;Scion does the Marvel Pantheons&quot; that's totally cool. There are even websites with all the information you could possibly want that will allow you to do so. Please LABEL your work as such though, so we can join in on commenting on THAT project. This thread isn't about that. It's about filling in a huge blank on the Scion pantheon representation map. It specifically cited to some commonly held (and largely mistaken ) mythic archetypes and was specifically stated to be such. Just like the Dreaming thread was about the same thing for Australia with many of the same issues. I've already tossed up an alternative idea about how to do BOTH. (Though the Australia project would be damn hard...)<br /> <br /> I hope to all the gods of Scion you are wrong about Interpretatio, because that's NOT what the original actual concept of Interpretatio represents AT ALL. And I don't think I'm alone in shuddering to think that Interpretatio is going to mean that Thor is going to change into a Hemsworth whenever he encounters anyone who has seen a Thor movie. THAT would take me right out the running for Scion:Origins. I won't buy a damn thing and I don't think I'm alone. We'll just be seeing Scion:Classic pop up in a few years and, in the meantime, people will be trying to run their own versions of the rules that don't force all of use to use the &quot;make my game stupid&quot; machine as a fundamental mechanic. Besides, that interpretation is definitely reading a lot into what we've been told about the mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T18:55:15-07:00","id":162085,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a Scion &quot;God-Machine.&quot;<br /> And that some may be very unhappy with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:07:55-07:00","id":162188,"title":"","content":"That's pretty much the most un-Sciony idea possible, other than saying the Gods are aliens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:22:53-07:00","id":162192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162041#post162041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does that mean that gods like Zeus and Thor are going to learn the name of every god who has the coyote as their divine animal, when they visit the US, or are they going to be lazy about it like the majority of humanity when it comes to specific info?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, a better question is: Does Thor bother to learn the difference between Sun Wukong and Susano-O? They're both chaotic, smashy Asian Gods. Does he really care which one is which? Or, does Zeus give two craps if he's talking to Shango or Set? Both African Storm Gods. Can Anubis be bothered to tell the difference between Njord and Manannan mac Lir? For an even better comparison, take Tezcatlipoca. When he's wandering around Europe, he just figures that Apollo, Freyr, Baldr and Lugh are the exact same person, right? That makes total sense. He doesn't care about Europe. They're not from his side of the planet. All those guys are just the same &quot;European Sun God&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> It's all the same thing, or at least it should be. If you're saying the Europeans, North Africans, Middle Easterners and Asians all recognize each other's diversity, but refuse to do so for the New Worlders, <i>that is racist as balls. </i>It might make sense <i>in character</i> (and it doesn't, if these Gods want to cooperate or deal with each other at all without murdering everyone), but it makes no sense from an <i>out of game</i> perspective like the one that should be used when writing Pantheons or developing the game.<br /> <br /> So, yes, if Zeus can tell the difference between Morrigan and Hel, then he can tell the difference between Sinkalip and Manikaksis. Because they're his equals, because they're dangerous enemies and valuable allies, because they're <i>all equally different figures</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:47:55-07:00","id":162200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162192#post162192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, a better question is: Does Thor bother to learn the difference between Sun Wukong and Susano-O? They're both chaotic, smashy Asian Gods. Does he really care which one is which? Or, does Zeus give two craps if he's talking to Shango or Set? Both African Storm Gods. Can Anubis be bothered to tell the difference between Njord and Manannan mac Lir? For an even better comparison, take Tezcatlipoca. When he's wandering around Europe, he just figures that Apollo, Freyr, Baldr and Lugh are the exact same person, right? That makes total sense. He doesn't care about Europe. They're not from his side of the planet. All those guys are just the same &quot;European Sun God&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> It's all the same thing, or at least it should be. If you're saying the Europeans, North Africans, Middle Easterners and Asians all recognize each other's diversity, but refuse to do so for the New Worlders, <i>that is racist as balls. </i>It might make sense <i>in character</i> (and it doesn't, if these Gods want to cooperate or deal with each other at all without murdering everyone), but it makes no sense from an <i>out of game</i> perspective like the one that should be used when writing Pantheons or developing the game.<br /> <br /> So, yes, if Zeus can tell the difference between Morrigan and Hel, then he can tell the difference between Sinkalip and Manikaksis. Because they're his equals, because they're dangerous enemies and valuable allies, because they're <i>all equally different figures</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, it's how the gods are interpreted in the general area. The different coyote gods were interpreted as Coyote by the general public because, as a race, humanity always wants to simplify things. Plus, I think another reason why the coyote gods are called Coyote and the raven/crow gods are called Raven is that the mythologies either didn't or couldn't expand beyond the tribes that they originated, again probably because of American opinion during that time, and therefore became a recent thing.<br /> <br /> You might say that the American gods are trying to actualize themselves after having their culture butchered by the Americans and were somehow left behind the more powerful pantheons. Whatever comes out in the end would be considered by the world as a brand new pantheon despite the apparent age of its members. <br /> <br /> Since it's going to be open-world, I hope that all options will be considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T23:22:25-07:00","id":162254,"title":"","content":"What? No. Modern culture doesn't affect the Gods. Thor didn't turn into a blonde superhero. Just because modern Americans don't know who Perun is doesn't mean he isn't a God. Just because a modern American can't tell the difference between Nirrti and Kali doesn't mean they're the same Goddess. <br /> <br /> I honestly <i>cannot understand</i> why you think it's cool for the European Thunder Gods to be different figures, but are dead set on saying every single North American Coyote God is the same.<br /> <br /> The reason all the Coyote Gods are called Coyote by modern Americans? Laziness and racism were keywords of the day back when settlers and colonists were first interacting with and 'learning' about the Native Americans. They translated the names literally (Thor's name, if translated literally, is Thunder, btw) or just <i>ignored</i> the native name and called the Gods by whatever they wanted to because who cares about accuracy? It's the same attitude that lead to photographers of the time documenting famous Native Americans in clothing from <i>entirely different tribes</i> just because it looked &quot;more exotic&quot; for their white audiences.<br /> <br /> Many options should be considered in the new edition of Scion, but <i>casual, blatant racism</i> is not a good option to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T01:56:45-07:00","id":162302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162254#post162254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? No. Modern culture doesn't affect the Gods. Thor didn't turn into a blonde superhero. Just because modern Americans don't know who Perun is doesn't mean he isn't a God. Just because a modern American can't tell the difference between Nirrti and Kali doesn't mean they're the same Goddess.<br /> <br /> I honestly <i>cannot understand</i> why you think it's cool for the European Thunder Gods to be different figures, but are dead set on saying every single North American Coyote God is the same.<br /> <br /> The reason all the Coyote Gods are called Coyote by modern Americans? Laziness and racism were keywords of the day back when settlers and colonists were first interacting with and 'learning' about the Native Americans. They translated the names literally (Thor's name, if translated literally, is Thunder, btw) or just <i>ignored</i> the native name and called the Gods by whatever they wanted to because who cares about accuracy? It's the same attitude that lead to photographers of the time documenting famous Native Americans in clothing from <i>entirely different tribes</i> just because it looked &quot;more exotic&quot; for their white audiences.<br /> <br /> Many options should be considered in the new edition of Scion, but <i>casual, blatant racism</i> is not a good option to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all about PERCEPTION. If the person doesn't know about the red-haired Thor, but remember what they read in Marvel comics, then Thor would look like the comic-book version, at least to them. An example of this would be this one old webcomic that I read once. These two friends went to hell and encountered Lucifer. Since one was a Christian, he saw Lucifer as how Christians view the Devil, monstrous with horns and a tail, the other, who was atheistic, saw Lucifer as he was before his Fall.<br /> <br /> Also, with the racism thing? With mythology? That's pretty thin, considering that the media has portrayed Jesus as a gun-toting crusader, and most of America took it with a grain of salt. Hell, most &quot;modern&quot; tales of the mythologies has the gods doing some stuff that would've never been considered in their original context. And most people are just fine about it. Sure racism is a touchy topic, but basing it on minority opinion is also not a good option to explore, because it undermines the majority. Now describing the differences with races by having blown-out caricatures of them? Now THAT's racist. (See the stories of the Redskins name in baseball and football and the Jim Crow controversy for examples.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T03:00:40-07:00","id":162316,"title":"","content":"Let me put it this way. Would it have been better if the Brothers Grimm, and later on Walt Disney didn't alter the local fairy tales, even if they were being told to children? Was it racist for the Walt Disney company to make a movie about Hercules that didn't involve the blood, tears, characters, and betrayals of the original material. I think what your saying is that changing the original material of the myth demeans it and offends the native believers of said myth. However, things change, especially myths. To deny the importance of different interpretations drains the creativity of the author and denies the curiosity of the source material in question. So when you say Coyote isn't real, you're also saying that people shouldn't have interest in the gods that made up Coyote as well. I think that the show Extra Credits stated somewhere in their Bonfire of the Vanities example is that if someone destroys the idea of God, they destroy God himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:29:15-07:00","id":162408,"title":"","content":"On one hand some want accuracy, on the other they don't want the racism that existed (and still does) in other cultures. And yet, I should think that the gods are expressions of their cultures in the way that they can grow beyond their borders, grow beyond their initial racism. These days, I wouldn't think that Thor is just for those in Scandinavia. (and if it takes a comic-book for his scion to grasp and accept his nature....then whatever it takes) Or to go even further, ancient Egypt's deities, as well as Mesopotamia's aren't likely looking into their respective countries. They all will have to grow to look beyond their racial blinders to survive so that the fight against the &quot;titans&quot; can move forward. I hesitate to say this but...superheroes are a pretty good &quot;gateway&quot; that could lead to the origins of myth/religion. (Red Wolf, Puma, Coyote et al) And I believe that there will be a supplement addressing this...&quot;superheroes as gods&quot; phenomena. So it's not unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><u>Red Wolf</u></b><br /> <img src=\"http://img2.wikia.nocookie.net/__cb20050619053834/marveldatabase/images/d/de/William_Talltrees_%28Earth-616%29_001.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I've always thought that this was a cool look.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Then there's another side of an argument. We have deities that represent a lot of cultural geographic areas of the world.<br /> There's an exclusion of most of North America. And this looks a lot like discrimination of a different kind. Or is it what we're calling &quot;racism&quot; still? (I've heard the derogatory of &quot;negro&quot; thrown in my face a few times that I still find the word &quot;racist&quot; in this thread rather amusing. &quot;Ethnic discrimination&quot; is a more accurate term.)<br /> Perhaps those that don't want Native American deities (of what we see as) are just trying to hide their own &quot;racism.&quot; Maybe their trying to say that they aren't good enough to join the other dozen fleshed out pantheons. <i>&quot;No one takes the time to do it&quot;</i> A common statement. <i>&quot;Oh how about one particular tribe...&quot;</i> Another common statement. Easy to pick and choose I guess out of 3 thousand tribes (?) And yet whenever someone tries to get a consensus...there isn't any. Someone/s always unhappy enough to rip any attempts apart. (You guys must have absolutely loathed Joseph Campbell)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T07:37:04-07:00","id":162412,"title":"","content":"People don't make up gods. Gods are real. They are not born of human belief, though they are somewhat affected by it,<br /> <br /> Welcome to Scion.<br /> <br /> Though there is some very little non-edited textual evidence to back up an idea that human belief can create gods, it's been disowned and discredited.<br /> <br /> Do not confuse Fateful Aura, Fatebound roles or what we know of Interpretatio as undermining this tenant. The mass will of human collective belief over time has an effect on how effective gods can be in certain specific circumstances while not jerking their fundamental nature around. Who wants to play that game? The game of no options.<br /> <br /> This Coyote you speak of as being created by the misguided ignorance of imperialist racists? That's not a thing in this game.<br /> <br /> Telgar is right. I said pretty much the same thing above. It looks like we can keep coming back again and again telling you the same things, but you flail all over the place looking for rationalizations.<br /> <br /> Here it is baldface - the Coyote you want and the pantheon you are proposing and the way you are proposing it are the product of racist misconceptions. Promoting them is promoting the underlying belief structure. Just to be clear, that underlying belief structure is racist. And it isnt' grounded in the rules of this game.<br /> <br /> Sinkalip, Manikaksis, Akba-Atatdia, Attse-Haske, Huehuecoyotl, Istaqa, Mika, etc. etc. ARE NOT the same god. Some of them aren't even vaguely like the mish-mash crap fake Coyote you're pushing. They aren't tricksters, etc. Trying to make them the same gods because you want them to be DOES NOT make it so.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that Scion:Origin is not seriously considering this option. It will bite them in the ass. Being completely insensitive jerks to groups of people that are suffering sometimes has that effect. It certainly has in the past with the gaming community and the White Wolf community specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-08-2014, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T10:25:04-07:00","id":162496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162408#post162408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there's another side of an argument. We have deities that represent a lot of cultural geographic areas of the world.<br /> There's an exclusion of most of North America. And this looks a lot like discrimination of a different kind. Or is it what we're calling &quot;racism&quot; still? (I've heard the derogatory of &quot;negro&quot; thrown in my face a few times that I still find the word &quot;racist&quot; in this thread rather amusing. &quot;Ethnic discrimination&quot; is a more accurate term.)<br /> Perhaps those that don't want Native American deities (of what we see as) are just trying to hide their own &quot;racism.&quot; Maybe their trying to say that they aren't good enough to join the other dozen fleshed out pantheons. <i>&quot;No one takes the time to do it&quot;</i> A common statement. <i>&quot;Oh how about one particular tribe...&quot;</i> Another common statement. Easy to pick and choose I guess out of 3 thousand tribes (?) And yet whenever someone tries to get a consensus...there isn't any. Someone/s always unhappy enough to rip any attempts apart. (You guys must have absolutely loathed Joseph Campbell)</div> </div> </div> </div>I, for one, will state clearly what you clearly want to hear: I would prefer that North America not get any Pantheons in 2e than that they get this amalgamated abomination. I would also prefer that the Deva not be in Scion 2e if we get a repeat of the terribly researched and presented material we got last time. Better the Aztecs not be in the game than they get treated like Hollywood B-movie villains again. If they cannot get the respect they deserve, better they not be in the game at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T13:46:34-07:00","id":162669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162412#post162412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here it is baldface - the Coyote you want and the pantheon you are proposing and the way you are proposing it are the product of racist misconceptions. Promoting them is promoting the underlying belief structure. Just to be clear, that underlying belief structure is racist. And it isnt' grounded in the rules of this game.<br /> <br /> Sinkalip, Manikaksis, Akba-Atatdia, Attse-Haske, Huehuecoyotl, Istaqa, Mika, etc. etc. ARE NOT the same god. Some of them aren't even vaguely like the mish-mash crap fake Coyote you're pushing. They aren't tricksters, etc. Trying to make them the same gods because you want them to be DOES NOT make it so.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that Scion:Origin is not seriously considering this option. It will bite them in the ass. Being completely insensitive jerks to groups of people that are suffering sometimes has that effect. It certainly has in the past with the gaming community and the White Wolf community specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet in every story about Native American culture that I have seen or read, the animal god characters were always termed as Eagle, or Raven, or even yes, Coyote. Hell, Christopher Moore wrote a fiction comedy novel about a guy who met Coyote and gets wrapped up in his problems called, Coyote Blues, including adding tales about the character interspersed with the novel. If there were any versions of the stories where they had the original names for the characters, I haven't found them anywhere, and perhaps so hadn't White Wolf when they made the first edition of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T13:54:52-07:00","id":162678,"title":"","content":"I personally would want to hear Onyx Path's opinion on this, because I believe that with Interpretio, both versions can co-exist. Because all I'm hearing is that because the interpretations were altered by people like Disney or anyone else, these versions should not be considered as parts of the mythos in any way whatsoever. It's basically the call of a pantheon purist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:32:29-07:00","id":162776,"title":"","content":"You know what? I don't care anymore. Forget this whole entire thing. If we are going to be divided on whether the Native American gods are this or that to the point that everyone is calling everyone else, plus the developers at Onyx Path, racist, perhaps it'll be best if North America doesn't have their own pantheon. I'm sorry to everyone for starting this thread. I thought that a Native Amercian pantheon can be represented in the world of Scion, but apparently I was wrong. I'm out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:44:03-07:00","id":162809,"title":"","content":"Jackalope, no one is calling everyone else racist. What is being said is that the common, American pop-culture view of Native Americans <i>is</i> racist. That's not up for debate. It's racist, and has been for hundreds of years. It's slowly getting better, but <i>we still have a Bureau of <b>Indian</b> Affairs</i>. That's the level of understanding we're at right now. We still prefer to call people Native American instead of Cherokee, Lakota or Navajo, because it's easier for us to just lump them all together.<br /> <br /> So I am in no way at all surprised that the Native American pop culture you see on TV, in movies, in comics and in fiction books follows the current cultural trends. That's understandable, but remember that 80 years ago, Little Black Sambos and Mammies were a prominent part of popular culture. Popular culture evolves and it's slowly working towards becoming <i>less</i> racist. Part of that is people agitating for change and saying that what we have right now isn't good enough. Part of evolving popular culture is saying that calling every figure connected with Coyotes &quot;Coyote&quot; isn't right, when they have real names and diverse stories.<br /> <br /> So, yes, Scion 1st Edition had some pretty racist parts because it's the product of a society where racism is still an issue and will continue to <i>be</i> and issue for a good long while. But that doesn't mean the consumers have to support that status quo. It's up to us, as consumers, to say &quot;Hey, if you're going to do this, be respectful. Be better than pop culture. Be progressive.&quot; And hopefully, they listen.<br /> <br /> <br /> No one, not a single person, has said that North America doesn't need its own Pantheon (it has one, the Aztecs, btw). In fact, resoundingly <i>everyone</i> has agreed that it <i>does</i> need one. So does Australia, so does South America, so does Sub-Saharan Africa. These are marginalized groups that could really be shown in a better light. They could introduce people to new things, new ideas and new stories. That's what pop-culture can do, <i>if used well</i>. What <b>has</b> been said is that Scion shouldn't try to make an &quot;African&quot; Pantheon that covers an entire continent. Nor a &quot;South American&quot; Pantheon, nor an &quot;Australian&quot; Pantheon. They should use the exact same approach they took with Europe and Asia: pick a specific, historically existent culture from that region and use <i>their</i> Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Write a Cherokee Pantheon. Write an Inca Pantheon. Write a Maori Pantheon. Write a Zulu Pantheon.<br /> <br /> We're saying <b><i>BE BETTER</i></b>. Because it isn't hard, and it does matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:18:01-07:00","id":163084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162809#post162809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jackalope, no one is calling everyone else racist. What is being said is that the common, American pop-culture view of Native Americans <i>is</i> racist. That's not up for debate. It's racist, and has been for hundreds of years. It's slowly getting better, but <i>we still have a Bureau of <b>Indian</b> Affairs</i>. That's the level of understanding we're at right now. We still prefer to call people Native American instead of Cherokee, Lakota or Navajo, because it's easier for us to just lump them all together.<br /> <br /> So I am in no way at all surprised that the Native American pop culture you see on TV, in movies, in comics and in fiction books follows the current cultural trends. That's understandable, but remember that 80 years ago, Little Black Sambos and Mammies were a prominent part of popular culture. Popular culture evolves and it's slowly working towards becoming <i>less</i> racist. Part of that is people agitating for change and saying that what we have right now isn't good enough. Part of evolving popular culture is saying that calling every figure connected with Coyotes &quot;Coyote&quot; isn't right, when they have real names and diverse stories.<br /> <br /> So, yes, Scion 1st Edition had some pretty racist parts because it's the product of a society where racism is still an issue and will continue to <i>be</i> and issue for a good long while. But that doesn't mean the consumers have to support that status quo. It's up to us, as consumers, to say &quot;Hey, if you're going to do this, be respectful. Be better than pop culture. Be progressive.&quot; And hopefully, they listen.<br /> <br /> <br /> No one, not a single person, has said that North America doesn't need its own Pantheon (it has one, the Aztecs, btw). In fact, resoundingly <i>everyone</i> has agreed that it <i>does</i> need one. So does Australia, so does South America, so does Sub-Saharan Africa. These are marginalized groups that could really be shown in a better light. They could introduce people to new things, new ideas and new stories. That's what pop-culture can do, <i>if used well</i>. What <b>has</b> been said is that Scion shouldn't try to make an &quot;African&quot; Pantheon that covers an entire continent. Nor a &quot;South American&quot; Pantheon, nor an &quot;Australian&quot; Pantheon. They should use the exact same approach they took with Europe and Asia: pick a specific, historically existent culture from that region and use <i>their</i> Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Write a Cherokee Pantheon. Write an Inca Pantheon. Write a Maori Pantheon. Write a Zulu Pantheon.<br /> <br /> We're saying <b><i>BE BETTER</i></b>. Because it isn't hard, and it does matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the information in Scion wasn't considered racist. If it was, then there wouldn't be a following for this game based on principle. Another thing that I realized was that the situation with the Native Americans was kind of like the situation with the African representation for their pantheon. Considering that a lot of people, including you Telgar, wanted the Yourba tribe's Pantheon of Shango and his fellow gods, wouldn't that mean that you and the others are just as racist for excluding the Fon as another part of African representation? How about the other tribes in Africa that had pantheons of their own that they believed just as strongly as the Yoruba are with the Orisha?<br /> <br /> The difficulty of making a representative pantheon for a nation with hundreds of pantheons is who will represent them? Will it be the Salish? The Navajo? The Seminole? Consider that the African pantheon is one of the Top Ten pantheons in Scion. Who made the decision to make the Orisha of the Yoruba tribe the representative pantheon of Africa, and why are they the best pantheon? Are the gods of other pantheons considered &quot;lesser gods&quot; as you and your compatriots talked about with Baron Samedi and others in your fan-made version?<br /> <br /> The only way that the &quot;white&quot; version of the pantheon would be so would be if all the pantheons of North America were decimated by the Titan that resides there. And with the sweeping plague that happened before the pilgrims came (read that from the De-Textbook), and the successful invasions later on, left the tribes, and the pantheons that they worshipped to be mere shadows of themselves. For this to happen, the Titan would have to be a Titan of Hubris, given that the tribal societies of North America seem to somewhat mirror the tribal societies of Africa. If the pantheons were decimated like this, I can see Sukcakega of Ho-Chunk mythology having to ally with Whyayloo of the Salish and Spilyay of the Yakama just for survival. This means that the resulting pantheon that white people know by mind, heart, and soul are basically remnants of their previous pantheons who hated one another, but was forced to work together and co-exist with the other pantheons of the world.<br /> <br /> So, using the same method that chose the Orisha to represent Africa and its interests, which Native American tribal pantheon would you pick to represent North America and why? The answer will forever alter the way players will see America and what it will do with the other pantheons of Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:32:03-07:00","id":163085,"title":"","content":"Scion 1st Ed got written and sold regardless of what anyone else's narrow definition of what they thought racism is.<br /> It. Still. Sold.<br /> Let's face it; It's discrimination to exclude North America. (o...yea...Aztecs whatever...Move past that)<br /> Don't say <i>write a Cherokee pantheon...</i> <b>Show me</b> what such a pantheon looks like instead. (You already have something, don't you?)<br /> But you could probably start crying the blues now. Because it was already said that you're going to hate some of the things being written anyway. But maybe you could show us all how you would do better. I would love to see it. Please.<br /> <br /> Pop culture is a way for gods to survive into mainstream consciousness. Ancient deities likely fare far better with said culture than they do today in their former country that only uses such for tourism. At least the ones we know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 06-08-2014, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:49:43-07:00","id":163099,"title":"","content":"No game can possibly have a Pantheon for every religion that has existed, ever. That's not rational to demand. No one is demanding that. There's no Pantheon for the Baltics, Slavs, Sumerians, Caananites, Welsh, Hittites, Koreans, Vietnamese, or dozens of other groups. That just means Scion doesn't cover everything. That's fine. They can still be implied to exist, there just isn't room for them in the books. Their non-publication does not imply non-existence. The ones that get selected might be the most marketable, the most recognizable, the ones with the easiest to access research material, the ones with the most <i>existing</i> research material or any of a hundred other things. That is <i>not</i> saying the ones that don't get selected are &quot;lesser&quot;. It does not imply they are <i>unworthy</i> of being published. Selecting the Orisha as an African Pantheon does not denigrate the Fon, the Zulu, the Masai or any other African culture. It just says &quot;Hey, here's a popular and fairly easy to research religion from Africa! You can play them!&quot; <br /> <br /> What isn't fine is saying &quot;Well, there's no Pantheon that represents the native people from the US and Canada, why don't we combine all their cultures together and create a mish-mash version of them drawn from pop-culture instead of from history?&quot; And yes, the same applies for Sub-Saharan Africa, Central America, South America and Australia/Oceania.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Loa aren't African, they're an African Diasporatic Religion. They exist <i>only</i> in the New World. They do not represent Africa, the continent, or any group that lives there. They represent groups of people living in and around the Caribbean. They come from a real, existing religion. They might not be handled super well, but they're given the same respect as the other Pantheons. Why I, and many others, prefer using the Orisha to the Loa is because we prefer to keep Monotheism and modern syncretism out of Scion. That's a <i>whole</i> other debate. It isn't because the Loa somehow represent &quot;all of Africa&quot;. They don't represent any part of Africa. And it <i>does not</i> make the Loa a &quot;lesser&quot; Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> The worship of the Greek Gods was devastated by the spread of Christianity. So was the worship of the Aesir. And the Tuatha de Danann. And the Slavic Gods. And the Baltic Gods. And the Basque Gods. And the Celtic Gods of Gaul were devastated even earlier by the spread of the Roman Empire. Yet, no one suggests that all those Pantheons be torn to shreds and forced to conglomerate into a combined Pantheon-Council of Europe. <i><b>Why should we treat the American, Australian, Oceanic and African groups differently</b></i>?<br /> <br /> If you want to know which Pantheon I'd choose from each area, it's the Cherokee (North America), the Aztecs (Central America), the Inca (South America), the Orisha (SubSaharan Africa), and the Maori (Australia-Oceania). However if someone else wanted the Navajo, the Maya, the Guarani, the Zulu Gods and one of the Australian cultures, that'd be fine too. Neither choice is wrong, neither choice implies that the ones left out are less important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T21:02:39-07:00","id":163109,"title":"","content":"How is anyone here operating on a narrow definition of racism, Shadowflame? Please, explain.<br /> <br /> Scion selling doesn't mean it hasn't got racist baggage. People still read HP Lovecraft and Robert Howard, the work of whom is <i>profoundly</i> racist. Scion at least didn't set <i>out</i> to be racist. They fell into the traps that make it so, so easy to ignore marginalized groups and continue a centuries long tradition of ignorance and laziness. Does that make the writers bad people? No. They were working with what they're familiar with. That's to be expected. However, when it's pointed out and brought up that their work could be vastly improved, it's important for them to work on that. <br /> <br /> If you want to see a Cherokee Pantheon, a poster named Lesignon has written one, though I don't know if he posted it for public consumption. Someone else was working on an Iroquois Pantheon. The folks at GothamByNight wrote an Inuit Pantheon, and an Inca Pantheon (for South America). I think GriffinGuy24 occasionally pokes at the idea of writing a Guarani Pantheon. The fan community <i>is</i> writing these Pantheons. Am I, personally, doing that? No, because my area of expertise lays in the Ancient Middle East, since that's what I studied in college.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T04:18:50-07:00","id":163381,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I'm thinking this the wrong way. Tonight, when I was thinking about this subject, my mind drifted to perhaps the most recognized deity in Native American mythology: Kokopelli.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokopelli\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/Kokopelli_kachina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokopelli\" target=\"_blank\"> Kokopelli - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokopelli\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kokopelli </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This guy is everywhere where people try to capture that Western feel of Americana. Plus since he's a god of both the Hopi and the Zuni, he has a step up on the pantheons who don't have joint custody on a god. So instead of my initial idea, perhaps a pantheon can be made revolving around Kokopelli and the pantheons of the Hopi and Zuni.<br /> <br /> It might work if North America needs a representative, much like the Orisha will be for sub-Saharan Africa. If anything, this is the Native American pantheon that I will pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T06:03:34-07:00","id":163488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=163381#post163381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So instead of my initial idea, perhaps a pantheon can be made revolving around Kokopelli and the pantheons of the Hopi and Zuni.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can absolutely make a Hopi pantheon AND a Zuni pantheon! We can figure out where Kokopelli goes along the way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:36:34-07:00","id":163680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162809#post162809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jackalope, no one is calling everyone else racist. What is being said is that the common, American pop-culture view of Native Americans <i>is</i> racist. That's not up for debate. It's racist, and has been for hundreds of years. It's slowly getting better, but <i>we still have a Bureau of <b>Indian</b> Affairs</i>. That's the level of understanding we're at right now. We still prefer to call people Native American instead of Cherokee, Lakota or Navajo, because it's easier for us to just lump them all together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just an FYI on the Bureau of Indian Affairs. The reason that it is still called that is because all of the treaties with the tribes use the word &quot;Indian&quot;. They don't use &quot;Native American&quot;. They don't categorically use the tribal name. (Which is a dicey affair in it's own right as most tribal names used were those used by the next people over since Europeans encountered new tribes one at a time and usually asked the people they were talking to what to call of the next people they would met . And the people they were talking to didn't always have a fond view of their neighbors, vide &quot;Sioux&quot; meaning &quot;those lowdown dirty snakes&quot; for the Lakota or were very practical, e.g. speaking to a member of the Illini Confederacy, &quot;What are the people up this river called? Oh, they're the Missouri - meaning &quot;people with the big canoes&quot;, but they actually call themselves the Chiwere.)<br /> <br /> That's REALLY important. If you can't be identified with the people mentioned in the treaty, it doesn't have to apply to you. For understandable reasons, even more treaties get abrogated is not going to be a good thing for most tribes.<br /> <br /> I worked extensively with the leadership of several tribes on behalf of the government. Virtually ALL of them wanted to be called &quot;Indians&quot;. They didn't want to risk losing what little they had and would do anything to protect their status.<br /> <br /> Which is a sad commentary in its own right. But those treaties are VERY VERY VERY important to the tribes. So there isn't going to be much of a change in nomenclature. The Senate is not going to revisit each and every treaty made and change the terminology. And I'm sure the people involved don't want that to happen. The Senate would undoubtedly change other things and it has even more of an upper hand than it did when the treaties were made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-09-2014, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:39:45-07:00","id":163684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=162809#post162809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">J<br /> <br /> So I am in no way at all surprised that the Native American pop culture you see on TV, in movies, in comics and in fiction books follows the current cultural trends. That's understandable, but remember that 80 years ago, Little Black Sambos and Mammies were a prominent part of popular culture. Popular culture evolves and it's slowly working towards becoming <i>less</i> racist. Part of that is people agitating for change and saying that what we have right now isn't good enough. Part of evolving popular culture is saying that calling every figure connected with Coyotes &quot;Coyote&quot; isn't right, when they have real names and diverse stories.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>We still have Uncle Ben rice and Aunt Jemima syrup. Those are both depictions of &quot;happy slaves.&quot; <br /> <br /> Racism is pervasive in ways that people can't even easily perceive. It's all over in nooks and crannies. Not just the aspects that get a lot of press, like Ms. Mankiller's crusade against the Redskins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:43:26-07:00","id":164196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=163488#post163488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can absolutely make a Hopi pantheon AND a Zuni pantheon! We can figure out where Kokopelli goes along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, I think it would be more prudent to make Kokopelli's pantheon Hopi, mainly for the reason that the tribe is more recognizable, thanks to the cliff dwellings that they are credited for. <br /> <br /> So, who are the other gods in the Hopi Pantheon?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:38:59-07:00","id":164240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi_mythology\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Arizona%2C_hopi%2C_otre_con_testa_di_katsina%2C_1890.jpg/1280px-Arizona%2C_hopi%2C_otre_con_testa_di_katsina%2C_1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi_mythology\" target=\"_blank\"> Hopi mythology - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi_mythology\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi_mythology </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:27:53-07:00","id":164306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=163109#post163109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is anyone here operating on a narrow definition of racism, Shadowflame? Please, explain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because what you're calling it isn't racism.<br /> Since it's a bit long; <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethnocentrism\" target=\"_blank\">Ethnocentrism</a><br /> <i>Ethnocentrism is judging another culture solely by the values and standards of one's own culture. Ethnocentric individuals judge other groups relative to their own ethnic group or culture, especially with concern for language, behavior, customs, and religion. These ethnic distinctions and subdivisions serve to define each ethnicity's unique cultural identity.</i><br /> <a href=\"http://www.britannica.com/blackhistory/article-234663\" target=\"_blank\">The difference between racism and ethnocentrism</a><br /> <i>Although they are easily and often confused, race and racism must be distinguished from ethnicity and ethnocentrism. While extreme ethnocentrism may take the same offensive form and may have the same dire consequences as extreme racism, there are significant differences between the two concepts. Ethnicity, which relates to culturally contingent features, characterizes all human groups. It refers to a sense of identity and membership in a group that shares common language, cultural traits (values, beliefs, religion, food habits, customs, etc.), and a sense of a common history. All humans are members of some cultural (ethnic) group, sometimes more than one. Most such groups feel\u2014to varying degrees of intensity\u2014that their way of life, their foods, dress, habits, beliefs, values, and so forth, are superior to those of other groups.<br /> The most significant quality of ethnicity is the fact that it is unrelated to biology and can be flexible and transformable. People everywhere can change or enhance their ethnicity by learning about or assimilating into another culture. American society well illustrates these facts, consisting as it does of groups of people from hundreds of different world cultures who have acquired some aspects of American culture and now participate in a common sense of ethnic identity with other Americans.<br /> Ethnic identity is acquired, and ethnic features are learned forms of behaviour. Race, on the other hand, is a form of identity that is perceived as innate and unalterable. Ethnicity may be transient and even superficial. Race is thought to be profound and grounded in biological realities. Ethnocentrism is based in a belief in the superiority of one's own culture over others, and it too may be transient and superficial. Racism is the belief in and promotion of the racial worldview described above. Ethnocentrism holds skin colour and other physical features to be irrelevant as long as one is a member of the same culture, or becomes so. The racial worldview holds that, regardless of behaviour or cultural similarities, a member of an inferior race (who is usually perceived to be so by means of physical features) can never be accepted. Race is an invented, fictional form of identity; ethnicity is based on the reality of cultural similarities and differences and the interests that they represent. That race is a social invention can be demonstrated by an examination of the history of the idea of race as experienced in the English colonies.</i><br /> Long-ish article. But I have <b>never</b> read where both Ethnicity and Race were actually one and the same.(Though I've heard such claims often enough)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> From the wiki article on the Hopi:<br /> <i>he Hopi maintain a complex religious and mythological tradition stretching back over centuries. However, it is difficult to definitively state what all Hopis as a group believe. Like the oral traditions of many other societies, Hopi mythology is not always told consistently and each Hopi mesa, or even each village, may have its own version of a particular story. But, &quot;in essence the variants of the Hopi myth bear marked similarity to one another.&quot;</i><br /> ---------------<br /> <br /> hmmm...<br /> <br /> At any rate, I find the older Native beliefs (what can be found) far more interesting.<br /> For example; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horned_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">the Horned Serpent</a> (aka the great Serpent)<br /> <i> <b>Other known names</b><br /><br /><ul><li><b>Misi-kinepikw</b> (&quot;great snake&quot;)\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cree_language\" target=\"_blank\">Cree</a></li> <li><b>Msi-kinepikwa</b> (&quot;great snake&quot;)\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shawnee_language\" target=\"_blank\">Shawnee</a></li> <li><b>Misi-ginebig</b> (&quot;great snake&quot;)\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oji-Cree_language\" target=\"_blank\">Oji-Cree</a></li> <li><b>Mishi-ginebig</b> (&quot;great snake&quot;)\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ojibwe_language\" target=\"_blank\">Ojibwe</a></li> <li><b>Pita-skog</b> (&quot;great snake&quot;)\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Abnaki_language\" target=\"_blank\">Abenaki</a></li> <li><b>Sinti lapitta</b>\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Choctaw_language\" target=\"_blank\">Choctaw</a></li> <li><b>Unktehi</b> or <b>Unktehila</b>\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dakota_language\" target=\"_blank\">Dakota</a></li> <li><b>Olobit</b>\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natchez_language\" target=\"_blank\">Natchez</a></li> <li><b>Uktena</b>\u2014<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherokee\" target=\"_blank\">aniyunwiya</a></li> </ul></i><br /> Fascinating how far this belief went. Almost as far as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunderbird_%28mythology%29\" target=\"_blank\">Thunderbird</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Underwater_panther\" target=\"_blank\">Underwater panther</a> it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T11:16:45-07:00","id":164962,"title":"","content":"The Horned Serpent and Great Snake appear all across Eurasia as well. It's hardly unique to North America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:16:08-07:00","id":165148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=164962#post164962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Horned Serpent and Great Snake appear all across Eurasia as well. It's hardly unique to North America.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> West Africa has various world snakes as well, like Da of the Fon, who is also connected to rainbows. It's a pretty universal myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:39:56-07:00","id":165210,"title":"","content":"you all have no idea how happy it makes me to have a Scion-based debate to watch that isn't about the abrahamic religions. seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:04:08-07:00","id":165246,"title":"","content":"With regard to Kokopelli, I think it might make sense for some gods to socialize with different pantheons without necessarily being a member of any one of them. As another example, Guanyin/Avalokitasvara Bodhisattva would presumably be on good terms with the Amatsukami, the Celestial Bureaucracy, the Hindu pantheon, and various Southeast Asian deities to boot. Of course, with gregarious deities you have the problem of not necessarily knowing what pantheon-specific purview to give them and their scions, but that seems like a fairly small issue to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T19:37:03-07:00","id":165534,"title":"","content":"Hmm...Lets see; We've got the horned serpent, Thunderbird, underwater panther, lets go further:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cougar#In_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">Cougar</a></b><i><br /> In North America, mythological descriptions of the cougar have appeared in the stories of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoc%C4%85k_language\" target=\"_blank\">Hoc\u0105k language</a> (&quot;Ho-Chunk&quot; or &quot;Winnebago&quot;) of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisconsin\" target=\"_blank\">Wisconsin</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illinois\" target=\"_blank\">Illinois</a> and the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheyenne\" target=\"_blank\">Cheyenne</a>, amongst others. To the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apache\" target=\"_blank\">Apache</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walapai\" target=\"_blank\">Walapai</a> of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arizona\" target=\"_blank\">Arizona</a>, the wail of the cougar was a harbinger of death.The Algonquins and Ojibwe believe that the cougar lived in the underworld and was wicked, whereas it was a sacred animal among the Cherokee.</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolves_in_folklore,_religion_and_mythology#Arctic_and_North_America\" target=\"_blank\">Wolves</a></b><i><br /> Some tribes, such as the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nunamiut\" target=\"_blank\">Nunamiut</a> of northern and northwestern <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska\" target=\"_blank\">Alaska</a> and the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naskapi\" target=\"_blank\">Naskapi</a> of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labrador\" target=\"_blank\">Labrador</a> respected the wolf's hunting skill and tried to emulate the wolf in order to hunt successfully. Others see the wolf as a guide. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska_Native\" target=\"_blank\">Tanaina</a> of Alaska believed that wolves were once men, and viewed them as brothers.<br /> In the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_direction\" target=\"_blank\">Cardinal directions</a> of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plains_Indians\" target=\"_blank\">Plains Indians</a>, the wolf represented the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West\" target=\"_blank\">west</a>, while for the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pawnee_people\" target=\"_blank\">Pawnee</a>, it represented the southeast.<br /> The Netsilik Inuit and Takanaluk-arnaluk believed that the sea-woman Nuliayuk's home was guarded by wolves. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navajo_people\" target=\"_blank\">Navajo people</a> feared witches in wolves' clothing called &quot;yee naaldlooshii&quot;, literally &quot;with it, he goes on all fours&quot;. Wolf in Navajo is m\u0105\u02bciitsoh- lit. &quot;large coyote&quot;. Wolves were feared by the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsilhqot%27in\" target=\"_blank\">Tsilhqot'in</a>, who believed that contact with wolves would result in nervous illness or death.</i><br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_depictions_of_spiders#In_folklore_and_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">Spider</a></b><i><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_American_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">North American cultures</a> have traditionally depicted spiders. The Native American <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lakota_people\" target=\"_blank\">Lakota people</a>'s oral tradition also includes a spider-trickster figure, which is <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iktomi\" target=\"_blank\">known by several names</a>. The spider is also present as the deity <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iktomi\" target=\"_blank\">Iktomi</a>, which is occasionally depicted in this form.In Native American mythology, the spider is also seen in the legend about the birth of the constellation Ursa Major. The constellation was seen as seven men transformed into stars and climbing to paradise by unrolling a spider's web. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi_people\" target=\"_blank\">Hopi</a> have the creation myth of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider_Grandmother\" target=\"_blank\">Spider Grandmother</a>. Spider Grandmother also plays an important role in the creation mythology of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navajo_Nation\" target=\"_blank\">Navajo</a>, and there are stories relating to Spider Woman in the heritage of many <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prehistoric_Southwestern_Cultural_Divisions\" target=\"_blank\">Southwestern native cultures</a> as a powerful helper and teacher</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl#The_Americas\" target=\"_blank\">Owls</a></b><i><br /> In the culture of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uto-Aztecan_languages\" target=\"_blank\">Uto-Aztec</a> tribe, the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hopi\" target=\"_blank\">Hopi</a>, taboos surround owls, which are associated with sorcery and other evils. The belief that owls are messengers and harbingers of the dark powers is also found among the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ho-Chunk\" target=\"_blank\">Ho\u010d\u0105gara</a> (Winnebago) of Wisconsin. When in earlier days the Ho\u010d\u0105gara committed the sin of killing enemies while they were within the sanctuary of the chief's lodge, an owl appeared and spoke to them in the voice of a human, saying, &quot;From now on the Ho\u010d\u0105gara will have no luck.&quot; This marked the beginning of the decline of their tribe. An owl appeared to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glory_of_the_Morning\" target=\"_blank\">Glory of the Morning</a>, the only female chief of the Ho\u010d\u0105k nation, and uttered her name. Soon afterwards she died<sup>.</sup> People often allude to the reputation of owls as bearers of supernatural danger when they tell misbehaving children, &quot;the owls will get you.&quot; Also, in the native Cherokee culture, as well as many other Native American cultures, owls are a very bad omen. It is said that if you are outside in the broad day light and an owl flies over your head a family member or loved one would die within the coming week.</i><br /> (Hmf..I've always liked owls)<br /> <br /> So...in line with the OP, we have some nice additions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T20:19:31-07:00","id":165556,"title":"","content":"I honestly can't tell if you're trying to provide information about a Hopi/Zuni Pantheon (they're similar enough culturally and linguistically that I'd find it <i>very</i> challenging to write a Pantheon for each), or if you're back to creating a Pantheon out of generic archetypes taken from all across the continental USA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T13:10:46-07:00","id":166191,"title":"","content":"It doesn't look like a Hopi/Zuni/Pueblo pantheon.<br /> <br /> (Puts on new bifocals)<br /> <br /> Nope. Still doesn't.<br /> <br /> I think it's the same thing over again. With some non-determinative scholarship attached....<br /> <br /> Cougar &gt;&gt;&gt; nothing I can find<br /> Wolf&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; nothing I can find<br /> Spider&gt;&gt;&gt; Hahti Wuhti, I think<br /> Owl&gt;&gt;&gt;. nothing I can find.<br /> <br /> pretty thin on the ground for finding optimal Hopi-ish deities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-11-2014, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:43:11-07:00","id":166238,"title":"","content":"That's because you both didn't read the full post, Allow me: <i>&quot;So...in line with the OP, we have some nice additions&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:59:23-07:00","id":166437,"title":"","content":"Call it &quot;Animal Pantheon&quot; You can bring in the ENTIRE world that way. Including Australia. Fill up all the empty bits with one pantheon. <br /> <br /> Don't bury your lead at the very end and expect people to read in any emphasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:14:20-07:00","id":166447,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* why bother posting vitriol in a thread asking for positive contributions...? Or should the OP be reposted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T20:31:27-07:00","id":166493,"title":"","content":"Ummmm.... vitriol? Look up the definition of that word, please. Considering the emotional flattening character of email, you need A LOT more to be throwing around terms like that when you read into some very very simple verbage. <br /> <br /> I was dead serious. If you're going to do this thing. Do it all the way. An &quot;Animal Spirit' &quot;Animist&quot; &quot;Totemist&quot; Pantheon seems like what's been underlying everything you've been looking at so far. It covers your perception of North American Native American religions, but it would also suck in Australian Aboriginal mythology (in one way of looking at things), works for certain values of viewing African pantheons, Papua New Guinea, Siberia, Anu.... it seems like you are really throwing down limits on what you're trying for. If you are going to simplify to seek some kind of underlying basic structure and then use that structure raw. Then, in previously used words, &quot;throw different hats&quot; on it. <br /> <br /> It worked for Campbell. It worked for Levi Strauss. I don't like it and probably won't use it. But things I didn't think I would like have wow-ed me before. Stranger things have happened. If there is something I like, I'll steal it without compunction or mercy. <br /> <br /> Writing advice is writing advice. You buried your lead. It's a bad idea. If you are trying to get things back on what you consider the topic, say it up front and clearly. I can see why Telgar was confused and so was I. Topics were hopped then the segue was put in at the end. How were we to know that the conversation had changed from Hopi &amp; Zuni, Hopi vs. Zuni, Kokopelli? It looked like some discussion was being laid down about a discrete Native American cultural pantheon. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T23:30:15-07:00","id":166671,"title":"","content":"Yep, that's what I initially set out to try to do when I started the thread. In the previous edition, they seemed to have a pantheon for each different area of the World. The Greeks were part of Mediterranean Europe, the Aesir was Northern or Scandinavian Europe (with the Tuatha representing the island of Ireland), The Egyptians were Saharan Africa and the Loa were sub-Saharan Africa, with a touch of America and Caribbean. The Yazata and the Deva had their own spot within the Middle East, and the Bureaucracy and the Amatsukami ruling the Asian continent with China and Japan respectively. The Aztecs take most of Latin America and the entirety of South America. The only two places that were untouched, since the Atlanteans once ruled what is now Antarctica, are Australia, and North America, (even though there was a slight hint of a pantheon there with the Yankee Pantheon, I don't think that anyone would want to use it for reasons.)<br /> <br /> Now that Scion is more open, I thought that a respectful pantheon dealing with the Totemic spirits of Native American mythology. The difficulty that is faced here was the fact that I barely knew anything about the different pantheons in general (given that the info the general population knew was &quot;flawed&quot;), and yet I also wanted to use the familiar for those players who aren't Native American mythophiles like some of the more educated posters here on this forum. Face it. If you say the name of the fox god Whyoloo (?), the normal player would at first wonder if it's the name of a character from My Little Pony or a new type of Pokemon. That's why, with the outpouring of authenticity from the posters, I decided to use Kokopelli as a base for a possible pantheon. Just like Baron Samedi is one of the most recognized Loa by the general public, most people in America are familiar with the name and form of Kokopelli, due to his form being placed on souvenir pottery, shirts and mugs to represent anything Western.<br /> <br /> If they are willing to make a full-blown book on Native American pantheons, I wonder how many of the pantheons can fit into the book without it seemingly overstuffed? I mean, they would have to need room for the Pantheon Purview, the Overworld and Underworld, Axis Mundi, and the Titan (if there's just one) that is currently plaguing the gods of North America. Given how many tribes are represented, I'm worried that certain ones will be cut from the roster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T00:36:55-07:00","id":166697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=166671#post166671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the previous edition, they seemed to have a pantheon for each different area of the World. The Greeks were part of Mediterranean Europe, the Aesir was Northern or Scandinavian Europe (with the Tuatha representing the island of Ireland), The Egyptians were Saharan Africa and the Loa were sub-Saharan Africa, with a touch of America and Caribbean. The Yazata and the Deva had their own spot within the Middle East, and the Bureaucracy and the Amatsukami ruling the Asian continent with China and Japan respectively. The Aztecs take most of Latin America and the entirety of South America.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonononono, see, you've got it backwards. They picked popular and well-known <i>cultures</i>, most of whom are native to Europe because that's where most of the audience is from. Those aren't areas being chosen, those are cultures. None of the Pantheons in Scion are a conglomeration of different cultures mashed together to cover a &quot;region&quot;. The AKA's do that a bit (saying, for example, that the Aztecs and Mayans had the same religion, when they didn't) but not anything like saying all of North American needs to be gathered up into a single Pantheon. Instead it's more like saying &quot;Hey, we can only do 10 of these guys, so here's some of the most well-known!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> If you want to make a Hopi Pantheon using Kokopeli as the &quot;big name&quot; there, that's cool. I'd be happy to help, but just so you know, Pantheon-writing takes a lot of research. It's not a few hours, it's a <i>lot</i> of work. When the folks from GBN wrote theirs, it was months of work. Even the fast-n-dirty sub-Pantheons that I wrote for the Etruscans and Vanir took days of tracking down references and reading what I could of the very, very few primary sources. Checking art, statues, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:42:15-07:00","id":166997,"title":"","content":"I agree with Telgar and then go far the opposite way. The gods and pantheons in Scion were picked for their familiarity and coolness factor. That's only intelligent marketing. Obscurity to the market doesn't mean trying to make pseudo-pantheons that look like the agglutination from transfusions of mismatched blood types.<br /> <br /> I was saying that your topic and they way in which you seem to want to handle it has even LARGER implications than trying to shoehorn vagueness and, frankly, the perpetuation of odious stereotyping. You can go all Campbell on this and create a pantheon of more fundamental abstractions that apply to some degree across the world. The Hopi have a bear god. The Ainu have a bear god. The Inuit have a bear god. Hell, the Cro Magnons look like THEY had a bear god. Hence, BEAR. Not Native American mishmash Bear, but BEAR. The BEAR of everywhere, everyone, everywhen. <br /> <br /> You could do the same thing with the Indo-European and analogues. Thunder Boy, God King (not always the same dude... Zeus confuses the issue), Sun, Moon, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:47:44-07:00","id":167002,"title":"","content":"Huh. Okay, I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T18:44:12-07:00","id":171274,"title":"","content":"Shadowflame, what would the general feel of the pantheon be? I might've missed that in a previous post? If you're doing this for Scion 1st edition, do you have any ideas for a psp? I can easily imagine the psp being focused on both the bond of the totem animal as well as the 'spirit world' or something akin to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T07:11:27-07:00","id":171627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=171274#post171274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowflame, what would the general feel of the pantheon be? I might've missed that in a previous post? If you're doing this for Scion 1st edition, do you have any ideas for a psp? I can easily imagine the psp being focused on both the bond of the totem animal as well as the 'spirit world' or something akin to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;General feel...&quot; Hmm..not something &quot;furry.&quot;<br /> <br /> I was thinking something that had to look more than a couple of of purviews (notable Animal, Earth, with a bit of old Mage the Ascension thrown in, such as Spirit and Life spheres)<br /> I would have focused on the majors at first since they're the ones most commonly known; mammal, bird, reptile, aquatic, the creepy-crawlies (insects and spiders etc,) and yes, even plants.<br /> The character in question wouldn't be limited to one particular animal unless that's how a person would play it that way. I myself would create a concept or create a situation that would lead the hero to that concept that would give a variety of &quot;totems.&quot; (Eg, vines, snakes, ivy, Things that are similar in the tone)<br /> Or create that singular animal, but focus on it's &quot;world.&quot; It's one thing for a human to revere the bison for all that it gives to support that human's life, but what would a moutain lion or wolf revere if it held a human consciousness? As you realize geography is also very much in play. Which also leads to &quot;night&quot; and &quot;day&quot; added to the concept, which are so much more alive to this character than simple &quot;darkness&quot; and &quot;sun.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now what's the goal? Strengthening the spiritual ties of life in all forms to those of mankind. (Yeah, that needs work)<br /> <br /> As for a psp...Something in the real world Gaian Hyposthesis, in that the world is a living breathing superorganism, and getting to know this organism might be a part of it.<br /> Our character/hero in question would invariably become stronger/ more powerful as s/he grows, eventually becoming a mythical leader (or avatar) in a shapeshifted form. To become as the worlf &quot;Fenris&quot; that was presented in the book Ragnarok and having all the abilities therein. Or &quot;Cerberus.&quot; There's an endless list of animals associated with the gods. I would posit for a game (and for the sake of this thread), that the gods be reminded &quot;why that is&quot; and that such an a link between god and animal, should be emulated in some way with human and animal.<br /> <br /> I concede that the whole idea might be a bit of a challenge to fit in with Scion unless god-level animals or &quot;concepts&quot; are presented. But they're there already in mythology and religions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T08:17:58-07:00","id":171658,"title":"","content":"As for a PSP, something like this maybe<br /> <br /> <b>Hero Quirk:</b> The Hero becomes aware if there's anything troubling the spirit world in an area (such as pollution, disrespectful treatment etc.)<br /> \u25cf Totem Protection: Animals of the chosen totem never attack the scion unless controlled by someone of greater legend than the scion.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Spirit Imbual: By sacrificing one of his totem animals, the Scion gain a few point of legend.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Spirit Step: The Scion can step through the spirit world with a single step and thus ignoring protections laid by those of lesser legend. Equal legend = resistance<br /> <b>Demigod Quirk:</b> The Scion can see spirits and speak to them<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Spirit Form: The Scion takes on the form of a spirit and becomes more difficult to hurt. His soak increases by his legend and his DV increases by his highest dot in the PSP<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Send Away: By displacing an object (or person) into the spirit world, the object becomes unreachable by normal means. Those of greater or equal legend can attempt to pull it back<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf Spirit Breath: The scion becomes one with the living world and gains a bonus to his rolls. This bonus is more powerful outside of civilization<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf Speak to the Ancestors: The Scion can imbue himself with the spirit of the world, turninga number of dice into auto-successes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T23:29:52-07:00","id":181711,"title":"","content":"I know when I was working on a Native American Pantheon for the Scion game I was running, I got around a lot of the cultural stickiness, by explaining that the Pantheon was an Alliance of the remaing active Native Gods. So while it had Gods worshiped by different Tribes in it, there was a reason for it.<br /> <br /> I never had a chance to work up a PSP, as the game ended before I could really use the Pantheon..<br /> <br /> I also had an American Pantheon that was composed entirely of Gods born into other Pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:46:14-07:00","id":181809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=181711#post181711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know when I was working on a Native American Pantheon for the Scion game I was running, I got around a lot of the cultural stickiness, by explaining that the Pantheon was an Alliance of the remaing active Native Gods. So while it had Gods worshiped by different Tribes in it, there was a reason for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much the same as I've done with my African Pantheon. It consists of those gods my group know about from different media (Anansi being one of them).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=181711#post181711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also had an American Pantheon that was composed entirely of Gods born into other Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically how I work with the American Pantheon for my games. The current Pantheon of Uncle Sam and the bunch are all ascended Scions of the gods from other Pantheons. They formed their own pantheon because of limited interest in their home pantheons to protect and expand America.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T16:39:34-07:00","id":182362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=181809#post181809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much the same as I've done with my African Pantheon. It consists of those gods my group know about from different media (Anansi being one of them).</div> </div> </div> </div>This was exactly what I did.. my reasoning being, they were the only Gods still active.. Coyote, Raven, Thunderbird, a few.. and I had a werewolf who was becoming the new Wolf, God of War others..<br /> <br /> In my game.. the Native Pantheon had been living under the &quot;protection&quot; of the American Gods..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:27:39-07:00","id":182974,"title":"","content":"While that sort of hodgepodge pantheon is fine in somebody's private game, I don't think it would be the best move for a company like Onyx Path, because it's a few short steps from there to accusations of racism and stereotyping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:42:49-07:00","id":182980,"title":"","content":"...at least here it seems to be...<br /> <br /> Uktena, Croatan, Wendigo...It's amazing that Werewolf the Apocalypse ever got written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:12:22-07:00","id":183094,"title":"","content":"Werewolf <i>was</i> pretty racist. That was a concern that got raised, but the 90s were a bit different. There was a lot of that &quot;everyone's better than white folks&quot; stuff floating around. All the Native Americans were inherently more peaceful, pure and respectful of the Land somehow. All the Asians were magically better at anything, Katanas were the best things ever... and in case you're not aware, Whitewolf is no stranger to brushes with racism. Gypsies, after all, was published. Kindred of East is often under fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T16:17:30-07:00","id":183312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=182980#post182980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...at least here it seems to be...<br /> <br /> Uktena, Croatan, Wendigo...It's amazing that Werewolf the Apocalypse ever got written.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159548#post159548\">Again</a>, <i>Werewolves aren't real.</i> Making up stuff about fictional cultures isn't comparable to making up stuff about real cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T19:10:26-07:00","id":183428,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=183312#post183312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=159548#post159548\">Again</a>, <i>Werewolves aren't real.</i> Making up stuff about fictional cultures isn't comparable to making up stuff about real cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, uktena, croatan..wendigo you ignored because of the context was werewolves? Shit. How about we make them into, o I don't know..how about spirits? Since they aren't real either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T20:02:15-07:00","id":183443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=183428#post183428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, uktena, croatan..wendigo you ignored because of the context was werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally ignore them because the context is that of a fictional subculture, one set apart and largely hidden from the actual real world Amerind cultures. The fictional beliefs of the fictional Uktena tribe only really reflect the beliefs of the fictional Uktena tribe, even if they draw <i>inspiration </i>from real world American Indian cultures. Even then, there are limits.<br /> <br /> Conversely, you're deliberately falsifying the mythology of the various actual real world American Indian cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T20:03:47-07:00","id":183444,"title":"","content":"Errrr...... Werewolves, not real.<br /> <br /> the Cherokee, the Croatoan tribe, the Algonquian peoples?<br /> <br /> All VERY real...<br /> <br /> Well, not so much the Croatoan, they're pretty much dead and gone. But they WERE real. People. Not water-snake-dragon-monsters or cannibal-ghosts/real life psychotic murderer cannibals. How much does it suck to have your entire nation reduced explicitly into some vague undefined monster because some starving greenhorns carved the name of your tribe into a tree and it spooked some other guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T07:10:26-07:00","id":183767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=182362#post182362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was exactly what I did.. my reasoning being, they were the only Gods still active.. Coyote, Raven, Thunderbird, a few.. and I had a werewolf who was becoming the new Wolf, God of War others..<br /> In my game.. the Native Pantheon had been living under the &quot;protection&quot; of the American Gods..</div> </div> </div> </div> You might find some inspiration in Ars Magica's Shaman; The Hidden Path. It's time/place is medieval Europe, but I would see if it fits. (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V%C3%A4in%C3%A4m%C3%B6inen\" target=\"_blank\">V\u00e4in\u00e4m\u00f6inen of Finnish lore</a> can be seen as a very prominent old shaman)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=183443#post183443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fictional beliefs of the fictional Uktena tribe only really reflect the beliefs of the fictional Uktena tribe, even if they draw <i>inspiration </i>from real world American Indian cultures. Even then, there are limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And just where were those limits seen in the books? Scion or Werewolf. I hear a lot of bitching and whining in this thread about this or that being racist (incorrect us of the word...says a bit) and that's exactly what we have were we to deconstruct myths of this or that culture...but we take the good and leave the bad, or so how we define it. But the old books sold well enough despite it. Indeed I'm beginning to wonder if those posting so negatively are just trying to sabotage the success and turn the new product into shit. Egyptian, Irish, Mexican, Norwegian, Greek, if I were to use the incorrect usage of the term I would say the whole system is very &quot;racist.&quot;<br /> <br /> Palladium books had their own success dealing with Native Americana...I'm tempted to say that any attempt by Scion can be just as successful if not more so. (Re; Jim Butcher's take on the &quot;naagloshi.&quot;)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=183443#post183443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, you're deliberately falsifying the mythology of the various actual real world American Indian cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, because none of the books do that now with other beliefs/religions.../sarcasm<br /> Cause celebres are tiresome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=183444#post183444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errrr...... Werewolves, not real.the Cherokee, the Croatoan tribe, the Algonquian peoples?<br /> All VERY real...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why yes, my point exactly. And they were used for Werewolves. Or to use your words:<br /> <i>How much does it suck to have your entire nation reduced explicitly into some vague undefined monster because some starving greenhorns carved the name of your tribe into a tree and it spooked some other guys?</i><br /> I'm sure you boycotted the book because of it, but it made for such a good story point.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T00:09:18-07:00","id":184630,"title":"","content":"Dudes.. it's a GAME, not a cultural disertation. It's a fictional setting brushed with broad strokes to make it accessible to as many people as possible.<br /> <br /> Are the Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota or Navajo the same people? No, no more then the French, Italians or Germans are the &quot;same people&quot;. But that's not the point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T02:23:33-07:00","id":184674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=184630#post184630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dudes.. it's a GAME, not a cultural dissertation.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.ironrealms.com/role-playing-muds-the-fallacy-of-its-just-a-text-game\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;</a><a href=\"http://www.ironrealms.com/role-playing-muds-the-fallacy-of-its-just-a-text-game\" target=\"_blank\">I</a><a href=\"http://www.ironrealms.com/role-playing-muds-the-fallacy-of-its-just-a-text-game\" target=\"_blank\">t's Just A Game!&quot; Fallacy</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T09:52:29-07:00","id":184919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=184630#post184630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dudes.. it's a GAME, not a cultural disertation. It's a fictional setting brushed with broad strokes to make it accessible to as many people as possible.<br /> <br /> Are the Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota or Navajo the same people? No, no more then the French, Italians or Germans are the &quot;same people&quot;. But that's not the point</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem being that &quot;broad strokes&quot; leaves the French (Nemetondevos), Italians (Dodekatheon) and Germans (Aesir) with three Pantheons but the Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota and Navajo with one, despite them all being equally distinct and unique. When &quot;broad strokes&quot; are only applied to certain types of people, it's an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:42:45-07:00","id":184951,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=184630#post184630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dudes.. it's a GAME, not a cultural disertation. It's a fictional setting brushed with broad strokes to make it accessible to as many people as possible.<br /> <br /> Are the Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota or Navajo the same people? No, no more then the French, Italians or Germans are the &quot;same people&quot;. But that's not the point</div> </div> </div> </div>I assure you I'm probably the last person that has any problem with this. (I've said nearly the same words in many posts already)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T09:27:20-07:00","id":185598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=184919#post184919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem being that &quot;broad strokes&quot; leaves the French (Nemetondevos), Italians (Dodekatheon) and Germans (Aesir) with three Pantheons but the Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota and Navajo with one, despite them all being equally distinct and unique. When &quot;broad strokes&quot; are only applied to certain types of people, it's an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to backstop that... The Cherokee, Algonquin, Lakota and Navajo are, by origin, by culture, by geography, by environment much more different than the Italian (Graeco-Roman), French (Greaco-Roman crossed with Scando-Germanic, and, if people insist, Celtic, but, as far as mythology goes, there's just &quot;no 'there' there&quot;), Germany (Scando-Germanic), all located adjacent to each other with largely the same environmental situations.<br /> <br /> So, yes, handwaving them together, when, unlike a pantheon like the Nemetondevos, we have TONS and TONS and TONS of relatively easy to access information, is somewhat questionable. Especially, also once again, when doing so is similar-to-the-point-of-being-congruant to several different types mistreatment the living members of those groups are still having to cope with, much less the devastating crap they had to deal with historically. <br /> <br /> It also seems..... well, lazy. All the energy we've discussed doing it one or the other, we could have been using to actually put together a project to populate North America with all these different pantheons. Many hands makes light work and a lot of people have chimed in here. Look at Scion 2.0. Creating a pantheon is much easier than that. Esp if you just start with some potential divine parents, a few Birthrights and a PSP and worry about the monsters, Under and Overworld and Titan later...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T10:47:43-07:00","id":185626,"title":"","content":"I have picked up some books from the library about myths related to the Cherokee tribe, Navajo tribe, and Hopi tribe. I intend on coming up with some sort of cohesive list of deities for each for scrutinization sometime soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T11:06:17-07:00","id":185634,"title":"","content":"It's easier when they directly mention attributes. Most of the lore/stories rarely ever get that detailed though. That's why we have one or two from each geographical area (give or take) that survive in today's consciousness, but the rest take some digging...and moreso an imaginative take on this or that story. The frustration is recognizing that the &quot;people&quot; have refused to tell all of their stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T12:56:35-07:00","id":185737,"title":"","content":"...Have you looked into native american mythology? Cause I have, and there's all kinds of stories about individual figures with tons of attributes. Their stories are just as detailed and powerful as anything from Europe. It's a bit harder to find, since there's a huge Eurocentric bias in our culture, but it's definitely out there. By &quot;survive in today's consciousness&quot; I think you may mean &quot;I've seen on TV or the internet&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T13:50:03-07:00","id":185773,"title":"","content":"Would it trouble you to cite some sources, Telgar? You've talked a lot about such sources existing in abundance, but haven't named any.<br /> <br /> Right now, I have the following books checked out:<br /> <br /> <i>Myths of the North American Indians</i> by Lewis Spence<br /> <i>Myths of the Cherokee and Sacred Formulas of the Cherokees</i> by James Mooney<br /> <i>Hopi Voices</i> by Harold Courlander<br /> <br /> Plus, I've got a free PDF copy of <i>The D\u00een\u00e9: Origin Myths of the Navaho Indians </i>by Aileen O'Bryan.<br /> <br /> I've also got a free HTML copy of <i>&quot;In the Beginning: A Navaho Creation Myth&quot;</i> that, I think, anyone can access <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/nav/itb/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T14:09:29-07:00","id":185787,"title":"","content":"Let me try this tact then.<br /> <br /> Take your arguement on what is or isn't racist ELSEWHERE. This not what is being discussed here at all.<br /> <br /> Here.. I'll solve the problem entirely... All the Native Gods are dead. Period. They went the way of the Mayans. So many of their worshippers were killed so quickly that they were lost to antiquity.<br /> <br /> What is it about White Wolf games that brings out the righteous indignation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T17:51:14-07:00","id":185868,"title":"","content":"Why would they be dead because their worshippers are? Why would the Mayan Gods be dead? Worshippers don't define or empower the Gods in Scion.<br /> <br /> It's not about White Wolf games, it's about marginalizing and treating cultures disrespectfully when it's <i>not that hard</i> to do better.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vary, I'll get back to you with some sources, I'd have to dig up some names. It's been years since I looked into Cherokee mythology seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:25:29-07:00","id":185943,"title":"","content":"It's negative crap that some people aren't interested at all in hearing. What some want to hear is a positive contribution. Something you should try to do at least <i>once</i> in this thread. Or be relegated to the &quot;ignore&quot; function. Quite frankly I'm tired of reading the destructive posts. Try giving a constructive one instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:29:56-07:00","id":185944,"title":"","content":"<i>Worshippers don't define or empower the Gods in Scion.</i> Those that run their respective game however certainly do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T21:47:22-07:00","id":186005,"title":"","content":"Did you just ignore all the posts talking about how to research and create well-founded native American Pantheons? Cause there's lots. They just don't agree with the approach of the OP or you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:19:14-07:00","id":186322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=185773#post185773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it trouble you to cite some sources, Telgar? You've talked a lot about such sources existing in abundance, but haven't named any.<br /> <br /> Right now, I have the following books checked out:<br /> <br /> <i>Myths of the North American Indians</i> by Lewis Spence<br /> <i>Myths of the Cherokee and Sacred Formulas of the Cherokees</i> by James Mooney<br /> <i>Hopi Voices</i> by Harold Courlander<br /> <br /> Plus, I've got a free PDF copy of <i>The D\u00een\u00e9: Origin Myths of the Navaho Indians </i>by Aileen O'Bryan.<br /> <br /> I've also got a free HTML copy of <i>&quot;In the Beginning: A Navaho Creation Myth&quot;</i> that, I think, anyone can access <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/nav/itb/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the bibliography and the link!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T09:28:08-07:00","id":186330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=185787#post185787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try this tact then.<br /> <br /> Take your arguement on what is or isn't racist ELSEWHERE. This not what is being discussed here at all.<br /> <br /> Here.. I'll solve the problem entirely... All the Native Gods are dead. Period. They went the way of the Mayans. So many of their worshippers were killed so quickly that they were lost to antiquity.<br /> <br /> What is it about White Wolf games that brings out the righteous indignation?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean &quot;lost to modern North American history&quot;, right? <br /> <br /> BTW, as an anthropologist who worked with compiling Mayan dictionaries and who has been to Mexico, Belize and Guatemala several times, I can absolutely 100% attest that the Mayans aren't even remotely gone. They live right where they always have. They just don't live in centralized cities marked by monumental architecture, with all sorts of inter-city conflict, etc. But, essentially, right there. You can go visit if you'd like. <br /> <br /> Also, despite several centuries of Christian overlay, a lot of those myths are still alive and well. For example, the whole luchador phenomena appears to have been influenced by what amounts to masked bare-knuckles boxing matches in honor of Cha'ac that still happen every year in several villages in Chiapas. Also, same festival, in one of the towns, they have a creepy ritual where all the children go down steps to a well and touch the water before climbing back up and out. It's a lock that, back in the day, not as many came back up the steps as went down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T23:37:52-07:00","id":186871,"title":"","content":"In the fictional game setting of SCION the Mayan Gods are gone, disappeared, dead. I don't need a cultural dissertation, I watch the History channel, I know the Mayan people still exist.<br /> <br /> Seriously, how hard is it for people to understand that this is a game, not a sociology paper? Is it inspired by real history? Yes.. but that's the end of it.. INSPIRATION.<br /> <br /> In the bounds of my game, the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; is a coalition of mant Gods because that's what I need it to be for the stories I want to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T01:24:35-07:00","id":186910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fictional game setting of SCION the Mayan Gods are gone, disappeared, dead. I don't need a cultural dissertation, I watch the History channel, I know the Mayan people still exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er. Really? Cause some of them appear as AKA's for the Aztec Gods (again, because telling brown people apart is <i>super hard you guys</i>) and that's the entire coverage Scion gives them. Are you talking about <i>your</i> game? Cause the fictional game setting of <i>your</i> game is different from the fictional game setting of Scion as a product line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how hard is it for people to understand that this is a game, not a sociology paper? Is it inspired by real history? Yes.. but that's the end of it.. INSPIRATION.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the copy of Little Black Sambo my Grandma gave me when I was a kid, that's totally cool, right, cause it's just a children's book? Seriously, how hard is it to understand that pop culture can be INSPIRED by real history without being racist or ethnocentric? It just takes the TINIEST bit more work for a vastly improved result that not only is better, but it might actually help introduce people to other cultures in a way they haven't experienced before. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the bounds of my game, the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; is a coalition of mant Gods because that's what I need it to be for the stories I want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it works great for your game. I would not want to see that as a published product for all the many, many reasons presented in this thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T04:09:01-07:00","id":186961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fictional game setting of SCION the Mayan Gods are gone, disappeared, dead. I don't need a cultural dissertation, I watch the History channel, I know the Mayan people still exist.<br /> <br /> Seriously, how hard is it for people to understand that this is a game, not a sociology paper? Is it inspired by real history? Yes.. but that's the end of it.. INSPIRATION.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely correct. This is a game inspired by the actual, real stories and cultures of humanity; and that's the key. We strive for historical and mythological accuracy to represent each of the cultures being showcased because if we wanted to play in a game based on make-believe and the extent of our imagination; we'd go to Exalted or Dungeons and Dragons for their fictional pantheons.<br /> <br /> We don't want fictional pantheons, we want the interaction and stories and connections with pantheons who were once very, very real and very, very important to different culture groups. Requesting that one has a basic grasp of mythology is not asking too much; and the very fact that those of you opposed to the idea of *gasp* research can't even give a good reason you're opposed to it just showcases how very little you actually care about the setting.<br /> <br /> And that's fine. For your own games if you want to have a mish-mash of slapstick ideas that come together because you're too lazy to pick up a book and read (or type in a reputable website and scroll through information) then go right ahead. We can complain and give it the side-eye, but no one's going to force you to change your playstyle in your personal games.<br /> <br /> But when you want to create something for the public consumption as a fan-based pantheon and have it stand side-by-side with the other, researched pantheons who were crafted with the basics of respect to the culture and stories they heralded from, you better get used to having your work scrutinized. If you can't handle it, take your ball and go home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the bounds of my game, the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; is a coalition of mant Gods because that's what I need it to be for the stories I want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newsflash: No one actually cares what you do in your personal games. You can have superheroes be gods for all we care, or have the mole people be the descendants of the Atlantean superculture that inspired all future religions. Just don't bring your substandard standards to the table and expect it to be given the same treatment as the actual dishes there, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">Comprende?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T07:17:45-07:00","id":187055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Newsflash: No one actually cares what you do in your personal games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Newsflash; This is a thread asking for certain things for running personal games. Not a debate on Onyx Path Publishing policies. No one is forcing you to read this thread. The cheap self-righteous bullshit should just go away. Far away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, how hard is it for people to understand that this is a game, not a sociology paper? Is it inspired by real history? Yes.. but that's the end of it.. INSPIRATION.<br /> <br /> In the bounds of my game, the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; is a coalition of many Gods because that's what I need it to be for the stories I want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> <br /> What I was doing for my own exercise, at least for the quick and dirty, was taking <a href=\"http://media-cache-ec0.pinimg.com/736x/5e/df/86/5edf86e8c60b483a84efa0e9e77c31b7.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this map</a> (There are better images, this is just an example) which mentions 4-6 major tribes per geographical region; and find the great spirits/deities that they each had in common. There's usually one or two that is fleshed out enough to characterize. I also added attributes of the geography itself to these spirits (if they weren't obvious enough) to help keep the flavor of the locale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  link fix 07-03-2014, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T08:34:48-07:00","id":187111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation#post152033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So this is the bare bones that I came up with about The Spirit Nation. Any help to flesh it out further and to clarify things would be great. If anything, I'm hoping that the suggestions will help Onyx Path to create this as a replacement to the Yankee Pantheon for 2E. So thanks for the help. Any suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div> As the OP states, he wanted it to be considered for actual use outside of personal games; even as a steeping point for the official line. My &quot;self-righteous&quot; statement holds truth. You want to be taken serious? Do some actual research into the various world mythologies and keep a respectful mindset while you're at it. Anyone on this forum is willing and happy to help with a project if the OP genuinely wants to dedicate the effort to it. We're not so happy when the OPs idea of research is looking up Wikipedia animal spirits and calling it a day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T09:11:00-07:00","id":187138,"title":"","content":"Okay, in my oppinion, this thread has gone waaaaaay over board... for those interested in my thoughts on the subject, see the text inside the rant signs. For those who are interested in potential contributions to the OP, see the text below the rant.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">/begin rant</span><br /> <br /> This thread sort of compiles the reason why I left the old Scion forum a while back and hanged around other more constructive places to discuss Scion. It really saddens me to see that the board has become even more deeply ingrained with these petty flame wars than it was before <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> IMO, the general &quot;do it my way or don't do it&quot; method around this forum is as bad as it was on the previous forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are absolutely correct. This is a game inspired by the actual, real stories and cultures of humanity; and that's the key. We strive for historical and mythological accuracy to represent each of the cultures being showcased because if we wanted to play in a game based on make-believe and the extent of our imagination; we'd go to Exalted or Dungeons and Dragons for their fictional pantheons.<br /> <br /> We don't want fictional pantheons, we want the interaction and stories and connections with pantheons who were once very, very real and very, very important to different culture groups. Requesting that one has a basic grasp of mythology is not asking too much; and the very fact that those of you opposed to the idea of *gasp* research can't even give a good reason you're opposed to it just showcases how very little you actually care about the setting. </div> </div> </div>This thread has made it blatantly clear that no, this &quot;we&quot; are not really the &quot;we&quot; you think it is. Some want it, others doesn't. The fact that this thread exists is proof that there's no single concencus on how to make pantheons for this game.<br /> <br /> Some (me among them) doesn't put the same emphasis on cultural accuracy or historical accuracy and instead wants to play the game without taking history classes or making tons of research first. We just want to pick up the game and run it as we feel its supposed to be run. I'm not saying either apporach is wrong, just that some people put the emphasis on other things than the historical accuracy.<br /> <br /> If someone want help in creating a spirit and totemist based native american pantheon, why not help him and thus maybe kindle his flame for a more accurate pantheon, than deride and flame his work with discussions about what racism is or isn't?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Er. Really? Cause some of them appear as AKA's for the Aztec Gods (again, because telling brown people apart is <i>super hard you guys</i>) and that's the entire coverage Scion gives them. </div> </div> </div>That might be a design decision from the creators of Scion. Maybe they wanted gods from different pantheons to interact and change depending on the circumstance they were encountered in. Maybe Thor didn't always use that name and prefered Donner when speaking to some gods. Scion always struck me as a game which were such things werent just common but benefitial. maybe the designers never intended for a Maya pantheon to have existed? Maybe they wanted it to be so that the<br /> <br /> They even do this with Zeus (Jupiter) and thus makes a single god into two different gods. When I put my Inca Pantheon togheter, I used this approach to create a far more dynamic pantheon than I could've done otherwise. I used one of the lesser rain gods as a god from another pantheon to create a (to me) logical bridge between two different pantheons. I also did this to the greek and norse pantheon by letting marriages take place as background to the current conflict in our game.<br /> <br /> If anyone would like to make a compilation of all the european pantheons into a single pantheon via broad strokes, let them. I wouldn't mind. The base similarities is already there, so why not? could be an interesting twist on a Scion-verse with Asiacentrism instead of Europeancentrism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the OP states, he wanted it to be considered for actual use outside of personal games; even as a steeping point for the official line. My &quot;self-righteous&quot; statement holds truth. You want to be taken serious? Do some actual research into the various world mythologies and keep a respectful mindset while you're at it. Anyone on this forum is willing and happy to help with a project if the OP genuinely wants to dedicate the effort to it. We're not so happy when the OPs idea of research is looking up Wikipedia animal spirits and calling it a day </div> </div> </div>The problem with saying this is that maybe he wants the Scion line to take a different approach or direction that you want it too. You and several other's aren't happy with him suggesting this, but others might be. I'd rather have a well woven interconnected world were gods from different pantheons either have connections or suggested connections, rather than an exact treatise on the pantheons of the ancient (or modern world). For that, I'll buy a book with that purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the copy of Little Black Sambo my Grandma gave me when I was a kid, that's totally cool, right, cause it's just a children's book? </div> </div> </div>The idea about what is racist or not has changed over the years. If the book is the one written in 1899, it was written in a world with values a whole lot different from the ones we have today. What we deem appropriate today might be deemed inappropriate by the future world. While that book might be racists by today's standards, maybe it wasn't considered as racist when it was printed. That book is okay for its time period. Look at the &quot;Pippi Longstockings&quot; books from Sweden. They are today considered highly racist because of some of the content, but it was considered okay for somewere around 40 years.<br /> <br /> The same thing goes for Werewolf the apocalypse. I dislike it for the same reasons I dislike masquerade and prefer Requiem... mainly that it stereotypes characters to behave a certain way because they belong to a certain tribe/clan. It's much more fun if a Ventrue isn't always recognizable as a ventrue... ButI dont judge the game for being inspired by real world cultures and socieites despite them using blatantly twisted and stereotyped presentations of non-white cultures. It's not reality. It's a game which is bound to not be the same as reality and if someone is unable to tell the difference between game and reality, one should probably not play the game from the beginning. The Scion books, much like other game books, werent meant as educational tools. They were meant to be a game where we all can have fun.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">/end of rant</span><br /> <br /> I've expanded my suggestion for PSP a bit and overhauled some of the suggestions I did for the PSP:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Spirit Totem</span><br /> Hero Quirk:</b> The Hero becomes aware if there's anything troubling the spirit world in an area (such as pollution, disrespectful treatment etc.). He lacks precise understanding, but gets a one sentence general feel about the area if he focuses on it.<br /> <br /> \u25cf Totem Protection: The Scion becomes immune to the attacks of his chosen totem. Animals of the chosen totem never attack the scion unless controlled by someone of greater legend than the scion. Only a totem creature of equal or greater legend may cause harm to the Scion.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf Spirit Imbual: The Scion can imbue legend points into an object, keeping it as a temporary reserve of legend.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Spirit Retrieval: The Scion can drain a friend's or his own relics for legend by reducing their potency temporarily.<br /> <br /> <b>Demigod Quirk:</b> The Scion can see spirits of lower legend (1 to 2) and speak to them without paying any cost. He can also force such spirits to leave his presence.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Spirit Form: The Scion takes on the form of a spirit and becomes more difficult to hurt. His soak increases by his legend and his DV increases by his highest dot in the PSP. He can also step through natural barriers less than a foot thick.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Send Away: By displacing an object (or person) into the spirit world, the object becomes unreachable by normal means. Those of greater or equal legend can attempt to pull it back<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf Spirit Breath: The scion becomes one with the living world and gains a bonus to his rolls. This bonus is more powerful outside of civilization<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf Honor thy Ancestors: The Scion can imbue himself with the spirit of the world, turninga number of dice into auto-successes.<br /> <br /> <b>God Quirk:</b> The Scion can see all spirits (of any legend) unless they are of equal or greater legend and attempt to hide from him. The Scion<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Totem Creation: The Scion can create a totem spirit out of thin air and use all previous boons on said Totem.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Totem Destruction: The Scion can sever the bounds between spirits, reducing the potency of relics and boons possessed by those of equal or lesser legend.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Spirit World: The Scion can create a whole new realm in the spirit world from scratch. The Scion may enter this realm freely at first, but as the world becomes more defined, it grows more distant and difficult to access.<br /> <br /> Also, as for gods, the typical coyote trickster character could borrow a page from old Loki and look something like this:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Coyote</span></b><br /> <i>Aka: The Fox, the trickster</i><br /> <br /> The god collectivly known as 'Coyote' may be, or might not be, several different gods. Why a collection of gods would pretend to be the same god is up to debate, but the impact of this one (or several) god is undeniable. Since the destruction of his home pantheon however, this god has been roaming free and sought alliances in other places.<br /> <br /> <b>Associated Powers:</b> Epic Intelligence, Epic Manipulation, Epic Charisma, Epic Wits, Animal (Coyote), Chaos, Illusion, Spirit Totem<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Athletics, Empathy, Larceny, Politics, Presence, Stealth<br /> <b>Rivals:</b> Loki, Set, Hermes, Tezcatlipoca","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T10:05:26-07:00","id":187217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MisterShifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=186871#post186871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the fictional game setting of SCION the Mayan Gods are gone, disappeared, dead. I don't need a cultural dissertation, I watch the History channel, I know the Mayan people still exist.<br /> <br /> Seriously, how hard is it for people to understand that this is a game, not a sociology paper? Is it inspired by real history? Yes.. but that's the end of it.. INSPIRATION.<br /> <br /> In the bounds of my game, the &quot;Native Pantheon&quot; is a coalition of mant Gods because that's what I need it to be for the stories I want to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Correction : No, the Mayan gods aren't gone in the game. They were syncretized to the Aztec pantheon. A lot of people want the two separated out, but insofar as the fictional game RAW, they most definitely exist. If you wish to eliminate them, I can give you the page numbers and the names to take off the alternative ID lists. Then, in your home game, you can have the Mayan pantheon dead for some in-game reason. Hopefully related to some cool plot you are running about pantheon genocide (pantheocide?) and not just out of spite. <br /> <br /> 2. Warning: Do not believe what you watch on the History Channel. It is very seldom history at all. The colleagues I know who have been interviewed have universally regretted their involvement. It is usually the worst level of sensationalized nonsense designed to feed the preconceptions on the topic at hand with a heavy handed dose of pure fiction tossed in for spice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T10:20:47-07:00","id":187229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187138#post187138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread sort of compiles the reason why I left the old Scion forum a while back and hanged around other more constructive places to discuss Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are these other constructive places?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187138#post187138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some (me among them) doesn't put the same emphasis on cultural accuracy or historical accuracy and instead wants to play the game without taking history classes or making tons of research first. We just want to pick up the game and run it as we feel its supposed to be run. I'm not saying either apporach is wrong, just that some people put the emphasis on other things than the historical accuracy.<br /> <br /> If someone want help in creating a spirit and totemist based native american pantheon, why not help him and thus maybe kindle his flame for a more accurate pantheon, than deride and flame his work with discussions about what racism is or isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>But this situation is unique. This is not just someone coming to the forums to ask for assistance with their personal game, the OP actually wants to create a supplement that he hopes will be used by Onyx Path. That is why everyone is coming out of the woodwork and demanding historical accuracy and no racism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T11:23:54-07:00","id":187277,"title":"","content":"~~<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187229#post187229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are these other constructive places?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously not for the few that post in this thread...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187229#post187229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this situation is unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only when you throw out the objective view of the success of the other books.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187229#post187229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is why everyone is coming out of the woodwork and demanding historical accuracy and no racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...&quot;everyone...&quot; And those few are completely ignoring the hypocrisy in their demands.<br /> Enough wallowing in the negative stuff...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187138#post187138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've expanded my suggestion for PSP a bit and overhauled some of the suggestions I did for the PSP:</div> </div> </div> </div>I like what you did.<br /> My focus has been different. Hard to elaborate as I've always been more of a reader of ideas.<br /> <br /> Regional PSP: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manitou\" target=\"_blank\">Manitou</a><i> Manitou is the spiritual and fundamental life force understood by Algonquian groups of Native Americans. It is omnipresent and manifests everywhere: organisms, the environment, events, etc.</i><br /> <br /> Regional PSP <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wakan_Tanka\" target=\"_blank\">Wakan</a><i> In the Sioux way of life, Wakan Tanka (Standard Lakota Orthography: Wak\u021f\u00e1\u014b T\u021f\u00e1\u014bka) is the term for &quot;the sacred&quot; or &quot;the divine&quot;. This is usually translated as &quot;The Great Spirit&quot;. It is interpreted as the power or the sacredness that resides in everything, resembling some animistic and pantheistic beliefs. This term describes every creature and object as wak\u021f\u00e1\u014b (&quot;holy&quot;) or having aspects that are wak\u021f\u00e1\u014b.</i><br /> <br /> Regional PSP <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Witch_(Navajo)\" target=\"_blank\">Witchery Ways</a> (Not nice stuff but I found it interesting)<br /> <i><br /> 1.) Corpse-poison Way; (literally, Witchery or Harming)<br /> 2.) Sympathetic magic; not based on the corpse-poison, but on the power of names, body material like fingernails, and possessions to affect their owners; it is a practice that revolves around sympathetic magic and curses.<br /> 3.) Frenzy Way; This kind of witchcraft involves magically influencing the minds and emotions of others.</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T11:58:22-07:00","id":187294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187277#post187277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously not for the few that post in this thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187277#post187277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only when you throw out the objective view of the success of the other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Success based on what?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187277#post187277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...&quot;everyone...&quot; And those few are completely ignoring the hypocrisy in their demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean. There were only four of you (Jackalope Vegas, Shadowflame, Gemstone, Mister Shifter) in support of homogenization, and fourteen of us (Telgar, Watcher, Samudra, Creticus, Iry, TruePrep1818, Griffinguy24, Me, Charles Red, Aynie, Ajax, Mr Innes, Guitarsniper, Varygoode) in support of respectfully depicting each pantheon. We're the majority.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure, but I think Jackalope Vegas swapped to our side after much discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T12:46:47-07:00","id":187317,"title":"","content":"How is it hypocritical to want all cultures to be treated with equal respect when being presented in pop culture and entertainment products? Regardless of the &quot;it's just a game/movie/video/show/book&quot; nonsense, positive portrayals of a wide variety of groups in pop culture is on the rise and that's a good thing. It doesn't matter if a product is just made for entertainment. Entertainment helps shape our culture and reflects our values. <br /> <br /> Does Scion need to go to Master's Thesis levels of examination? No. But it's only right to treat all cultures the same. If we break Europe down into distinct cultural groups based on real, historical societies and religions, we should do the same for Africa, Asia, North America, South America, Australia and Oceania.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T16:08:29-07:00","id":187488,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">OT</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187229#post187229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are these other constructive places?</div> </div> </div> </div>I took my ideas to Sverok's (Sweden's Association for Roleplaying games and conflict games) forums and to my own Wiki were those I play with collaborate to create things for our games ^^ Plus the skype chat were I hang out with a lot of other roleplayers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187229#post187229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this situation is unique. This is not just someone coming to the forums to ask for assistance with their personal game, the OP actually wants to create a supplement that he hopes will be used by Onyx Path. That is why everyone is coming out of the woodwork and demanding historical accuracy and no racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I can understand why people want to defend their views. But if they really want historical accuracy they could create their own thread which handles this matter more accuractly and suggest it as an alternative to what is done here. If he wants to produce a &quot;broad strokes&quot; pantheon that works better with how most people view, then I suggest that we either help or say we dislike it and move on to other threads <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now I've just returned to this forum after a prolonged abscene, so the new forum might be different from the old one. This thread however, doesn't really give that notion any real credit.<br /> <br /> [/quote]I'm not sure what you mean. There were only four of you (Jackalope Vegas, Shadowflame, Gemstone, Mister Shifter) in support of homogenization, and fourteen of us (Telgar, Watcher, Samudra, Creticus, Iry, TruePrep1818, Griffinguy24, Me, Charles Red, Aynie, Ajax, Mr Innes, Guitarsniper, Varygoode) in support of respectfully depicting each pantheon. We're the majority[/quote]<br /> Still, 4 out of 18 means that not everyone wants to do it &quot;your&quot; way. To me, the most important thing is to have a fun game. I prefer to have detailed and well described pantheons, but I can understand the value of doing something the other way around.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">/OT</span><br /> <br /> This might work as a basis for the purview selection of said totem pantheon.<br /> <br /> Bear: Epic Strength, Epic Stamina, Epic Wits, Animal (Bear), Earth<br /> Eagle: Epic Dexterity, Epic Intelligence, Epic Perception, Animal (Eagle), Justice, Sky<br /> The Great Spirit: Epic Intelligence, Epic Wits, Death, Earth, Fertility, Health<br /> Raven: Epic Perception, Animal (Raven), Chaos, Darkness, Sky<br /> Wolf: Epic Strength, Epic Stamina, Epic Perception, Animal (Wolf), Earth<br /> Otter: Epic Stamina, Epic Charisma, Earth, Water<br /> <br /> I'm rather strongly in favor for building the pantheon up from shattered pantheons. Any suggestions for how this happened? Maybe the Titans escaped nearby their godrealm and annihilated them and the other pantheons close by during their escape? That could explain what happened.<br /> <br /> Going with the pop-culturesque idea of this Pantheon, maybe a Titan to reflect said value? A titan of corruption or destruction perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T16:31:34-07:00","id":187499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187488#post187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took my ideas to Sverok's (Sweden's Association for Roleplaying games and conflict games) forums and to my own Wiki were those I play with collaborate to create things for our games ^^ Plus the skype chat were I hang out with a lot of other roleplayers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! I appreciate it! I'm browsing around it now with the help of Google Translate.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187488#post187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I can understand why people want to defend their views. But if they really want historical accuracy they could create their own thread which handles this matter more accuractly and suggest it as an alternative to what is done here. If he wants to produce a &quot;broad strokes&quot; pantheon that works better with how most people view, then I suggest that we either help or say we dislike it and move on to other threads <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, this is probably the best course of action. We probably would have, if it were not for Shadowflame; he has a way of inciting flame wars. Someone should make a new thread and start putting together a historically accurate (to the best of our ability) pantheon for one of the native american tribes. Maybe the Scion 2.0 people since Gotham By Night is gone?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187488#post187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, 4 out of 18 means that not everyone wants to do it &quot;your&quot; way. To me, the most important thing is to have a fun game. I prefer to have detailed and well described pantheons, but I can understand the value of doing something the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the racism issue seems to be a big deal. I do not think anyone here would suggest not having fun, but is that fun acceptable when it is embracing a lot of harmful stereotypes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T17:32:53-07:00","id":187536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187499#post187499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that fun acceptable when it is embracing a lot of harmful stereotypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of contention in a sentence, that is. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T19:02:43-07:00","id":187570,"title":"","content":"We would work on pantheons but with the legal issues with gotham by night's mechanics we're playing catch up with those first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T19:35:52-07:00","id":187597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187570#post187570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We would work on pantheons but with the legal issues with gotham by night's mechanics we're playing catch up with those first</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of legal issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T20:31:31-07:00","id":187616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187294#post187294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean.<br /> Success based on what?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the thread &quot;Any updated information on Scion:Origins?;&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=180147#post180147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telgar- Your remark &quot;one of the least played games released by WW&quot; is simply untrue. Every release for Scion did very well, far beyond any reasonable idea that they were all bought just to read- people played. For many it wasn't easy, for some it was, and for others it was impossible because of the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187499#post187499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, this is probably the best course of action. We probably would have, if it were not for Shadowflame; he has a way of inciting flame wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Lol! How is it that none of you did this &quot;best course of action&quot; already? Seems to me you prefer having a thread where you can troll those that have put forth their imagination in producing something for their respective game runs.<br /> Don't reply. Just move along and create your own thread now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187488#post187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rather strongly in favor for building the pantheon up from shattered pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>From <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Native_Americans_in_the_United_States#mediaviewer/File:Nordamerikanische_Kulturareale_en.png\" target=\"_blank\">this map</a> hmm...some distinct geographical cultures. The more well known are the ones I'd choose as they've survived to today's frame of reference.<br /> 1.) <u><b>Artic</b></u>; Nanook; Sedna (The Inuit belief seems harsh. From <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit_mythology\" target=\"_blank\">wiki</a><i>Indeed, the traditional stories, rituals and taboos of the Inuit are so tied into the fearful and precautionary culture required by their harsh environment that it raises the question as to whether they qualify as beliefs at all, much less religion. Knud Rasmussen asked his guide and friend Aua, an angakkuq (shaman), about Inuit religious beliefs among the Iglulingmiut (people of Igloolik) and was told: &quot;We don't believe. We fear.&quot; Living in a varied and irregular world, the Inuit traditionally did not worship anything, but they feared much.</i><br /> 2.) <u><b>Subartic</b></u>; Nanabozho; Gitche Manitou; Nokomis<br /> 3.) <u><b>Plateau/Basin</b></u>; Wiped out. Raven took over.<br /> 4.) <u><b>Pacific Northwest</b></u>; Raven; Kaiti; Dzelarhons<br /> 5.) <u><b>East Atlantic</b></u>; Uktena (Horned Serpent); Dawn; Atahensic; Gendenwitha (Morning Star); Sosondowah<br /> 6.) <u><b>Northeast Woodlands</b></u>; Glooscap; Tabaldak; Odzihodo; Pamola<br /> 7.) <u><b>Southwest</b></u>; Grandmother Spider; Coyote; Killer-of-Enemies; Kokopelli; Toho<br /> <br /> And I'm running out of time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187488#post187488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any suggestions for how this happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had toyed with the idea of the &quot;White Plague&quot; that was brought over from other countries. A Titan of a sort that seems to devour Native cultures. A kinda of spiritual counterpart to the &quot;Black Death&quot; pandemic that happened in Europe in the 14th Century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T21:25:02-07:00","id":187690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187616#post187616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the thread &quot;Any updated information on Scion:Origins?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't understand. What does the success of the current edition of Scion have to do with homogenization of pantheons?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187616#post187616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Lol! How is it that none of you did this &quot;best course of action&quot; already? Seems to me you prefer having a thread where you can troll those that have put forth their imagination in producing something for their respective game runs.<br /> Don't reply. Just move along and create your own thread now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a troll. You bait people into responding to loaded statements. Why does anyone respond to a troll in the first place? I guess we have weak willpower to resist. I'm not sure if I should be the one to create the new thread. I don't know anything about Native Americans. Maybe someone more informed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 07-04-2014, 12:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T00:16:21-07:00","id":187759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187616#post187616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had toyed with the idea of the &quot;White Plague&quot; that was brought over from other countries. A Titan of a sort that seems to devour Native cultures. A kinda of spiritual counterpart to the &quot;Black Death&quot; pandemic that happened in Europe in the 14th Century.</div> </div> </div> </div>It happened. It was called smallpox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T00:58:35-07:00","id":187768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187597#post187597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of legal issues?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm terribly sorry this is off topic and I don't mean to detract from the conversation going on here. But, Gotham By Night have just requested that we take down a number of their Purviews and Pantheon Specific Purviews due to some difficulties on their end of things. We had permission originally, but they have had to withdraw it, which we entirely understand. We are currently working on Storms/Thunder and Me, and I am doing research in order to develop a new PsP for the Bogovi. The full details of things are <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=180299#post180299\">here</a>,<br /> <br /> We would love to work on a Pantheon for one of the Native North American groups. The Huron, the Iroquois, or the Cree are my personal favorites and, when we eventually recover from this all hands on deck focus on recovering from the situation at hand, I would like to spend my time starting to work on one of those three. Assuming, of course, the Iroquois have a consistent culture and religion, since they are a group of different tribes in a confederacy, if I am remembering my early Canadian history correctly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T03:53:59-07:00","id":187799,"title":"","content":"OT<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187690#post187690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't understand. What does the success of the current edition of Scion have to do with homogenization of pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point he's trying to make is that Scion, despite the generalization of its pantheons, was a success. Scion doesn't need to be an academic paper to be successful. Take my group for example, we really love the aztec pantheon and the loa pantheon despite not being true to the source material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187690#post187690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are a troll. You bait people into responding to loaded statements. Why does anyone respond to a troll in the first place? I guess we have weak willpower to resist. I'm not sure if I should be the one to create the new thread. I don't know anything about Native Americans. Maybe someone more informed?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowFlame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Lol! How is it that none of you did this &quot;best course of action&quot; already? Seems to me you prefer having a thread where you can troll those that have put forth their imagination in producing something for their respective game runs.<br /> Don't reply. Just move along and create your own thread now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm gonna go out on a limb here and say that you both view the other as a troll because you strongly disagree on something. You both clearly have very strong oppinions, but calling someone a troll will only lead to further flaming and derailing of the thread. Take a step back, a few breaths and then add to the discussion once more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This thread has made it very clear that there are at least two different groups trying to work at this board, can we at least try to respect eachother?<br /> <br /> I'd also like to point out that I actually enjoy reading well researched pantheons and I do take my research seriously when I feel it's needed, but that doesn't mean I can't read something that was written via the help of wikipedia without flaming it. This is a board to promote creativity, not to stamp out those who has a different oppinion. That goes for both sides <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> /OT<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Pox - the Titan of Disease</span><br /> <b>Favored Purviews:</b> Chaos, Darkness, Death, Health (the destructive part only), War<br /> <b>Banned Purviews:</b> Justice, Sun, Fire, Health (the healing part only), Justice<br /> Pox represents the destructive forces of the world that tore asunder the land and destroyed the native inhabitants once the europeans began to colonize the new world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T04:34:37-07:00","id":187809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187799#post187799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point he's trying to make is that Scion, despite the generalization of its pantheons, was a success. Scion doesn't need to be an academic paper to be successful. Take my group for example, we really love the aztec pantheon and the loa pantheon despite not being true to the source material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember very many pantheons that were homogenized in RAW Scion. The Loa represent a very real modern religion, even if I think the Orisha are a better choice. The Aztecs are partially syncretized with the Mayans, so a half point to them. The Shen are definite offenders, so I will count them as a full point, but they have a pretty good reason for being homogenized (they were actually homogenized in real life, and we lack information about pre-homogenization). So that is .5 pantheons in core Scion and one and 1.5 if you include Companion. That seems to be very little homogenization overall, unless I am missing someone?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187799#post187799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm gonna go out on a limb here and say that you both view the other as a troll because you strongly disagree on something. You both clearly have very strong oppinions, but calling someone a troll will only lead to further flaming and derailing of the thread. Take a step back, a few breaths and then add to the discussion once more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I was definitely upset with him a month or two ago, but now I am pretty mellow about it. I figured out his name from the old forums, and he got into an enormous amount of fights with other posters. So this is more of an objective judgement. I suppose talking about it is not very constructive though, so I won't bring it up in this thread again for the sake of not derailing it further than I already have.<br /> <br /> Seriously, does anyone know enough about a Native American tribe to start a new thread about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T05:37:01-07:00","id":187866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187809#post187809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, does anyone know enough about a Native American tribe to start a new thread about them?</div> </div> </div> </div> I will, soon. I have several books. I will post a thread for each one as I develop it. Cherokee, Hopi, Navajo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T06:06:53-07:00","id":187881,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187690#post187690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if I should be the one to create the new thread. I don't know anything about Native Americans. Maybe someone more informed?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the equivalent about bitching about a movie you've never seen. Maybe you should have taken the time to review the links I've posted. You might have discovered to your painful embarrassment that you actually didn't have a damn thing to complain about. O but ..troll. Yeah, continue. Or you can finally take the road that you're not travelling, do the homework and give a positive contribution instead...Too much to ask?<br /> <br /> Moving along;<br /> <br /> Regional PSP <b><u>Diyi</u></b>; <i>The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apache#Religion\" target=\"_blank\">term</a> diy\u00ed\u2019 refers to one or all of a set of abstract and invisible forces which are said to derive from certain classes of animals, plants, minerals, meteorological phenomena, and mythological figures within the Western Apache universe. Any of the various powers may be acquired by man and, if properly handled, used for a variety of purposes.</i><br /> <br /> Hmm...how many potential PSPs does that make so far...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T13:17:11-07:00","id":188200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187881#post187881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the equivalent about bitching about a movie you've never seen. Maybe you should have taken the time to review the links I've posted. You might have discovered to your painful embarrassment that you actually didn't have a damn thing to complain about. O but ..troll. Yeah, continue. Or you can finally take the road that you're not travelling, do the homework and give a positive contribution instead...Too much to ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I work over 60 hours a week and I'm a single parent. I am not proud to admit that I count upon the generosity of others when it comes to my hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T20:58:35-07:00","id":188468,"title":"","content":"How is Twitch bitching about a movie he's never seen? He's saying &quot;Hey, I don't know enough about an admittedly obscure area of mythology that doesn't get much attention in pop culture, but I'd like to learn more.&quot; That's about as positive a place to come from as any.<br /> <br /> Does one have to be an expert on Native American mythology to say that it's unfair to treat them badly, or to want a higher level of inclusion and equal treatment from the pop culture you do consume? No. That's dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:11:52-07:00","id":188475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187881#post187881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the equivalent about bitching about a movie you've never seen. Maybe you should have taken the time to review the links I've posted. You might have discovered to your painful embarrassment that you actually didn't have a damn thing to complain about. O but ..troll. Yeah, continue. Or you can finally take the road that you're not travelling, do the homework and give a positive contribution instead...Too much to ask?<br /> <br /> Moving along;<br /> <br /> Regional PSP <b><u>Diyi</u></b>; <i>The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apache#Religion\" target=\"_blank\">term</a> diy\u00ed\u2019 refers to one or all of a set of abstract and invisible forces which are said to derive from certain classes of animals, plants, minerals, meteorological phenomena, and mythological figures within the Western Apache universe. Any of the various powers may be acquired by man and, if properly handled, used for a variety of purposes.</i><br /> <br /> Hmm...how many potential PSPs does that make so far...?</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys do realize that what you seem to want to do has already been done. Twice, actually. Once by the French and another fan version. Why don't you just use those? They seem to meet each and every requirement you've set up. Perhaps a little too wordy with too many details and too many gods. Too many mythic figures that don't rate in the current edition of the zeitgeist. <br /> <br /> Seems like a huge tempest in a tea cup, when there are two full tea pots right over there. (Points)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:14:48-07:00","id":188478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187768#post187768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> We would love to work on a Pantheon for one of the Native North American groups. The Huron, the Iroquois, or the Cree are my personal favorites and, when we eventually recover from this all hands on deck focus on recovering from the situation at hand, I would like to spend my time starting to work on one of those three. Assuming, of course, the Iroquois have a consistent culture and religion, since they are a group of different tribes in a confederacy, if I am remembering my early Canadian history correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were all from one cultural source originally, but, as things got weird in North America, new tribes joined up that weren't originally from the same neighborhood.<br /> <br /> More of an early US History thing than Canadian. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T00:06:24-07:00","id":188555,"title":"","content":"OT<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwtichTheRat;N187690</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I was definitely upset with him a month or two ago, but now I am pretty mellow about it. I figured out his name from the old forums, and he got into an enormous amount of fights with other posters. So this is more of an objective judgement. I suppose talking about it is not very constructive though, so I won't bring it up in this thread again for the sake of not derailing it further than I already have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand being mellow. I'm still pretty mellow about a lot of things from the old forum, seeing how... well... ingrained it was. I can still remember a few old goodies, but oh well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=187690#post187690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if I should be the one to create the new thread. I don't know anything about Native Americans. Maybe someone more informed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I dont see the problem with you creating such a thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You could always ask for someone more informed in the first post of the thread to help you ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You guys do realize that what you seem to want to do has already been done. Twice, actually. Once by the French and another fan version. Why don't you just use those? They seem to meet each and every requirement you've set up. Perhaps a little too wordy with too many details and too many gods. Too many mythic figures that don't rate in the current edition of the zeitgeist.<br /> <br /> Seems like a huge tempest in a tea cup, when there are two full tea pots right over there. (Points) </div> </div> </div>Well for one, maybe they didn't like the way those previous attempts turned out? Maybe they want something else out of such a pantheon than the creators of the previous pantheons wanted?<br /> <br /> The problem with having less known gods in a game might become the fact that no one uses them. Just because I know who the Egyptian deity Bast is doesn't mean my players know who said deity is. this is especially strong when dealing with less known pantheons. Take my group as an example. If I pulled out an inuit god, no one would ever use it because a lot of my players doesn't even know who the Inuit's are.<br /> <br /> If, however, I say &quot;I made a native indian Pantheon with a great spirit pantheon head&quot;, they might find it interesting because they recognize that and can put it into their own context and as far as I know, my entire group has watched enough old cowboy movies to recongize the great spirit or heck, even coyote. Wendigo however, is to obscure for most people I know.<br /> <br /> So can we please put this argument to a rest now? Let's agree we disagree. It's not much more difficult than that.<br /> /OT<br /> <br /> Hmm, once we move into names and such my knowledge thins quickly. I guess I can still try to come up with rules and such if you'd like. I'm pretty good at figuring out boons. Balancing them on hte other hand... heh...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm...how many potential PSPs does that make so far...? </div> </div> </div>Possible, one could make a rather unqiue PSP... instead of making a single psp for every region, one could make a single PSP and then replace powers in it based upon the region.<br /> <br /> Or one could posible design them like this:<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Burden of...<br /> Dice Pool: Appearance + Command<br /> Cost: 2 Legend + 1 Willpower<br /> Action: Misc<br /> <br /> When this boon is first bought, chose a climate to associate with this boon. Pick two defining features with this climate from the list below. These are the effects that applies to everyone in the scene, except the user of this boon.<br /> <br /> Cold: -1 Dexterity penalty<br /> Hot: -2 penalty to all rolls<br /> Swampy: Everyone moves at half speed unless they can move above the swampy ground<br /> Windy: Range attacks suffers a -4 penalty<br /> Rainy: Perception rolls are at a -4 penalty<br /> Harsh: All skills lose a dot for the duration of the scene.<br /> Dry: 1 Bashing level inflicted after every action<br /> <br /> This makes for a fairly interesting boon. It makes it possible to play someone from the far north (Cold, Harsh) who has the same boon as someone from the deep desert (Hot, Dry).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:13:48-07:00","id":188768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=188555#post188555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well for one, maybe they didn't like the way those previous attempts turned out? Maybe they want something else out of such a pantheon than the creators of the previous pantheons wanted?<br /> <br /> The problem with having less known gods in a game might become the fact that no one uses them. Just because I know who the Egyptian deity Bast is doesn't mean my players know who said deity is. this is especially strong when dealing with less known pantheons. Take my group as an example. If I pulled out an inuit god, no one would ever use it because a lot of my players doesn't even know who the Inuit's are.<br /> <br /> If, however, I say &quot;I made a native indian Pantheon with a great spirit pantheon head&quot;, they might find it interesting because they recognize that and can put it into their own context and as far as I know, my entire group has watched enough old cowboy movies to recongize the great spirit or heck, even coyote. Wendigo however, is to obscure for most people I know.<br /> <br /> So can we please put this argument to a rest now? Let's agree we disagree. It's not much more difficult than that.<br /> /OT<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously. Everything you guys are trying to do is exactly what has already been done. You're breaking down the areas the same. You're using the same names for PSP and having the same potential regional PSP's. If you don't like the way the previous attempts turned out, it makes no sense to walk down exactly the same path...<br /> <br /> If you guys are going to end up with the same result barring some cosmetic differences, why reinvent the wheel? The Manittowok and Manitou are already out there. I believe they even have links in the link thread. <br /> <br /> Even if this is purely an aesthetic exercise for the participants, as some have stated they don't play Scion they merely like mucking around in the sandbox, there are a TON of areas and pantheons that don't even have this kind of love. <br /> <br /> Based on Jackalope's original intent, this result could have been handled with those links.... In fact, insofar as getting a publishable product, the Manittowok actually WERE published in French.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:09:53-07:00","id":189573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=188768#post188768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously. Everything you guys are trying to do is exactly what has already been done. You're breaking down the areas the same. You're using the same names for PSP and having the same potential regional PSP's. If you don't like the way the previous attempts turned out, it makes no sense to walk down exactly the same path...<br /> <br /> If you guys are going to end up with the same result barring some cosmetic differences, why reinvent the wheel? The Manittowok and Manitou are already out there. I believe they even have links in the link thread.Even if this is purely an aesthetic exercise for the participants, as some have stated they don't play Scion they merely like mucking around in the sandbox, there are a TON of areas and pantheons that don't even have this kind of love.<br /> <br /> Based on Jackalope's original intent, this result could have been handled with those links.... In fact, insofar as getting a publishable product, the Manittowok actually WERE published in French.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they wanna go down that path, I'm happy to help them regardless of someone else having gone down the path before. If my suggestion makes someone happy, I'm glad to give them ^^.I'm trying to keep this thread constructive after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T17:35:19-07:00","id":189723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=189573#post189573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they wanna go down that path, I'm happy to help them regardless of someone else having gone down the path before. If my suggestion makes someone happy, I'm glad to give them ^^.I'm trying to keep this thread constructive after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>One way to be constructive is to not do more work then you need to. Just speaking as someone who has done game design. If there is something out there that can give you bedrock, you use it. It's definitely worth DISCUSSING what may be in place to figure out what you want to use, what you want to discard, what you want to modify. Why bother to waste the time to write up Di ya id there's is cool? Or at least a good jumping off point. If everyone involved think that the extant Kokopeli nails it, why spin wheels and recreate it?<br /> <br /> I'd be interested to hear what Jackalope has to say after he takes a look at them. Was that what he was talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T23:58:00-07:00","id":209878,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the wait. I had a lot of stuff on my mind.<br /> <br /> I made the initial roster of deities for this based on what was COMMON about the Native American mythologies for the average American. For the casual gamer, they are known as the Great Spirit, Coyote, Raven, Eagle, etc, not because of some some racist's agenda, but because 90% of all people knew them by those names. When they read the mythology, those are the names that are presented to the general public, it's &quot;bedrock&quot; as Ajax put it.<br /> <br /> Then, the next day, I've been swarmed by mythology buffs, (or as Homer Simpson would call them, &quot;NEEEEERRRRRDDDD!&quot;), as they stated of how I was wrong and it was based on regional preference. And when I tried to explain of why I had it that way, I've been called &quot;racist' for not doing things their way. To tell you the truth, I didn't realize that there so many different names for the characters, depending on which tribe was represented. It seemed overwhelming to me at first, and then I remember that the term &quot;a.k.a.&quot; was used for this exact purpose, because of the regional dialect of the area in question. When that was brought out, then they called White Wolf and Onyx Path &quot;racist&quot; for putting it in their game mechanincs. This, I felt, was uncalled for, and after a few heated words, I stopped posting for a bit.<br /> <br /> After thinking on it, I was willing to go halfway and promote Kokopeli and the Hopi tribe's version because, again, the majority knew him and the Hopi.<br /> <br /> Now after all the backlash, I have evidence that I was right at the start. A few weeks ago, I saw the Disney movie &quot;Planes: Fire and Rescue&quot; with my brother. In it, there was a log carrier that was categorized as Native American descent. During a scene where Dusty and the other fire-fighters were schmoozing with a RV couple, the guy told a story of a certain animal spirit. I was half expecting them to use the name for the tribe of the Redwood area. Instead, the log carrier called the animal spirit &quot;Coyote&quot;. There was no call against the Disney company of slander of a tribe's belief system. To Disney, and to the viewers of the movie, the spirit is called Coyote, and will always be called Coyote to them.<br /> <br /> If Onyx Path decides on the route that I initially specified, then interest from casual gamers will rise. If they want to know more, then we as responsible players, can guide them to the correct book and/or website containing the info they seek. That's how people should know about the mythology behind the hype, just like Mummy: The Resurrection got me interested to know more about the Egyptian pantheon, and how Hercules and Percy Jackson got me interested in the game of Scion, and mythology in general.<br /> <br /> To be bombarded with a negative response, not to mention esoteric knowledge that only a minority knows and/or cares about, the one who was attacked would think negatively about the person and would turn themselves off (and their friends) from the game because of said experience. And that's one of the worst kind of troll, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T08:58:22-07:00","id":210250,"title":"","content":"Disney is not a bastion of cultural sensitivity. This thread has been full of people saying that modern pop culture is <i>not a good source</i> for information about Native Americans or other marginalized cultures. Because they're marginalized. Because there's centuries of Eurocentrism and racism saying that they don't matter, they're all the same. <br /> <br /> If you want to spark interest and introduce people to North American mythology, or Australian mythology, or African mythology, you should do that by presenting something based on reality, not based on the rest of the terrible representations that exist in pop culture. It takes some work. It takes some research, but you can present North American mythology in an accurate, respectful way. Learning about the Cherokee as separate from the Lakota is not <i>worse</i> than learning about &quot;Native Americans&quot; as one lump group of exotic foreigners. It's many, many times better. <br /> <br /> Yes, pop culture can be used to introduce people to subjects. This thread's full of people saying that. The trick is to use pop culture responsibly, to create material that doesn't perpetuate stereotypes and racism. Don't hand someone a book full of stuff ripped straight from the pages of Saturday morning cartoons from the 90s. Hand them something actually based on reality and let that whet their interest. Let them see how things really <i>work</i> and they'll explore on their own, from a better starting point. <br /> <br /> Are you saying that a well-written, well-researched Cherokee Pantheon would be <i>less</i> helpful, <i>less</i> useful, <i>less</i> interesting and <i>less</i> inspiring than some mishmash of popculture ideas tossed together from all over North America? Is it somehow insulting, trollish and mean to give readers and players a more truthful look at mythology, without all the bullcrap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:10:40-07:00","id":210355,"title":"","content":"This thread has posts that show pop culture keeping mythology alive. As well as the &quot;amazing&quot; posts that show nothing but squelch curiosity and kills interest. WTG with those!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:30:19-07:00","id":210387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=209878#post209878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To tell you the truth, I didn't realize that there so many different names for the characters, depending on which tribe was represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the point we NEEEEERRRRRDDDDs have been trying to make. They're <i><b>not</b></i> different names for the <i><b>same</b></i> characters. <i><b>They are different characters</b></i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:46:27-07:00","id":210402,"title":"","content":"Not according to some tribes. But as I've already posted links to such, you believe what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T11:11:17-07:00","id":210413,"title":"","content":"A Disney cartoon as evidence... <br /> <br /> Because they did so well treating the Native Americans well *cough*Peter Pan*cough*. Or respecting mythology *cough*Hercules*cough*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:27:09-07:00","id":210529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210402#post210402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not according to some tribes. But as I've already posted links to such, you believe what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you haven't. You've posted Wikipedia links to generic articles about different languages and cultures. A few about specific figures like Iktomi (who is <i>not</i> the same as Grandmother Spider from the Zuni, btw) and absolutely <i>nothing</i> that says there are Inuit people who will say that the figures of their mythology are the same figures as those in Cherokee mythology. Because that isn't true. Cherokee and Inuit mythology aren't the same. They're not even as closely related as Norse and Greek mythology. How or why would they be? They're thousands and thousands of miles apart, in entirely different climates and situations. Their cultures had no contact until colonization. <br /> <br /> <br /> Saying a Cherokee figure and an Inuit figure are the same figure is <b><u><i>exactly</i></u></b> like saying that a Norse figure and a pre-Islamic Arabian figure are the same. No seriously, it's like that. Have you compared the size of North America to Europe? North America is way, way bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T14:18:39-07:00","id":210566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=209878#post209878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made the initial roster of deities for this based on what was COMMON about the Native American mythologies for the average American. For the casual gamer, they are known as the Great Spirit, Coyote, Raven, Eagle, etc, not because of some some racist's agenda, but because 90% of all people knew them by those names. When they read the mythology, those are the names that are presented to the general public, it's &quot;bedrock&quot; as Ajax put it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general public cannot name all 50 capitals, or even find countries like Belgium, Georgia, or Sudan on a map. That does not mean they do not exist, and anyone who tried to claim otherwise is going to get laughed at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T16:12:48-07:00","id":210619,"title":"","content":"And this is perhaps the reason why there will never be a Native American pantheon in any game on mythology. There's a common source of info out there that people, who have heard about them, believe to be cultural, in the way that someone says, &quot;Hey, these things existed!&quot;. It's when we get into semantics is when things get complicated.<br /> <br /> I actually saw a &quot;History of English&quot; documentary on io9, and there was something that made me think about this entire thing. During Newton's time, everything that was scientific was talked about in Latin. The problem was that there were multiple ways to say a term, and that led to confusion and arguing. It was then that they realized that it would be easier to speak about these things in English, because it was a language that they ALL spoke. And so they did.<br /> <br /> Trying to force people to call Coyote and Raven by their regional name, to me, is like having a scientific conversation with a friend, and someone comes up and calls you mentally retarded for not discussing it ONLY in Latin. When I get into a semantic argument about a culture's mythology, I feel like I'm feeding the mythology trolls that wander around this forum. I don't want to do that, and now I'm convinced that there won't be any UNIFIED Native American pantheon in the Scion game world, (meaning that the America of Hero's Journey is probably more accurate as a portrayal of mythology than Scion will.) I would LOVE to hear Onyx Path's opinion about this, but since they are not responding, I will follow their lead and stop talking about this lost cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:36:57-07:00","id":210667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210619#post210619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to force people to call Coyote and Raven by their regional name</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, no. This is the problem. <b>Those Are <u><i>Not</i></u> Regional Variations On A Single Figure!!</b> They are <i>completely different figures</i> that European scholars smashed together because <i>racism is a real thing</i>. Re-read that bolded sentence again, that's what this entire thread boils down to. &quot;Coyote&quot; is a construction of <i>Europeans</i>. He <i>did not ever exist</i> before colonialism. He is <i>false</i>. <br /> <br /> If you want a <i>functional</i> analogy, what you're doing (and pop culture is doing, and a lot of bad scholars have been doing) is saying that Poker, Go Fish, Whist, Black Jack, and Hanafuda are the same thing. Yes, they are all <i>card games</i> but they are not the same card game. They are not even just variations on the same card game. If someone sat you down and told you they were going to teach you to play Card Game, you wouldn't know what they meant. You wouldn't learn any existing game. You'd learn some weird mishmash they'd made up in their head that combined ruled from every single existing card game in reality.<br /> <br /> Don't do that. Teach someone to play Poker and maybe they'll decide card games are awesome, and even want to try something out of the ordinary for them, like Hanafuda or Whist. <br /> <br /> Pretending that all card games are the same game with just slight variations is silly. No one would do that. It wouldn't make sense. Don't do that to religions or cultures either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm convinced that there won't be any UNIFIED Native American pantheon in the Scion game world</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there never will be. Because that very idea is as insane as a UNIFIED European Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:53:56-07:00","id":210670,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I checked the phone book. There are 12 people with the same first and last name as me.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">We are not all the same person.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T17:59:16-07:00","id":210677,"title":"","content":"Here's a stopgap if you want to run pantheons in a game: In Butterflies and Hurricanes, the game I run, the various First Nation pantheons have, themselves, formed a delegation that works as a diplomatic powerhouse on the global scale of politics. It's essentially like they're a divine Senate representing each of their cultures and beliefs.<br /> <br /> Instead of merging everything into a collective mash of nothing and stripping all the flavors of culture from each different pantheon, build one that's a Senate of sorts. You could pick and choose your gods from each pantheon and those picks can then spark storylines and drama because those gods are not all going to be in mind with eachother.<br /> <br /> There is a way, Jackalope, to do what you want without diminishing the cultures and people behind the various gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:17:50-07:00","id":210706,"title":"","content":"Same old...Everyone has their opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210529#post210529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you haven't. You've posted Wikipedia links to generic articles about different languages and cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah..as usual, you missed a few posts. But why waste time in arguing. After all I at least posted my sources, encouraged positive posts. Where as you posted...what exactly? I mean besides your usual negative shit. I could have a dozen elders from various tribes yelling at you, but you will never accept how wrong you are. So, just quit the pissing and moaning and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210677#post210677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a stopgap if you want to run pantheons in a game: In Butterflies and Hurricanes, the game I run, the various First Nation pantheons have, themselves, formed a delegation that works as a diplomatic powerhouse on the global scale of politics. It's essentially like they're a divine Senate representing each of their cultures and beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bad. Very diplomatic. I like it!<br /> <br /> A rather encouraging and positive post...wow.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:28:59-07:00","id":210718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210619#post210619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is perhaps the reason why there will never be a Native American pantheon in any game on mythology. There's a common source of info out there that people, who have heard about them, believe to be cultural, in the way that someone says, &quot;Hey, these things existed!&quot;. It's when we get into semantics is when things get complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>O I disagree in part. I think we'll see some things that certain others won't like at all. And it's all about interpretation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:34:39-07:00","id":210721,"title":"","content":"I will second the recommendation of a Senate or something similar. This allows you to have any major figures you desire from any of the many and varied pantheons of North America. It can function similar to the United Nations or other establishments. This way you preserve the vital culture of each region.<br /> <br /> Though it may be funny having Coyote, Coyote, Coyote and Coyote attending. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T19:39:51-07:00","id":210724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210721#post210721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will second the recommendation of a Senate or something similar. This allows you to have any major figures you desire from any of the many and varied pantheons of North America. It can function similar to the United Nations or other establishments. This way you preserve the vital culture of each region.<br /> <br /> Though it may be funny having Coyote, Coyote, Coyote and Coyote attending. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The various Coyotes have a competition to see which one of them will be THE Coyote to represent the various groups. This encourages storylines where the PCs are contacted to support various Pantheons to support THEIR Coyote's run for the position. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T20:38:58-07:00","id":210798,"title":"","content":"[OT]<br /> Okay, this has... turned into something completly different from the actual original post...<br /> <br /> I've rewritten this post a few times to avoid anything that would come off as flaming or non-constructive. It makes me sad to see this trail derailed to this point, despite attempts to set it back on track... Setting up a new thread simply runs the risk of being derailed and run into the bog by the same argument.<br /> <br /> The reason people generalize is to make things simpler. Pop-culture usually does this to avoid having to give out tons of backstory or to clarify and thus save screen time. Maybe only a few knows who [x] is, but possible quite a few knows him if we call him &quot;Coyote&quot;. This in itself isn't bad... If someone find such a myth/story interesting enough, they might look up the truth behind the myth and thus learn something.<br /> <br /> Can't we just agree to let this thread return to the original intent of creating a generalized native american pantheon?<br /> <br /> [/OT]<br /> <br /> The idea of a collction of gods forming a ruling council is a really good one. It makes it possible to update the pantheon as it goes and it also makes for a whole lot of divine politics. It would work in the setting as described by Scion as well... It could actually be a good idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:34:40-07:00","id":211322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210387#post210387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of the point we NEEEEERRRRRDDDDs have been trying to make. They're <i><b>not</b></i> different names for the <i><b>same</b></i> characters. <i><b>They are different characters</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Exactly. 100%<br /> <br /> All those a.k.a's? Those are the same divinity.... the Greeks, Romans considered Jupiter and Zeus to be the same guy, adding in some common epithets and the Mycenaen version of the name... STILL the same guy. <br /> <br /> Your fake &quot;Coyote&quot;? That's the Lakota &quot;Coyote&quot; - Mika, the Aztec &quot;Coyote&quot; - Huehuecoyotl, the Hopi &quot;Coyote&quot; - Istaqa, the Navajo &quot;Coyote - Attse0Haske, the Crow &quot;Coyote&quot; - Abka-Atadia, etc., etc. ETC. all mashed together and they are NOT the same guy (or, in some cases, gal). At all. Your Coyote is a trickster? Some of those gods aren't. At all. They are creator gods, people-eating demon gods, etc. <br /> <br /> There is pandering and there is pandering. Pandering to the lowest common denominator is actually fine. Sad. But fine.<br /> <br /> Pandering to culturally damaging stereotypes is completely different. Witness the difference between the way people are treating the debate over the use of the name &quot;Redskins&quot; for a football team. Witness the fact that, even though Native Americans have a legitimate case for objecting to other Native American themed team names (Chiefs, Braves, Seminoles, Etc.), there is not nearly as much support for it? I'm not saying what you are doing is tantamount to using the term &quot;Redskin&quot; to refer to a football team (Which IS as bad as people are saying it is. It's not being over-sensitive. If I suggested using the equivalent terms for gay people, Black people, Jewish people, etc. as team names, I would, quite rightly, be banned from this board.) but it definitely falls into a lesser degree of the same phenomenon. <br /> <br /> Why do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:53:07-07:00","id":211375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210798#post210798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[OT]Okay, this has... turned into something completly different from the actual original post...<br /> <br /> I've rewritten this post a few times to avoid anything that would come off as flaming or non-constructive. It makes me sad to see this trail derailed to this point, despite attempts to set it back on track... Setting up a new thread simply runs the risk of being derailed and run into the bog by the same argument.<br /> <br /> The reason people generalize is to make things simpler. Pop-culture usually does this to avoid having to give out tons of backstory or to clarify and thus save screen time. Maybe only a few knows who [x] is, but possible quite a few knows him if we call him &quot;Coyote&quot;. This in itself isn't bad... If someone find such a myth/story interesting enough, they might look up the truth behind the myth and thus learn something.<br /> <br /> Can't we just agree to let this thread return to the original intent of creating a generalized native american pantheon?[/OT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Because we have a few people preferring to add their socio-political crap in the game instead of making a new thread. (Probably because such a thread wouldn't receive the same traffic as one that pertains to the game itself.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210798#post210798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a collction of gods forming a ruling council is a really good one. It makes it possible to update the pantheon as it goes and it also makes for a whole lot of divine politics. It would work in the setting as described by Scion as well... It could actually be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me that we've enough material in this thread to do just that here and now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T10:01:59-07:00","id":211384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=210706#post210706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same old...Everyone has their opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah..as usual, you missed a few posts. But why waste time in arguing. After all I at least posted my sources, encouraged positive posts. Where as you posted...what exactly? I mean besides your usual negative shit. I could have a dozen elders from various tribes yelling at you, but you will never accept how wrong you are. So, just quit the pissing and moaning and move on.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Get those elders to join the board and please have them set us straight. Until then, I will hold out some of the people who deal and have dealt with these issues on an actual academic or professional level. Some of which have dipped in and out of this discussion. Myself included. <br /> <br /> No elders of any tribe I ever worked with has ever, ever, ever been unhappy to have their culture honored as distinct, unique and worthy of respect. And that's a lot of tribes. As a State Archaeologist and NAGPRA Coordinator in a state at the confluence of the two major systems in North America which also was unfortunately on the path of the Trail of Tears and the Trail of Death, that's dozens. In the tribal legal office of yet another tribe with close allegiances the tribes of yet another region as well as being the person responsible writing the tribal Cultural Resource law and reaching out to tribes across the US and Canada to write the best possible law for my employers, that's dozens more. And, finally, having been honored by being ceremonially adopted into the into the tribe of my cousin who suffered from FAS to be part of his support network, I have some experience with another tribe. <br /> <br /> People are &quot;pissing and moaning&quot; for very valid reasons. They are concerned about developing something ugly that the OP was floating to be added as canon to the game. No one has questioned whether you can do this in your own game,, either by spackling over massive cultural differences or the more &quot;elevated&quot; way that Aynie was suggesting.<br /> <br /> They are not &quot;squelching creativity&quot;, since I have seen and floated several different ideas, such as trying to put together a work group to hammer out a few regional pantheons. That would hit the OP's idea of trying to pander to people's preconceptions. People are aware of the Cherokee, the Sioux/Lakota, the &quot;Eskimos&quot;(shudder)/&quot;Inuit&quot;, the Navajo/Dine, the Hopi, the Northwestern Coastal tribes/Haida, the Iroquois Confederacy, etc. So why not hit those tribes. THAT'S exactly what the Scion developers did when they created the game. They pandered to the generalized knowledge of the NA European-descended zeitgeist. A &quot;North of Mexico&quot; North American set of pantheons can do the same for a specific area. <br /> <br /> People are questioning your references for the same reasons they would get hammered in any class I've ever taught, they are from a sources that are questionable at best and are being held out as authoritative. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T19:14:55-07:00","id":211936,"title":"","content":"[OT]<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are &quot;pissing and moaning&quot; for very valid reasons. They are concerned about developing something ugly that the OP was floating to be added as canon to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it might be ugly to you, but not to me. I dont have a problem with such a pantheon in the game, much like I have no problem with Disney's Hercules nor portrayal of most mythology in pop-culture. It has been said (several times) that a lot of people (on the forum) dislike this idea and that some like this idea. Beating a dead horse won't make the dead horse come back to life after all.<br /> <br /> For the record, if they so choose to portray the European pantheons as a generalized pantheon for Scion 2, I wouldn't have a problem with that either. If you do have a problem with it, create a thread and gather support for your opinion and see if the writers of Scion 2 picks it up ^^ For all the work we do, OPP might uterly disagree with us, but creating a suggestion is a first step <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not &quot;squelching creativity&quot;, since I have seen and floated several different ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, seeing how the thread has basically been turned into yet another &quot;SP&quot; (Socio-Policial) discussion I'd argue that the creativity has been severely hampered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=211375#post211375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because we have a few people preferring to add their socio-political crap in the game instead of making a new thread. (Probably because such a thread wouldn't receive the same traffic as one that pertains to the game itself.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one can do nothing else than to voice one's opinion and hope it might influence people <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's really awesome that people want to make more pantheons, knacks and such for Scion.<br /> <br /> One has to respect anyone's right to say &quot;I believe this is a bad idea&quot;, but this has... gone on to derail and basically make the thread defunct.<br /> <br /> [/OT]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowflame</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to me that we've enough material in this thread to do just that here and now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's some things to work with... A senate is a wonderful idea and I can easily see such a collective being opposed to the Allied pantheon. It would actually be fairly awesome to write something about them allying with the axis-pantheons during WW2... it could work as an alternative explaination to why the pantheon didn't join the fight until later. They were busy trying to deal with a native american collective. A peace treaty could later lead to the american pantheon getting support from the native collective as they took the war to Europe and Japan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","user":"Gemstone","date":".  fixed a few things 07-28-2014, 10:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:41:43-07:00","id":212005,"title":"","content":"I do want to comment here for a sec. The &quot;Senate&quot; of the Native North American Gods is not a Pantheon in Butterflies and Hurricanes. It is an organisation of Pantheons. They don't have a single PsP, they are not a single Pantheon. All they are is a way in which the hundreds of Pantheons can be interacted with. There are similar organisations for the Pantheons of North Africa and the Middle East, and an additional one of the lands the Theoi have conquered recently.<br /> <br /> So, it's not a single Pantheon by any stretch. Just as the Grecian Confederacy is not a single Pantheon (Greeks, Irish [Long story], Not-Slaughtered Gauls (Very few), Romans, Etruscans [Present in theory], Iberians [Again, in theory], and many others). Not all Native North American Pantheons are involved in the &quot;Senate&quot;, for example, the Inuit have refused to cooperate with anyone, and the various Cree Gods are keeping an eye on the Eastern Northern border for the Greeks (Native &quot;Senate&quot; is in bed with the Greeks as a series of Client Kingdoms due to truly colossal social rolls).<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion. But, just wanted to clarify it. It is a Pan-Pantheon Senate, while the Greeks have a Trans-Pantheon Kingdom, and the North Africans + Middle East has an alliance. They are are individual Pantheons, distinct, and possessing their own PsPs. There are multiple &quot;Coyote's&quot; (Who are not all named Coyote) just as there are many &quot;Lughs&quot; (Not all named Lugh), and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-28-2014, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:57:43-07:00","id":212023,"title":"","content":"Well, if this will happen, I think that a sidebar should be included to clarify, because there are tons of people who adhere to the notion of &quot;Coyote&quot; and &quot;Raven&quot;, and they will, at best, be very confused about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T21:14:42-07:00","id":212032,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, explaining things for people is always a good idea. It would be really stupid to expect everyone coming to Scion to walk in with a B.A. in Anthropology or History, so explaining away common misconceptions about various Pantheons would likely be a wonderful idea to open it up to everyone. To say the least, there are a lot. Some from dissonance between ancient and modern mindsets, and other misconceptions that have arisen over the ages. A bar explaining how &quot;Coyote&quot; isn't really a thing, a bar to explain that Hephaestus is mercilessly mocked by the Theoi for his disfigurement and it is entirely acceptable to do so in their culture, how The Dagda isn't a big dumb brute, how Cuchulain was probably boinking his foster-brother, ect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:32:15-07:00","id":212540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=212005#post212005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do want to comment here for a sec. The &quot;Senate&quot; of the Native North American Gods is not a Pantheon in Butterflies and Hurricanes. It is an organisation of Pantheons. They don't have a single PsP, they are not a single Pantheon. All they are is a way in which the hundreds of Pantheons can be interacted with. There are similar organisations for the Pantheons of North Africa and the Middle East, and an additional one of the lands the Theoi have conquered recently.<br /> <br /> So, it's not a single Pantheon by any stretch. Just as the Grecian Confederacy is not a single Pantheon (Greeks, Irish [Long story], Not-Slaughtered Gauls (Very few), Romans, Etruscans [Present in theory], Iberians [Again, in theory], and many others). Not all Native North American Pantheons are involved in the &quot;Senate&quot;, for example, the Inuit have refused to cooperate with anyone, and the various Cree Gods are keeping an eye on the Eastern Northern border for the Greeks (Native &quot;Senate&quot; is in bed with the Greeks as a series of Client Kingdoms due to truly colossal social rolls).<br /> <br /> Sorry for the confusion. But, just wanted to clarify it. It is a Pan-Pantheon Senate, while the Greeks have a Trans-Pantheon Kingdom, and the North Africans + Middle East has an alliance. They are are individual Pantheons, distinct, and possessing their own PsPs. There are multiple &quot;Coyote's&quot; (Who are not all named Coyote) just as there are many &quot;Lughs&quot; (Not all named Lugh), and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Lugh, Llew and Lug all sit down in a bar together and try to figure out if they're the same person? :-)<br /> <br /> And across the room, all the &quot;Coyotes&quot; are arguing about which one is who and how many of them there are, until they all realize they are actually Loki?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:53:04-07:00","id":212568,"title":"","content":"God, with the Lughs it's probably a whole lotta fighting between themselves. Fighting and yelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:59:55-07:00","id":212571,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/west-coast-coyote.htm\" target=\"_blank\">West Coast Coyote/Northwestern</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/southwest-coyote.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Southwest Coyote</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/plains-coyote.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Plains Coyote</a><br /> <br /> Hmmm...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.native-languages.org/great-spirit.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Great Spirit</a><br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Native American Names For The Great Spirit</b></u><br /> <br /> Above Old Man (Wiyot Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Apistotoke (Blackfoot Great Spirit)<br /> Caddi-Ayo (Caddo Great Spirit)<br /> Chebbeniathan (Arapaho Great Spirit)<br /> Gici Niwaskw (Abenaki Great Spirit)<br /> Gitchi Manitou (Ojibwe Great Spirit)<br /> Ha-Wen-Neyu (Huron Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Kisulkw (Micmac Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Ketanitowet (Lenape Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Maheo (Cheyenne Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Orenda (Iroquois Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Sky-Chief (Carib Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Spider of Heaven (Gros Ventre Great Spirit)<br /> Tirawa Atius (Pawnee Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Utakke (Carrier Great Spirit)<br /> Wakantanka (Sioux Indian Great Spirit)<br /> Wakonda (Omaha Indian Great Spirit)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T10:13:01-07:00","id":212591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=212568#post212568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, with the Lughs it's probably a whole lotta fighting between themselves. Fighting and yelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>And pointing out that each other is already dead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T15:36:51-07:00","id":212874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/152033-the-spirit-nation?p=212540#post212540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Lugh, Llew and Lug all sit down in a bar together and try to figure out if they're the same person? :-)<br /> <br /> And across the room, all the &quot;Coyotes&quot; are arguing about which one is who and how many of them there are, until they all realize they are actually Loki?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When the PCs had a giant meeting of the gods, Father Raven from the Inuit, one of the Coyotes from North America, and Loki all sat around and tried to A) Hit on the Morrigan and B) Show up the others for Ultimate Trickster status.<br /> <br /> It gave the PCs migraines. Having multiples of the gods that are vaguely linked to eachother but not ultimately the same at all only serves for greatness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T21:20:29-07:00","id":213138,"title":"","content":"Somehow, I think it would be funny if the modern interpretation of the Native American gods was just the newest pantheon to come into being in this scenario. Imagine if all the tribal pantheons took notice that the lowly animal spirits, from their legends, became gods in their own right, thanks to modern Americans. What if Whyoloo of the Salish met Fox of the new pantheon? What would happen? Would the original pantheons consider this new addition to be an abomination, or would they have some interest in them? Considering that American Gods, the book from which inspired the first edition of this game, had gods based on Media and Modern Life, having a co-existence of traditional pantheon and new pantheon wouldn't be too far off.<br /> <br /> And on another note, here's a strip telling how modern interpretations pollute original intent...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.escapistmagazine.com/articles/view/comicsandcosplay/comics/critical-miss/12024-Its-Not-Like-I-Reich-You-Or-Anything\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.escapistmagazine.com/arti...ou-Or-Anything</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T08:39:50-07:00","id":1495480,"title":"","content":"Did this homebrew ever get finished. I have a player who is interested in Navajo and there might be some things in this that could inspire us to come up with a story for him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27242-ravynwinter","name":"Ravynwinter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}